E["item:creeper-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Creeper Ichor",z="hillsbrad",s="Across the Hillsbrad forests, rare, virulent Creeper Ichor is harvested from moss creepers. The Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill seeks it as a biological agent for formulating novel plagues against the living.",h="Across the Hillsbrad forests, rare, virulent Creeper Ichor is harvested from moss creepers.",sec={{t="Apothecary Research in Hillsbrad",b="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon seeks natural toxins and biological catalysts to craft deadly new toxins and eradicate the surrounding human population. The clean air and vibrant life of the foothills offend him. Among the forest’s giant arachnids, mature moss creepers hold an elusive ichor that makes an ideal base for his Elixir of Suffering. Mixed with other reagents, including gray bear tongues, the fluid helps the Forsaken perfect their lethal alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield Creeper Ichor?",a="Moss creepers throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills yield the fluid. They include Giant Moss Creepers, Forest Moss Creepers, Elder Moss Creepers, and the notable arachnid Creepthess.",al={"where to get creeper ichor","what drops creeper ichor","creeper ichor mobs"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need this fluid?",a="Apothecary Lydon uses Creeper Ichor as a vital killing agent in his ongoing alchemical research. It helps him brew the Elixir of Suffering, designed to plague and exterminate the living humans in Hillsbrad.",al={"why lydon wants ichor","elixir of suffering purpose","what is creeper ichor used for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Creeper Ichor so difficult to find?",a="Moss creepers are common in the forests around Tarren Mill, but usable reservoirs of this virulent ichor are uncommon. Hunters may have to slay many arachnids before securing a usable specimen.",al={"why rare","creeper ichor drop rate"},gp=true},{q="What is Creeper Ichor?",a="Creeper Ichor is an exceptionally rare bodily fluid harvested from the moss creepers that haunt the Hillsbrad Foothills. These giant arachnids stalk the forests and fields around Tarren Mill, but only rarely does one yield ichor potent and pure enough to serve as a viable alchemical reagent. To the Royal Apothecary Society, this noxious essence represents a prime lethal agent, prized for its natural toxicity and volatile brewing potential.",al={"what is creeper ichor","creeper ichor lore","moss creeper ichor"},it="identity",add="f45507cb"},{q="Where does Creeper Ichor come from?",a="Creeper Ichor is not crafted by hands, but harvested directly from the various species of moss creepers native to the Hillsbrad Foothills, including giant, forest, and elder creepers, as well as notorious beasts like Creepthess. It is a natural biological fluid that forms within these giant predatory spiders, though finding a specimen that contains a usable, concentrated amount requires tracking down and slaying dozens of the creatures throughout the wilderness.",al={"where does creeper ichor come from","creeper ichor origin","who made creeper ichor"},it="origin",add="3620ba85"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken loyalist, securing lethal components like Creeper Ichor directly advances the Royal Apothecary Society’s campaign to scour the living from Lordaeron."},kw={"apothecary lydon","creeper ichor","creepthess","elixir of suffering","hillsbrad foothills","moss creeper","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:496","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","item:gray-bear-tongue","topic:human"},src={"Creeper Ichor","Elixir of Suffering (quest)"}}
E["item:elixir-of-pain"] = {t="item",n="Elixir of Pain",z="hillsbrad",s="Forsaken apothecaries at Tarren Mill brew the Elixir of Pain for dangerous experiments. The mixture tests biological agents meant to advance Lady Sylvanas's darker ambitions.",h="Forsaken apothecaries at Tarren Mill brew the Elixir of Pain for dangerous experiments.",sec={{t="Apothecary Experimentation",b="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks formulas to strengthen the Forsaken against their mortal neighbors and the Scourge. The Elixir of Pain is one such trial, made with freshly harvested ingredients from around the Hillsbrad Foothills. Its living subjects matter little to its makers; the potion tests volatile substances meant to aid the Dark Lady.",sp=0},{t="Field Testing on Stanley",b="The apothecaries seek a quiet test before risking military assets or exposing their work to Hillsbrad's defenders. They give the Elixir of Pain to Stanley, Farmer Ray's seemingly harmless domestic dog at the northern farmstead of Hillsbrad Fields. The brew does not kill him quietly. It mutates Stanley into an enraged, monstrous beast.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Pain?",a="The Elixir of Pain tests biological compounds for the Royal Apothecary Society. Its creators hope these mixtures will eventually yield devastating concoctions for Lady Sylvanas and secure Forsaken dominance.",al={"why make elixir of pain","elixir purpose","what does the elixir do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Stanley?",a="Stanley is Farmer Ray's pet dog at the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields. Forsaken apothecaries choose the seemingly harmless domestic dog as an unsuspecting subject for their new elixir.",al={"who is stanley","farmer ray dog","stanley dog"},it="target"},{q="Why is the elixir tested on Stanley?",a="Apothecary Lydon wants to test his newly mixed elixir in the field, so he sends it to Farmer Ray's little dog Stanley to see how the animal responds.",al={"what happens to stanley","does stanley die","stanley wolf transformation"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="Where is the elixir tested?",a="The test takes place outside Farmer Ray's northern farmhouse in Hillsbrad Fields, southwest of Tarren Mill. Stanley usually rests near the front porch.",al={"where do i take the elixir","stanley location","farmer ray farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Elixir of Pain?",a="The Elixir of Pain is an experimental alchemical concoction brewed for the Forsaken war effort in Hillsbrad Foothills. Brewed using freshly harvested blood combined with volatile reagents, it serves as an early prototype for the dark plagues and toxins the Royal Apothecary Society seeks to engineer for Lady Sylvanas.",al={"what is elixir of pain","elixir of pain item","pain potion"},it="identity",add="5a45fd3d"},{q="Where does the Elixir of Pain come from, and who made it?",a="The elixir is brewed at the Forsaken outpost of Tarren Mill. An apothecary mixes fresh creature blood gathered from the surrounding foothills with other caustic ingredients, intending to craft a virulent weapon to advance the Dark Lady's conquest of the region.",al={"who made elixir of pain","elixir of pain creator","where does elixir of pain come from"},it="origin",add="52862df0"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society's callous field trials show the Forsaken's willingness to use any means necessary to develop chemical weapons against the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Forsaken allies may witness the unsettling methods used by Tarren Mill's researchers during these grim tests."},kw={"apothecary","elixir of pain","farmer ray","hillsbrad fields","royal apothecary society","stanley","sylvanas","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:501","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Elixir of Pain","Elixir of Pain (2)"}}
E["item:elixir-of-suffering"] = {t="item",n="Elixir of Suffering",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon brews an experimental draught for the Royal Apothecary Society. Its work aims to create a virulent plague against living humans and the Scourge.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon brews an experimental draught for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sec={{t="Apothecary Experimentation",b="Apothecary Lydon gathers raw reagents from the wilderness around ruined Tarren Mill and combines them into toxic draughts. The work follows the Royal Apothecary Society's overarching mandate to formulate a new plague that will exterminate the living and the dead alike. To test the brew's potency, Lydon gives it to his assistant, a frog named Umpi.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Suffering?",a="Apothecary Lydon brews the elixir as an experiment for the Royal Apothecary Society. The Society intends its new plague to eradicate living humans and the Scourge.",al={"why make elixir of suffering","what does the elixir do","elixir of suffering purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a frog kept by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Though jokingly called his assistant, Umpi is an unwitting test subject for newly brewed alchemical toxins.",al={"who is the frog","who is the toad","lydon's assistant"},it="people"},{q="What happens when Umpi drinks the elixir?",a="When Umpi drinks the Elixir of Suffering, the frog croaks and almost instantly succumbs to the poison. The test shows how deadly Lydon's brew is.",al={"does umpi die","what happens to the toad"},sp=1},{q="What is the Elixir of Suffering?",a="The Elixir of Suffering is an experimental concoction brewed by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill. Designed as part of the Forsaken's ongoing pursuit of a new plague, this lethal mixture is crafted to inflict agonizing pain and death upon both the living and the undead.",al={"what is elixir of suffering","elixir of suffering lore","what does elixir of suffering do"},it="identity",add="14f85f3d"},{q="Where does the Elixir of Suffering come from, and who made it?",a="The elixir is brewed by Apothecary Lydon, stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Working on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, Lydon gathers local components across the foothills to formulate and refine the deadly potion.",al={"who made elixir of suffering","creator of elixir of suffering","where did elixir of suffering come from"},it="origin",add="fa4e475a"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want to create the Elixir of Suffering?",a="Apothecary Lydon concocts the elixir to fulfill the Dark Lady's grand design: crafting a weapon potent enough to eradicate both the Scourge and humanity. He tests its lethality on local subjects to ensure the brew inflicts maximum torment and swift demise.",al={"why make elixir of suffering","purpose of elixir of suffering","why does lydon want the elixir"},it="why_wanted",add="1d085d8d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Across Lordaeron, the Royal Apothecary Society works to create a weapon that will secure the Forsaken's independence from the Scourge and living humanity. Lydon's experiments in Tarren Mill are one step in that work."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of suffering","forsaken plague","hillsbrad foothills","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","npc:umpi","quest:496","zone:hillsbrad","topic:scourge","topic:human"},src={"Elixir of Suffering","Elixir of Suffering (2)"}}
E["item:farren-s-report"] = {t="item",n="Farren's Report",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Farren's Report carries Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's findings on the local naga. He hopes the dispatch will win him a return to Stormwind.",h="In Southshore, Farren's Report carries Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's findings on the local naga.",sec={{t="A Ticket Out of Southshore",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle grew tired of Southshore's embattled coast, its local leadership, and its remote frontier. He had adventurers hunt the Daggerspine naga to gather proof of their threat, then gathered the findings into a formal report. Farren plans to send it to Major Samuelson, captain of the guard in Stormwind Keep, rather than to his commanding officer, Marshal Redpath. Samuelson trained Farren, and Farren hopes the report will show his competence and earn him an immediate transfer back to Stormwind City's comforts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Farren's Report?",a="Farren's Report is a military dispatch by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle, summarizing his operations against the Daggerspine naga encroaching on Southshore's beaches.",al={"farrens report","what is this report","orinelle report"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Farren want this delivered to Stormwind?",a="Farren hopes to leave Southshore and return to Stormwind City. He sends the report to Major Samuelson, his former mentor and captain of the Stormwind guard, hoping for a favorable transfer.",al={"why send report to stormwind","farrens goal","why samuelson"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Farren keeping the report a secret from Redpath?",a="Farren wants to avoid scrutiny from Marshal Redpath and local leadership. They might take offense at an officer using a local threat to arrange a personal transfer back to safety in the capital.",al={"why hide from redpath","ol redpath secret"},it="motive"},{q="How does Major Samuelson react upon receiving it?",a="Major Samuelson praises his former student for taking initiative against the Southshore naga. He promises to consider the report when reviewing guard assignments in the coming month.",al={"samuelson reaction","turn in reassignment"},sp=1},{q="Where does Farren's Report come from, and who made it?",a="The document was drafted in Southshore by Lieutenant Farren Orinelle himself. Stationed out in the dangerous frontier of Hillsbrad Foothills, Farren compiled the report detailing his efforts against the regional murlocs and naga to catch the eye of high command in the capital.",al={"who wrote farren's report","farrens report origin","who made farrens report"},it="origin",add="97a8ff6b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Farren's Report reveals the maneuvering within its military, as officers in distant Hillsbrad seek safer duty in Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the Alliance, carrying Farren's Report connects besieged Southshore with the royal court in Stormwind Keep."},kw={"farren orinelle","farren's report","major samuelson","naga","reassignment","redpath","southshore","stormwind keep"},rel={"quest:563","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","npc:major-samuelson","subzone:southshore","subzone:stormwind-keep","quest:562","quest:559","topic:naga"},src={"Farren's Report","Reassignment"}}
E["item:frostwolf-banner"] = {t="item",n="Frostwolf Banner",z="hillsbrad",s="In Alterac Valley, Horde initiates seek the Frostwolf Banner in Wildpaw Cavern. Recovering it is an ancestral rite of passage that awakens their battle spirit and earns their first clan insignia.",h="In Alterac Valley, Horde initiates seek the Frostwolf Banner in Wildpaw Cavern.",sec={{t="A Rite of Passage",b="Horde warriors seeking a place among the Frostwolf clan face a trial of grit in Alterac Valley. Warmaster Laggrond sends new recruits south into Wildpaw Cavern, where territorial gnolls fill the damp, hostile corridors. Reaching the hidden banner and bringing it back unbroken proves their courage and shows their battle rage has awakened. The trial earns each warrior the Frostwolf initiate's insignia.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Frostwolf Banner inside a gnoll cave?",a="Warmaster Laggrond and the clan use the banner's place in Wildpaw Cavern as an initiation test. New fighters must enter gnoll territory, face danger, and shake off complacency to awaken their battle spirit.",al={"why is banner in wildpaw","gnolls have banner","frostwolf banner location"},it="place"},{q="Who do I return the Frostwolf Banner to?",a="Return the banner to Warmaster Laggrond in Alterac Valley. Presenting it to him welcomes an initiate into the Frostwolf ranks and earns an insignia of standing.",al={"who wants frostwolf banner","banner quest turn in","laggrond banner"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does the standard look unusual for a Frostwolf crest?",a="Warmaster Laggrond recognizes the banner as a clan trial standard, though its markings resemble older tribal insignias. Those include symbols associated with early orcish clans from the old Horde.",al={"twilight hammer symbol banner","banner looks wrong","frostwolf banner design"}},{q="What is the Frostwolf Banner?",a="The Frostwolf Banner is a tribal standard representing the Frostwolf clan in Alterac Valley. While its emblazoned sigil strangely resembles ancient clan iconography rather than their usual crest, it remains an honored symbol of the clan's presence and authority in the frozen valley.",al={"what is frostwolf banner","frostwolf banner lore","about frostwolf banner"},it="identity",add="cf6c63b1"},{q="Why does Warmaster Laggrond want the Frostwolf Banner recovered?",a="Warmaster Laggrond requires all newcomers seeking to fight alongside the Frostwolves in Alterac Valley to undergo a rite of battle. Retrieving the banner from the depths of the gnoll-infested Wildpaw Cavern proves your courage, awakening your warrior spirit and earning you an initiate's insignia among the clan.",al={"why recover frostwolf banner","why does laggrond want banner","frostwolf banner purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="518ec450"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the banner formally bloods a warrior into the Frostwolf clan under Warmaster Laggrond.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, returning a clan standard from savage gnolls honors the Frostwolf clan's legacy and Thrall's ancestral heritage in the Alterac mountains."},kw={"alterac valley","frostwolf banner","gnolls","insignia","proving grounds","warmaster laggrond","wildpaw cavern"},rel={"npc:warmaster-laggrond","topic:horde","topic:gnoll","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Frostwolf Banner","Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Horde)"}}
E["item:gray-bear-tongue"] = {t="item",n="Gray Bear Tongue",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad Foothills, gray bear tongues are raw reagents sought by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill for experimental toxins.",h="In Hillsbrad Foothills, gray bear tongues are raw reagents sought by the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren...",sec={{t="Apothecary Research in Hillsbrad",b="Gray bears roam the wilds around Tarren Mill in several sturdy varieties. Their tongues hold heavy muscular tissue and fluids that Apothecary Lydon uses as a base ingredient for lethal solutions, including the Elixir of Suffering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants gray bear tongues?",a="Apothecary Lydon, stationed at the Forsaken outpost of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, seeks gray bear tongues to brew experimental killing agents.",al={"who needs bear tongues","apothecary lydon tongues","bear tongue turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Apothecary using these tongues for?",a="Lydon uses gray bear tongues as one of the primary organic agents in the Elixir of Suffering, a lethal concoction designed to help plague Hillsbrad’s living human populations. Creeper ichor is another ingredient.",al={"why does lydon want tongues","bear tongue purpose","elixir of suffering ingredients"},it="purpose"},{q="Which creatures drop these tongues?",a="Gray bear tongues come from local gray bears roaming the Hillsbrad Foothills, including standard gray bears, elder gray bears, vicious gray bears, and Big Samras, a notorious beast.",al={"where do bear tongues drop","which bears have tongues","hillsbrad bears"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is Gray Bear Tongue?",a="It is exactly what it sounds like: a freshly carved tongue taken from one of the wild gray bears roaming the Hillsbrad Foothills. While unappealing to most travelers, alchemists and researchers among the Forsaken value animal tissues for their specific chemical properties when formulating new concoctions.",al={"what is gray bear tongue","gray bear tongue item","what are gray bear tongues"},it="identity",add="57051fe5"},{q="Where does a Gray Bear Tongue come from?",a="These tongues are harvested directly from the gray bears that prowl the forests and hills surrounding Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Hunters can claim them from common gray bears, elder specimens, vicious variants, or notable beasts like Big Samras.",al={"gray bear tongue source","where do gray bear tongues come from","who drops gray bear tongues"},it="origin",add="4de594f1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you help the Royal Apothecary Society craft new plagues against the living by procuring organic components from local wildlife."},kw={"apothecary lydon","big samras","elixir of suffering","gray bear tongue","hillsbrad foothills","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:496","item:creeper-ichor","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Gray Bear Tongue","Elixir of Suffering (quest)"}}
E["item:hillsbrad-human-skull"] = {t="item",n="Hillsbrad Human Skull",z="hillsbrad",s="Across the Hillsbrad Foothills, Forsaken gather the skulls of slain humans. At Tarren Mill, they keep them as grim mementos of the assault on local settlements.",h="Across the Hillsbrad Foothills, Forsaken gather the skulls of slain humans.",sec={{t="Trophies of a Bitter War",b="Forsaken forces from Tarren Mill fight the humans of Southshore and nearby settlements. During the Battle of Hillsbrad, Deathstalkers and soldiers carry out the purge Darthalia ordered. Guards left on watch want a share of the slaughter. Deathguard Samsa collects skulls from the fighters on the front lines, taking pleasure in keeping the remains of people the Forsaken once lived among. These trophies are proof of the killing as the conflict rages.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants these human skulls?",a="Deathguard Samsa, a Forsaken sentry at Tarren Mill, collects the skulls. Envious of soldiers sent to battle and pillage Hillsbrad while he remains on guard, he asks passing adventurers to bring him thirty for his private collection.",al={"who wants skulls","who takes human skulls","deathguard samsa skulls"}},{q="Where are Hillsbrad Human Skulls gathered?",a="Forsaken gather the skulls from human combatants and laborers across the Hillsbrad Foothills, especially near the human-held farms, mines, and town fortifications attacked during the Battle of Hillsbrad.",al={"where do skulls drop","farm human skulls","who drops human skulls"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken collect human remains?",a="Some Forsaken collect human remains out of hatred and dark humor. Soldiers like Samsa treat the skulls as prized curiosities and proof that Hillsbrad is nearing defeat.",al={"why do forsaken want skulls","forsaken skull collection"}},{q="What is a Hillsbrad Human Skull?",a="These are the gruesome trophies severed from the fallen human defenders and townsfolk scattered across the Hillsbrad Foothills. As conflict rages between the Forsaken of Tarren Mill and the living humans of Hillsbrad, such macabre tokens serve as tangible proof of Alliance casualties in the contested territory.",al={"what are hillsbrad human skulls","hillsbrad skull item","hillsbrad human skull info"},it="identity",add="0091f8c0"},{q="Where does a Hillsbrad Human Skull come from, and who made it?",a="These skulls are taken directly from the mortal humans inhabiting the Hillsbrad Foothills, harvested by Horde fighters engaged in the ongoing border war. Rather than being manufactured, they are morbid battlefield remnants claimed from the slain soldiers, farmers, and citizens defending the local human settlements against the Forsaken.",al={"hillsbrad human skull origin","where do hillsbrad skulls come from","who makes hillsbrad skulls"},it="origin",add="9eb161fa"},{q="Why does Deathguard Samsa want Hillsbrad Human Skulls?",a="Deathguard Samsa, stationed on guard duty at Tarren Mill, is intensely envious of the warriors sent out to pillage and fight the living. Stranded behind the front lines, he collects the skulls as precious personal souvenirs of death to share vicariously in the slaughter of Hillsbrad's human defenders.",al={"why does samsa want skulls","who wants hillsbrad human skulls and why","why collect hillsbrad human skulls"},it="why_wanted",add="a9ea879b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may see the skulls as vengeance and a grim reminder of the living kin who shun you.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see Hillsbrad's farmers and soldiers reduced to trinkets, a sign of the Forsaken campaign's cruelty in Lordaeron."},kw={"darthalia","hillsbrad","samsa","skull","southshore","tarren mill","trophy"},rel={"quest:546","npc:deathguard-samsa","quest:527","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:human","item:courser-eye"},src={"Hillsbrad Human Skull","Souvenirs of Death"}}
E["item:hillsbrad-town-registry"] = {t="item",n="Hillsbrad Town Registry",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad Fields, the town hall keeps a ledger of the settlement's surviving citizens and landowners. The Hillsbrad Town Registry records civic matters, and the Forsaken seek it during their offensive against the human stronghold.",h="In Hillsbrad Fields, the town hall keeps a ledger of the settlement's surviving citizens and landowners.",sec={{t="A Record of Defiance",b="The Hillsbrad Town Registry records the town's people and rights. It rests in the town hall near the podium of Magistrate Burnside. From Tarren Mill, the Forsaken press to break human resistance in the foothills. Darthalia sends Horde champions into the town hall to kill the council and seize the ledger. Its records cover Hillsbrad's population, households, and administrative rights. The registry would strip the town of its civic order and give the Undercity intelligence on the surviving population and their assets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hillsbrad Town Registry kept?",a="The registry is kept in a corner of the town hall at the Hillsbrad Fields, near the stairs leading to Magistrate Burnside's platform.",al={"registry location","where is town registry","find hillsbrad registry"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to steal it?",a="High Executor Darthalia wants to dismantle human governance in the foothills. The registry holds records of the town's citizens, households, administrative rights, and property, and would give the Forsaken intelligence on the surviving community.",al={"why steal registry","darthalia registry quest","purpose of registry"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who guards the registry?",a="Magistrate Burnside and the Hillsbrad Councilmen guard the registry. They wield defensive magic and rally inside and around the town hall.",al={"who protects registry","town hall defenders"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is the Hillsbrad Town Registry?",a="The Hillsbrad Town Registry is an official record book kept inside the town hall of the Hillsbrad Fields settlement. Maintained by the local human administration under Magistrate Burnside, it documents the civic affairs, population, and governance of one of the Alliance's surviving holdings in the foothills.",al={"what is hillsbrad town registry","hillsbrad registry","what is the registry book"},it="identity",add="188a667c"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, capturing the town registry helps break human authority in the foothills and secure the Forsaken stronghold at Tarren Mill.",["race:Human"]="As a human, the ledger records the formal existence and rights of Hillsbrad's remaining townsfolk. Its loss would strike the regional community hard."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad town hall","hillsbrad town registry","magistrate burnside"},rel={"quest:527","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:human","topic:mage"},src={"Hillsbrad Town Registry","Battle of Hillsbrad (4)"}}
E["item:humbert-s-sword"] = {t="item",n="Humbert's Sword",z="hillsbrad",s="At Dun Garok, Humbert's Sword lies among the dwarves who took it from his camp. Deathguard Humbert left his post to gather firewood while scouting the stronghold.",h="At Dun Garok, Humbert's Sword lies among the dwarves who took it from his camp.",sec={{t="A Scout's Careless Moment",b="Deathguard Humbert left his hidden post near Dun Garok one morning to gather firewood for boiling water. High Executor Darthalia had sent him to watch the dwarven presence there. While he was away, a dwarven patrol found his campsite and plundered his gear, including his personal blade. With so many dwarves to search, Humbert needs Horde agents to enter the fortress and recover it.",sp=0},{t="The Dwarven Trove",b="Dun Garok's defenders carried Humbert's belongings behind the stronghold's barricades. Riflemen, mountaineers, and priests pass supplies around the garrison. Finding the thief means searching among the defenders in the trenches and redoubts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns this sword?",a="The sword belongs to Deathguard Humbert, a Forsaken sentry stationed in Tarren Mill and assigned to scout Dun Garok.",al={"whose sword is this","humbert owner","who is humbert"},it="identity"},{q="How did the dwarves get Humbert's sword?",a="Humbert left his scout camp just outside Dun Garok one morning to gather firewood. While he was away, a dwarven patrol ransacked the camp and took his gear.",al={"how did dwarves get it","why do dwarves have sword","how was sword stolen"}},{q="Why is Humbert so desperate to get his sword back?",a="Humbert needs his weapon to keep watch on Dun Garok as High Executor Darthalia ordered. With so many dwarves in the garrison, he cannot find the thief alone.",al={"why humbert want sword","what happens if humbert loses sword","why does humbert care"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the sword be found?",a="The sword is with the dwarven forces at Dun Garok in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. It can be recovered from the mountaineers, riflemen, or priests stationed throughout the post.",al={"where does sword drop","sword location","how to find humbert's sword"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="High Executor Darthalia keeps strict discipline over the Forsaken forces in Hillsbrad. Negligent sentries like Humbert are desperate to hide their mistakes.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the sword fits the Horde's wider operations against Dun Garok's dwarven enclave, including collecting dwarven blood and military insignias."},kw={"darthalia","deathguard humbert","dun garok","hillsbrad","humbert's sword","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:547","npc:deathguard-humbert","subzone:dun-garok","subzone:tarren-mill","npc:high-executor-darthalia","quest:527","quest:509","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Humbert's Sword","Humbert's Sword (quest)"}}
E["item:keg-of-shindigger-stout"] = {t="item",n="Keg of Shindigger Stout",z="hillsbrad",s="In Dun Garok, Shindigger Stout fills the dwarves’ kegs and draws interest from Tarren Mill. The Royal Apothecary Society wants the ale for a purpose far darker than drink.",h="In Dun Garok, Shindigger Stout fills the dwarves’ kegs and draws interest from Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Favorite",b="Dwarves of Ironforge hold Dun Garok in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. Within its barracks and mess halls, defenders share Shindigger Stout through the cold and the siege against their regional enemies. The brew is a staple of the garrison’s daily life.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Lydon's Poison Vessel",b="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks an intact keg of Shindigger Stout for the Forsaken’s Elixir of Agony. He rejects testing the formula on beasts and plans to spike the ale for captured human farmers held in Tarren Mill.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Shindigger Stout used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill wants Shindigger Stout for the Elixir of Agony. He plans to lace the ale with the poison and test it on humanoid subjects.",al={"why get shindigger stout","shindigger stout purpose","what does lydon do with the keg"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can a Keg of Shindigger Stout be found?",a="Kegs of Shindigger Stout are kept in Dun Garok, in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. The dwarves store them in the fortress’s mess halls and lower barracks.",al={"keg location","where is shindigger stout","find the stout"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who brews Shindigger Stout?",a="The dwarves of Dun Garok brew and keep Shindigger Stout. They hold a fortified garrison in Hillsbrad Foothills for Ironforge.",al={"who makes shindigger stout","is it dwarven ale"},it="origin"},{q="Why doesn't Apothecary Lydon brew his own alcohol for the test?",a="Lydon asks for a keg kept at Dun Garok to use in his experiment. The account gives no reason beyond his need for the ale and says nothing about him brewing alcohol himself.",al={"why steal dwarven beer","why dun garok beer"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Keg of Shindigger Stout?",a="A Keg of Shindigger Stout is a barrel of potent dwarven ale kept by the Ironforge dwarves stationed in the fortress of Dun Garok. While intended to supply the dwarven soldiers during their deployment in the Hillsbrad Foothills, its strong brew makes it a prime vehicle for Apothecary Lydon's experiments on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"what is keg of shindigger stout","shindigger stout keg info","what is shindigger stout"},it="identity",add="b55cb0ca"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can use alcohol to mask the scent and taste of deadly concoctions made for Lady Sylvanas.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you can strike at Dun Garok, an Alliance military foothold in the southeastern hills of Hillsbrad Foothills."},kw={"apothecary lydon","dun garok","dwarven ale","elixir of agony","keg of shindigger stout","shindigger stout","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","subzone:dun-garok","subzone:tarren-mill","npc:umpi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:horde"},src={"Keg of Shindigger Stout","Elixir of Agony (4)"}}
E["item:mountain-lion-blood"] = {t="item",n="Mountain Lion Blood",z="hillsbrad",s="Across Hillsbrad and Alterac, Mountain Lion Blood draws Apothecary Lydon’s interest. In Tarren Mill, Lydon seeks fresh blood to make the Royal Apothecary Society’s dreaded Elixir of Pain.",h="Across Hillsbrad and Alterac, Mountain Lion Blood draws Apothecary Lydon’s interest.",sec={{t="Reagent of the Hills",b="Mountain lions prowl the highlands and foothills of Hillsbrad and Alterac. Hunters prize their pelts and claws, while the Forsaken of the Royal Apothecary Society seek the blood in their veins. Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill believes fresh mountain lion blood can form the base of a potent brew meant to bring misery to the living.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the New Plague",b="Apothecary Lydon’s experiments in Tarren Mill support the Royal Apothecary Society’s work to perfect the Forsaken’s New Plague. Lydon gathers blood from vigorous wild beasts to refine a concoction called the Elixir of Pain, testing how local organic compounds can be turned against the enemies of the Dark Lady.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mountain Lion Blood used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill needs ten vials of Mountain Lion Blood to make the Elixir of Pain. The Royal Apothecary Society studies new diseases.",al={"what is mountain lion blood for","who needs lion blood","elixir of pain blood"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Mountain Lion Blood be collected?",a="Mountain Lion Blood comes from lions hunting across the Hillsbrad Foothills and the snowy crags of the nearby Alterac Mountains.",al={"where to find mountain lion blood","mountain lion blood location","which lions drop blood"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon specifically want wild cat blood?",a="Lydon believes the vital fluids of hardy, aggressive mountain lions can form the basis of a toxic brew that brings great pain to Hillsbrad’s living inhabitants.",al={"why lion blood","why does lydon want lion blood"},it="motive"},{q="Is Mountain Lion Blood useful for alchemy crafting recipes?",a="No. Mountain Lion Blood is an experimental reagent for Apothecary Lydon’s work, not an ingredient in standard alchemy recipes.",al={"can alchemists use mountain lion blood","is lion blood for alchemy"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Mountain Lion Blood?",a="It is fresh blood harvested from the predatory mountain lions prowling the rugged slopes of the Hillsbrad Foothills and Alterac Mountains. Though useless to common alchemists or tradesfolk, it possesses biological qualities prized by the Royal Apothecary Society for their lethal alchemical experiments.",al={"what is mountain lion blood","mountain lion blood lore","what is this blood"},it="identity",add="dcf44a54"},{q="Where does Mountain Lion Blood come from, and who made it?",a="It is not crafted or manufactured, but drawn directly from the feral cats indigenous to northern Lordaeron. The mountain lions that roam the highlands between Hillsbrad and Alterac are hunted and bled by agents working on behalf of the Forsaken apothecaries stationed at Tarren Mill.",al={"where does mountain lion blood come from","source of mountain lion blood","who made mountain lion blood"},it="origin",add="7c379830"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, each vial you collect helps the Royal Apothecary Society develop biological weapons to secure Lordaeron for the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, gathering beast reagents around Tarren Mill strengthens your presence against hostile human enclaves in Hillsbrad."},kw={"alterac","apothecary lydon","elixir of pain","hillsbrad","mountain lion blood","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:501","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:horde","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Mountain Lion Blood","Elixir of Pain (quest)"}}
E["item:mudsnout-blossom"] = {t="item",n="Mudsnout Blossom",z="hillsbrad",s="Mudsnout Blossoms grow in Nethander Stead, south of Tarren Mill. Mudsnout gnolls guard the foul, toxic mushrooms, and Apothecary Lydon seeks them for his elixir research.",h="Mudsnout Blossoms grow in Nethander Stead, south of Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Toxic Fungus",b="South of Tarren Mill, Mudsnout Blossoms grow in Nethander Stead. Despite their name, they are large, foul-smelling mushrooms that flourish in soiled dirt among the local Mudsnout gnolls' camps. The gnolls defend the territory fiercely. The mushrooms' spores and flesh poison living things, causing agony and rapid bodily decay.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for the Royal Apothecary Society",b="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon uses Mudsnout Blossoms in his chemical experiments. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has charged the Royal Apothecary Society with creating a plague to eradicate both the Scourge and living humanity. The mushrooms' caustic, flesh-withering properties make them a base for Lydon's Elixir of Agony.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Mudsnout Blossom?",a="Despite the name, a Mudsnout Blossom is a large, pungent, toxic mushroom found in the damp soil of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"mudsnout blossom lore","is mudsnout blossom a flower","what kind of plant is mudsnout blossom"},it="identity"},{q="Where do Mudsnout Blossoms grow?",a="Mudsnout Blossoms grow throughout Nethander Stead, an abandoned farmstead south of Tarren Mill and east of the river that runs past Southshore. Mudsnout gnolls heavily infest the area.",al={"mudsnout blossom location","where to find mudsnout blossoms","nethander stead mushrooms"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society collecting them?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill needs Mudsnout Blossoms to brew the Elixir of Agony. The Forsaken study toxins to help make a plague that can wipe out both the living and the Scourge.",al={"why does lydon want mudsnout blossoms","elixir of agony ingredients","apothecary lydon mushroom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does the Royal Apothecary Society use the blossoms for?",a="Apothecary Lydon gathers the foul-smelling mushrooms for his next elixir, part of the Forsaken's research into disease and poisons.",al={"mudsnout blossom experiments","mudsnout blossom elixir use"},it="power"},{q="Where do Mudsnout Blossoms come from?",a="Mudsnout Blossoms are large, foul-smelling mushrooms that sprout in the fields of Nethander Stead in the southern Hillsbrad Foothills. They thrive around the local Mudsnout gnolls who dwell there and fiercely guard the patch, though whether the gnolls intentionally cultivate the pungent fungi or merely nest among them is uncertain.",al={"mudsnout blossom origin","where did mudsnout blossoms come from","who made mudsnout blossom"},it="origin",add="f0998bd9"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the Royal Apothecary Society harvests Mudsnout Blossoms for their toxic properties and to refine biochemical weapons.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you may expect a flower, but Mudsnout Blossom is a volatile, foul-smelling fungus prized by toxicologists and dark alchemists."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","hillsbrad foothills","mudsnout blossom","mudsnout gnolls","nethander stead","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","subzone:nethander-stead","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:gnoll","zone:hillsbrad","quest:367"},src={"Mudsnout Blossom","Elixir of Agony"}}
E["item:murloc-head"] = {t="item",n="Murloc Head",z="hillsbrad",s="Along the Western Strand, Murloc Head is grim proof of a threat Southshore wants brought under control. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle collects the severed heads for Marshal Redpath, who requires evidence of the murlocs being culled.",h="Along the Western Strand, Murloc Head is grim proof of a threat Southshore wants brought under control.",sec={{t="A Grislier Kind of Proof",b="Southshore's fishermen and coastal travelers face an immediate threat from aggressive murlocs along the Western Strand. Alliance fighters often clear the beaches, but Marshal Marcus Redpath wants proof before he approves reports of the threat being reduced. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle hires fighters to bring him murloc heads. Farren finds the work repulsive, and the sight has spoiled his appetite for Southshore's seafood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Farren Orinelle want murloc heads?",a="Marshal Marcus Redpath wants physical proof that murlocs have been cleared from the beaches. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle collects their severed heads to satisfy him.",al={"farren proof","why murloc heads","who wants murloc heads in southshore"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are these murlocs found?",a="The murlocs are found along the Western Strand, the coast west of Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"murloc head location","where to get murloc heads hillsbrad","western strand murlocs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Farren so disgusted by them?",a="Farren finds the murlocs unnatural and stomach-turning. Their severed heads disgust him so much that he refuses to eat fish, a staple of Southshore's diet.",al={"farren reaction","farren eating fish"}},{q="Does collecting the heads solve Southshore's murloc problem?",a="The heads give Marshal Redpath the proof he asked for. He accepts them and sends Farren to deal with threats on the Eastern Strand.",al={"do murlocs stop attacking","farren quest chain"}},{q="What is a Murloc Head?",a="It is the freshly severed skull of a murloc slain along the coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Cold, slimy, and oozing foul fluids, it serves as undeniable physical evidence of a beast cut down in the defense of Southshore.",al={"what is murloc head","murloc head info","murloc head item"},it="identity",add="ab7abae9"},{q="Where do Murloc Heads come from?",a="They are hacked directly from the bodies of the murlocs prowling the Western Strand, just west of Southshore. Rather than crafted goods, they are grisly trophies taken from the shoreline raiders troubling the Alliance garrison.",al={"where do murloc heads drop","who made murloc head","murloc head source"},it="origin",add="598cfa24"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, clearing the Western Strand helps protect Southshore's fishing economy and secure its coastline in Lordaeron."},kw={"farren orinelle","farren's proof","hillsbrad foothills","marshal redpath","murloc","murloc head","southshore","western strand"},rel={"quest:559","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:murloc","quest:536","quest:562","quest:563"},src={"Murloc Head","Farren's Proof"}}
E["item:renferrel-s-findings"] = {t="item",n="Renferrel's Findings",z="hillsbrad",s="In Silverpine Forest, Renferrel's Findings carry research south to Tarren Mill. Apothecary Renferrel gathered the notes at the Sepulcher for Apothecary Lydon, who is helping brew the Forsaken's New Plague.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Renferrel's Findings carry research south to Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Plague in Development",b="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel records his work on the New Plague. The Royal Apothecary Society labours under direct orders from Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Dark Lady. Researchers scattered across Lordaeron must work together to achieve a breakthrough. Renferrel sends his findings south to Tarren Mill, where fellow researchers can build on his results.",sp=0},{t="To Tarren Mill",b="The papers link Silverpine Forest to Hillsbrad Foothills and the Forsaken's alchemical network. Apothecary Lydon awaits Renferrel's notes in Tarren Mill, where he can compare them with his own work against the living and the Scourge. Reliable couriers must cross Hillsbrad's contested roads; without them, the Society's scattered research would quickly stall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Renferrel's Findings?",a="Renferrel's Findings contain Apothecary Renferrel's latest research and experimental data from Silverpine Forest. The notes concern the Forsaken's work to brew a New Plague.",al={"what are the findings","renferrel research","what is in the notes"},it="item"},{q="Who is supposed to receive this research?",a="Apothecary Lydon is to receive the documents. He conducts plague research in Tarren Mill, a Forsaken settlement in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who gets renferrels findings","where do the findings go","delivery target"},it="target"},{q="Why are the apothecaries sharing notes?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has ordered the Royal Apothecary Society to create a New Plague. The apothecaries believe comparing results will bring a breakthrough far more quickly than working alone.",al={"why share findings","why send to lydon","apothecary communication"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Apothecary Renferrel conduct his experiments?",a="Apothecary Renferrel conducts his experiments at the Sepulcher, the primary Forsaken outpost in the heart of Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is renferrel","apothecary renferrel location","who wrote renferrels findings"},it="place"},{q="What are Renferrel's Findings?",a="Renferrel's Findings are a collection of alchemical notes and research documents compiled by Apothecary Renferrel. They detail his ongoing experiments conducted on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society, intended to be shared directly with his fellow practitioners across Lordaeron.",al={"what is renferrels findings","renferrel findings item","what are these findings"},it="identity",add="f680c460"},{q="Where do Renferrel's Findings come from, and who made them?",a="These documents were authored by Apothecary Renferrel, an ambitious researcher stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Working diligently under the mandate of the Forsaken, he penned these notes to record his progress and breakthroughs in compounding experimental concoctions.",al={"who wrote renferrels findings","where did renferrels findings come from","renferrels findings creator"},it="origin",add="bf8d559a"},{q="Why does anyone want Renferrel's Findings?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society faces immense pressure from Lady Sylvanas Windrunner to concoct a New Plague. Believing that collaboration will accelerate their grim work, Renferrel sent his research to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, who is eager to study his colleague's methods and integrate them into his own efforts.",al={"why deliver renferrels findings","who wants renferrels findings","why does lydon want renferrels findings"},it="why_wanted",add="21b2c0f4"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know these papers serve Sylvanas Windrunner's ambition: to perfect a New Plague against the Scourge and the living foes encroaching on Forsaken lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know couriers carrying Renferrel's papers connect outposts such as the Sepulcher and Tarren Mill, strengthening the Horde's foothold across Lordaeron."},kw={"findings","lydon","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:493","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:367"},src={"Renferrel's Findings","Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills"}}
E["item:sack-of-murloc-heads"] = {t="item",n="Sack of Murloc Heads",z="hillsbrad",s="Along the Hillsbrad beaches, a gruesome sack of Murloc Heads is gathered as proof of military action against local shore pests. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle hands the bundle to passing adventurers for delivery to Marshal Redpath in Southshore.",h="Along the Hillsbrad beaches, a gruesome sack of Murloc Heads is gathered as proof of military action against...",sec={{t="Bureaucracy and Coastal Pests",b="Southshore faces constant attacks from Syndicate outlaws, Forsaken skirmishers, and wild murlocs along the coast. Local officers must show town leaders that coastal threats are being culled to secure funding and favor. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle collects severed heads as proof, but finds the cargo distasteful. His squeamishness leads him to hand the sack to travelers instead of bringing the grisly evidence to Marshal Redpath himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sack of Murloc Heads?",a="The Sack of Murloc Heads is a burlap sack of severed murloc heads gathered from Hillsbrad's western beaches. It gives Southshore's garrison commander physical proof of efforts to pacify the coast.",al={"sack of heads","murloc sack","what is this item"},it="identity"},{q="Why won't Lieutenant Farren deliver it himself?",a="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle finds carrying a foul-smelling bag of decaying murloc heads revolting. He hands the unpleasant delivery across Southshore to an obliging adventurer.",al={"why farren makes you carry it","farren's excuse","lazy farren"},it="motive"},{q="Who receives the sack?",a="Marshal Redpath receives the sack. He commands Southshore's defenses, assesses the town's security, and demands proof of defensive efforts.",al={"who gets the heads","where do i bring it","marshal redpath turn in"},it="target"},{q="Why does Southshore require murloc heads as proof?",a="Southshore requires murloc heads as proof because murlocs constantly raid the coast and threaten the harbor. Officers must verify that patrols maintain perimeter security, and tangible trophies help ensure soldiers do not claim credit for idle watches.",al={"why collect murloc heads","proof of kill"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Sack of Murloc Heads come from, and who made it?",a="The sack is assembled from the severed heads of the murlocs you hunted along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Lieutenant Farren Orinelle packed them together to present to his commanding officer, though he quickly hands the repulsive parcel back to you to deliver in his stead.",al={"who made sack of murloc heads","where did the sack of heads come from","who gave sack of murloc heads"},it="origin",add="3f14ed35"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the frayed logistics and unglamorous daily burdens Southshore's defenders bear as they hold the northern Alliance enclave together."},kw={"bounty","farren orinelle","heads","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","murloc","southshore"},rel={"quest:559","subzone:southshore","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","item:murloc-head","topic:murloc","quest:536","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Sack of Murloc Heads","Farren's Proof (2)"}}
E["item:shipment-of-iron"] = {t="item",n="Shipment of Iron",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad Fields, a crate of raw iron waits at the human smithy. The metal feeds local arms production, making the shipment a target for Forsaken forces seeking to cut the supply lines that arm the townsfolk.",h="In Hillsbrad Fields, a crate of raw iron waits at the human smithy.",sec={{t="Fueling the Resistance",b="Across the Hillsbrad Foothills, human peasants have mounted stiff resistance against Tarren Mill. Much of their strength comes from the smithy at the southwestern edge of Hillsbrad Fields, where Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices work round the clock, making weapons and armor from heavy shipments of iron. Forsaken commanders ordered the forge put out, its smiths killed, and its stored metal seized for the Horde war effort, hoping to break the farmers’ resolve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the shipment of iron kept?",a="The shipment is kept inside the blacksmith workshop at the southwestern edge of Hillsbrad Fields. Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices guard it closely.",al={"shipment of iron location","where is the iron","hillsbrad iron location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Forsaken want this iron?",a="The iron arms the local human militia, and the Forsaken want to cut off that supply. High Executor Darthalia also means to use the stockpiles for the Horde war machine when the offensive turns toward razing Southshore.",al={"why steal iron","tarren mill iron","battle of hillsbrad iron purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was using this iron originally?",a="Blacksmith Verringtan and his four apprentice smiths used the iron to arm the townspeople and field workers, turning simple farmers into a local defense force against the undead.",al={"who owns the iron","verringtan iron","hillsbrad blacksmiths"},it="origin"},{q="Who orders the retrieval of the iron shipment?",a="High Executor Darthalia, commanding Forsaken operations out of Tarren Mill, orders the smiths slain and the iron claimed during the Battle of Hillsbrad.",al={"who gives the quest","darthalia iron quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Shipment of Iron?",a="The Shipment of Iron is a stockpile of raw metal stored at the human blacksmith shop in the Hillsbrad Fields. It serves as the primary material Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices use to forge weapons and armor for the local Hillsbrad townsfolk resisting the Forsaken.",al={"what is shipment of iron","shipment of iron","iron shipment hillsbrad"},it="identity",add="8a003d21"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For a blacksmith, raw iron keeps human arms production in the valley alive. Without the ingots, Verringtan’s forge sits useless.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, denying Hillsbrad supplies weakens the farmers’ armed resistance before the campaign moves against Southshore."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad fields","shipment of iron","tarren mill","verringtan"},rel={"quest:527","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:human"},src={"Shipment of Iron","Battle of Hillsbrad (3)"}}
E["item:stormpike-banner"] = {t="item",n="Stormpike Banner",z="hillsbrad",s="Alliance recruits enter Icewing Cavern to earn the Stormpike Banner. The trial lies southwest of Dun Baldar in Alterac Valley, where harpies guard the standard.",h="Alliance recruits enter Icewing Cavern to earn the Stormpike Banner.",sec={{t="A Rite of Induction",b="Lieutenant Haggerdin sends new Alliance soldiers into Icewing Cavern southwest of Dun Baldar. Before they face the Frostwolf orcs, recruits must brave the harpies, seize the Stormpike Banner, and bring it back alive. Those who return earn the rank and insignia of an initiate in the Stormpike Guard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stormpike Banner located?",a="The Stormpike Banner lies deep inside Icewing Cavern, southwest of Dun Baldar in Alterac Valley.",al={"banner location","where is the stormpike banner","how to find banner"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do recruits have to retrieve the banner?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin asks Alliance recruits to prove their courage before joining the battle lines. Bringing back the banner earns them their initial Stormpike Insignia.",al={"proving grounds trial","why get banner","haggerdin quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What threats guard the banner inside the cave?",a="Savage local harpies guard Icewing Cavern and attack trespassers seeking the banner.",al={"monsters near banner","icewing cavern enemies"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Who do I return the banner to once found?",a="Return the banner to Lieutenant Haggerdin, the Alliance officer stationed outside the cave entrance in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"turn in banner","banner hand in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Stormpike Banner?",a="The Stormpike Banner is a military standard representing the Stormpike Guard, the dwarven expedition currently waging war across Alterac Valley. Planted deep inside the perilous, harpy-infested Icewing Caverns southwest of Dun Baldar, the banner serves as a trial marker. Recruits must venture into the frozen depths, brave the feral beasts lurking within, and recover the colors to prove their mettle and worthiness to wear the Stormpike insignia.",al={"what is stormpike banner","stormpike banner lore","about stormpike banner"},it="identity",add="27f01085"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance recruit, bringing back the banner earns you entry into the Stormpike Guard and the right to carry its battle insignia against the Frostwolf Clan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see the banner as a sign of Ironforge's claim and the Stormpike clan's mission to uncover relics of their past throughout the valley."},kw={"alterac valley","dun baldar","haggerdin","icewing caverns","insignia","proving grounds","stormpike banner"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-haggerdin","zone:alterac","topic:alliance","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Stormpike Banner","Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Alliance)"}}
E["item:tainted-keg"] = {t="item",n="Tainted Keg",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Tainted Keg carries stolen dwarven stout laced with a lethal Forsaken brew made by Apothecary Lydon. Sent to imprisoned human farmers as refreshments, it tests poisons being developed by the Royal Apothecary Society.",h="At Tarren Mill, Tainted Keg carries stolen dwarven stout laced with a lethal Forsaken brew made by Apothecary...",sec={{t="A Deadly Vintage",b="Dun Garok's dwarven riflemen lost a barrel of Shindigger Stout to thieves. Apothecary Lydon mixed the stout with his newly refined Elixir of Agony. The Forsaken chose an ordinary drink to carry the poison, hoping it would escape suspicion. A familiar ale became a swift death sentence.",sp=0},{t="Testing on the Condemned",b="Several human farmers were held upstairs in the Tarren Mill inn. High Executor Darthalia suspected a Stormwind military strategist was hiding among them. When word came that the strategist had died elsewhere, the farmers were no longer of use. Darthalia gave them to Lydon, who placed the poisoned keg on the rug in their holding room as part of a cruel celebration. Thirsty and desperate, the prisoners drank. The elixir killed them swiftly, proving its fatal potency.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Tainted Keg?",a="The keg holds Shindigger Stout, a dwarven ale stolen from Dun Garok and mixed with the Elixir of Agony, an experimental poison made by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",al={"tainted keg contents","what poison is in the keg","what is in the barrel"},it="item"},{q="Where did the ale originally come from?",a="The stout was taken from the dwarven mountaineers and riflemen at Dun Garok, a heavily defended fortress in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who made the ale","where was the stout stolen from","shindigger stout source"},it="origin"},{q="Who drinks from the keg?",a="Human farmers held in an upstairs room of the Tarren Mill inn drink from the keg and die almost at once from the poisoned brew.",al={"who drinks it","tainted keg victims","captured farmers"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Why were the farmers being held prisoner?",a="High Executor Darthalia imprisoned the farmers because she suspected an Alliance military strategist from Stormwind was hiding among them. After the strategist was confirmed dead in the Plaguelands, the farmers were deemed useless and handed to the apothecaries.",al={"why captive farmers","why did darthalia capture farmers","why are farmers in tarren mill"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Tainted Keg?",a="The Tainted Keg is a vessel of stolen dwarven Shindigger Stout that has been laced with a deadly concoction brewed by the Forsaken. Apothecary Lydon created this lethal batch of tainted brew to serve as a practical trial for his ongoing alchemical research.",al={"what is tainted keg","tainted keg item","what is this keg"},it="identity",add="fd5e0197",nx={6}},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want the Tainted Keg used?",a="Apothecary Lydon wants the keg delivered to test the efficacy of his newly finished Elixir of Agony. With the captured human farmers handed over to his disposal by High Executor Darthalia, offering them poisoned stout provides the Royal Apothecary Society a convenient means to observe the toxin's fatal effects firsthand.",al={"why use the tainted keg","why does lydon want tainted keg","purpose of tainted keg"},it="why_wanted",add="5c778a45"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Royal Apothecary Society, the tainted stout marks progress in making biological weapons that can eradicate humanity.",["race:Human"]="Laced ale used to kill captured rural laborers shows the merciless tactics facing the living remnants throughout Hillsbrad."},kw={"apothecary lydon","captured farmers","dun garok","elixir of agony","shindigger stout","tainted keg","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","item:keg-of-shindigger-stout","subzone:dun-garok","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:horde","topic:human"},src={"Tainted Keg","Elixir of Agony (5)"}}
E["item:worn-stone-token"] = {t="item",n="Worn Stone Token",z="hillsbrad",s="Across the Alterac Mountains, Worn Stone Token enchantments have faded, though Dalaran crafted them to command elementals. The tokens remain with Dalaran personnel, from mages to laborers.",h="Across the Alterac Mountains, Worn Stone Token enchantments have faded, though Dalaran crafted them to...",sec={{t="Tokens of Elemental Mastery",b="Dalaran’s magi command elementals with talismans that bend beings from other realms to their will. Worn Stone Tokens are depleted versions of these implements. Theurgists and summoners carry them, as do Dalaran laborers and guards stationed around the ruins and internment camps of Alterac. Their presence shows how deeply elemental binding reaches into Dalaran’s daily work.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Curiosity",b="At Tarren Mill, the Forsaken watch the nearby wizards. Magus Voidglare seeks Worn Stone Tokens to study Dalaran’s methods of enslaving elementals. Keeper Bel'varil directs agents to gather worn, inert tokens first. These let the Magus examine basic enchanting techniques safely before attempting more potent, volatile conduits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were these tokens used for?",a="Dalaran’s wizards use the stone tokens to bind and command elementals summoned from other realms, setting them to work as laborers, guards, and defenders.",al={"worn stone token purpose","what are stone tokens","why do dalaran carry tokens"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the tokens described as worn?",a="The tokens’ active enchantments have faded with time and heavy use. Keeper Bel'varil considers inert specimens safer for Magus Voidglare’s first study of Dalaran’s binding rituals.",al={"why worn","are tokens magical","inert tokens"}},{q="Who carries these tokens?",a="Dalaran personnel in the southern Alterac Mountains carry them, from high-ranking summoners and theurgists to ordinary laborers, shield guards, and Warden Belamoore at the internment camp.",al={"who drops worn stone tokens","where to get tokens","dalaran token drops"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Forsaken want them?",a="Magus Voidglare wants to study Dalaran’s arcane control of elementals and unravel its arts of summoning and subjugation.",al={"why does belvaril want tokens","magus voidglare tokens"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is a Worn Stone Token?",a="A Worn Stone Token is a faded magical artifact crafted by the mages of Dalaran. These enchanted stones serve as arcane implements used to bind, command, and control elemental servants summoned from other dimensions. Over time or through extensive handling, their innate magic has dulled into an inert state, yet they still retain the structural secrets of Dalaran's elemental craft.",al={"what is worn stone token","worn stone token","stone tokens"},it="identity",add="4cdbd814"},{q="Where do the Worn Stone Tokens come from, and who made them?",a="The tokens are created by the wizards and artificers of Dalaran, a magocracy renowned for its mastery over extradimensional magic. You will find them carried by Dalaran's forces stationed across the Alterac Mountains, including summoners, theurgists, shield guards, workers, and Warden Belamoore at the nearby internment camps.",al={"who made worn stone token","origin of stone tokens","where do stone tokens come from"},it="origin",add="2e06b1f4"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you recognize these tokens as practical focuses the Kirin Tor uses to keep conjured elementals stable and obedient in the field.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help the Forsaken at Tarren Mill study the arcane defenses and practices of the hostile Kirin Tor presence in Alterac."},kw={"alterac mountains","dalaran","elementals","keeper bel'varil","magus voidglare","stone tokens","tarren mill","worn stone token"},rel={"quest:556","npc:keeper-bel-varil","subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Worn Stone Token","Stone Tokens"}}
E["npc:brewmeister-bilger"] = {t="npc",n="Brewmeister Bilger",z="hillsbrad",s="Brewmeister Bilger waits in Southshore's inn cellar for deliveries from distant lands. The intoxicated dwarf passes his hours tasting potent spirits.",h="Brewmeister Bilger waits in Southshore's inn cellar for deliveries from distant lands.",sec={{t="Life in the Cellar",b="Brewmeister Bilger paces the cellar beneath Southshore's inn, nursing hiccups as he seeks the strongest brews Azeroth can offer.",sp=0},{t="A Taste for Potent Imports",b="Brewmeister Bilger can judge spirits despite his constant stupor. He favors heavy dwarven moonshines and potent southern liquors, and eagerly receives special batches such as the moonshine Foggy MacKreel sends from the Thandol Span.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Find Brewmeister Bilger in the cellar beneath the inn at Southshore, the Alliance port town in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"bilger location","where is bilger","southshore cellar dwarf"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Brewmeister Bilger receives rare liquor from the Wetlands, including strong spirits such as MacKreel's Moonshine, shipped north to Southshore.",al={"bilger quest","mackreel's moonshine quest"},gp=true},{q="Who is Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Brewmeister Bilger is a dwarven brewer who spends his days drinking in the cellar of the Southshore inn, hiccupping his way through strong spirits and waiting on moonshine owed to him by friends like Foggy MacKreel.",al={"who is bilger","brewmeister bilger identity","who is brewmeister bilger"},it="identity",add="0436bf77"},{q="Whose side is Brewmeister Bilger on?",a="Bilger is aligned with the Alliance and the town of Southshore. A dwarf of Ironforge, he makes his home peacefully among the local townsfolk, even if he prefers the quiet company of the cellar barrels to civic duties.",al={"bilger faction","is bilger alliance","whose side is bilger on"},it="side",add="29798063"},{q="Why is Brewmeister Bilger here?",a="Bilger has made the cellar of Southshore's inn his home, spending his days down among the casks with his strong spirits and the moonshine owed to him by friends like Foggy MacKreel.",al={"why is bilger in southshore","what is bilger doing here","why is brewmeister bilger here"},it="why_here",add="5541902b"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Bilger's love of strong drink thriving in a human port town far from Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find Bilger in Southshore's inn cellar, one of the dwarves who make their home among the humans of this beleaguered town."},kw={"bilger","brewmeister bilger","hillsbrad foothills","inn cellar","mackreel","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:647","topic:dwarf","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},src={"Brewmeister Bilger"}}
E["npc:chef-jessen"] = {t="npc",n="Chef Jessen",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Chef Jessen works to feed the town amid constant border tensions. He is best known for his famous turtle bisque.",h="In Southshore, Chef Jessen works to feed the town amid constant border tensions.",sec={{t="A Cook in Southshore",b="Chef Jessen supplies meat and provisions in Southshore, in the southern Hillsbrad Foothills, for locals and visiting Alliance soldiers. He is a skilled cook. Before plague and war disrupted northern Lordaeron, he often traveled north past Dalaran to the shores of Lordamere Lake. There he gathered meat from native snapjaw turtles to make his prized, hearty Soothing Turtle Bisque. He will share the recipe with travelers who help him gather its ingredients.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Chef Jessen?",a="Chef Jessen is a human butcher and cook in Southshore, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He sells meat and shares local recipes with travelers who support the Alliance.",al={"jessen","chef jessen southshore","who is jessen"},it="identity"},{q="What is Chef Jessen's famous dish?",a="Chef Jessen's signature dish is Soothing Turtle Bisque. In years past, he gathered fresh snapjaw turtle meat from around Lordamere Lake, north past Dalaran, to make the hearty broth.",al={"turtle bisque recipe","jessen specialty","soothing turtle bisque"},it="fame"},{q="Why does Chef Jessen ask travelers for help?",a="Gathering snapjaw turtle meat around Lordamere Lake has grown dangerous because of regional instability and the nearby Forsaken presence. Chef Jessen relies on capable travelers to collect the meat for his bisque.",al={"jessen quest","turtle meat quest"},it="wants"},{q="Does Chef Jessen sell anything unusual?",a="Chef Jessen sells meat to the people of Southshore. His specialty is Soothing Turtle Bisque, a recipe he teaches cooks who help gather snapjaw meat.",al={"jessen specialty","jessen food vendor"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Chef Jessen on?",a="Chef Jessen is loyal to the Alliance. He lives and works in Southshore, the primary human refuge and Alliance stronghold along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, catering to locals and travelers fighting to hold the line in Lordaeron.",al={"chef jessen alliance or horde","is chef jessen alliance","chef jessen faction"},it="side",add="4b3f98b6"},{q="Why is Chef Jessen in Southshore?",a="Chef Jessen operates as a local meat vendor and cook in Southshore. While he once traveled up past Dalaran and out to Lordamere Lake to hunt snapjaws himself, these days he stays safely behind in the town, relying on adventurous passersby to bring in fresh ingredients.",al={"why is chef jessen in southshore","chef jessen why here","what brought chef jessen to hillsbrad"},it="why_here",add="73d1d0ab"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook passing through Hillsbrad, you can turn to Jessen for his turtle bisque recipe, a substantial meal for hardy travelers.",["faction:Alliance"]="In Southshore, Jessen helps feed Alliance soldiers and adventurers holding the defensive line against northern threats."},kw={"chef jessen","cooking","hillsbrad foothills","jessen","lordamere lake","snapjaw","southshore","turtle bisque"},rel={"subzone:southshore","quest:555","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:dalaran","topic:alliance"},src={"Chef Jessen"}}
E["npc:christoph-jeffcoat"] = {t="npc",n="Christoph Jeffcoat",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Christoph Jeffcoat supplies the Forsaken with goods for trade and travel. His wares help crafters and travelers in Hillsbrad Foothills, where the Alliance and the Syndicate contest the land.",h="At Tarren Mill, Christoph Jeffcoat supplies the Forsaken with goods for trade and travel.",sec={{t="A Merchant on the Front Lines",b="Christoph Jeffcoat tends to the practical needs of Tarren Mill, the Forsaken stronghold in Hillsbrad Foothills. He sells reagents, tools, threads, and spices to soldiers and traveling artisans. His goods include the spices used in turtle bisque, rare schematics, and alchemical vials. Horde forces passing through southern Lordaeron rely on such supplies as they face Southshore and the dangers of the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Christoph Jeffcoat?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat is in Tarren Mill, the main Forsaken and Horde stronghold in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"christoph jeffcoat location","where is jeffcoat","tarren mill trade vendor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kinds of goods does he sell?",a="He sells tailoring threads, blacksmithing hammers, fluxes, alchemy vials, and cooking spices, including soothing spices and hot spices. He also carries select recipes.",al={"what does jeffcoat sell","christoph jeffcoat wares","jeffcoat items"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is he important for local cooks?",a="Jeffcoat sells Soothing Spices for Soothing Turtle Bisque and teaches the recipe to Horde cooks who bring him turtle meat from the snapjaws.",al={"soothing spices vendor hillsbrad","soothing turtle bisque ingredients","jeffcoat cooking"},gp=true},{q="Who is Christoph Jeffcoat?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat is an undead merchant stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He serves the Forsaken by providing trade supplies, raw materials, and crafting components to travelers, artisans, and defenders holding the Horde's front lines in the region.",al={"who is christoph jeffcoat","christoph jeffcoat identity","who is jeffcoat"},it="identity",add="36cd3db3"},{q="Whose side is Christoph Jeffcoat on?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat is firmly loyal to the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed inside the heavily contested outpost of Tarren Mill, he caters directly to Horde adventurers and champions battling the nearby Alliance forces from Southshore.",al={"christoph jeffcoat faction","is christoph jeffcoat horde","who does christoph jeffcoat serve"},it="side",add="1470d19f"},{q="Why is Christoph Jeffcoat here in Tarren Mill?",a="With Tarren Mill acting as the northern anchor for Horde operations in Hillsbrad Foothills, crafters and fighters constantly run low on everyday supplies. Christoph Jeffcoat is stationed here to ensure trade goods, vials, threads, and spices remain readily available to those defending the post.",al={"why is christoph in tarren mill","christoph jeffcoat why here","why is jeffcoat in hillsbrad"},it="why_here",add="7ff6f152"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook in Hillsbrad, you can buy Soothing Spices from Christoph Jeffcoat. Bring him snapjaw meat, and he teaches you his Soothing Turtle Bisque recipe.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion campaigning in Hillsbrad Foothills, you can find crafting materials and common tools at Christoph Jeffcoat's shop in Tarren Mill."},kw={"christoph jeffcoat","forsaken merchant","hillsbrad","soothing spices","tarren mill","trade supplies","trade vendor"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:7321","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Christoph Jeffcoat"}}
E["npc:deathguard-humbert"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Humbert",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Deathguard Humbert watches the Alliance presence in Hillsbrad. The Forsaken sentry has lost his military gear to dwarves from Dun Garok.",h="At Tarren Mill, Deathguard Humbert watches the Alliance presence in Hillsbrad.",sec={{t="A Guard Relieved of His Steel",b="Deathguard Humbert watches Dun Garok from a hidden camp for High Executor Darthalia. One morning, he left to gather firewood. Dwarven scouts from Dun Garok took his prized sword and other equipment while he was away. Now he must recover his arms and save his pride before high command learns what happened.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Humbert?",a="Deathguard Humbert guards and scouts from Tarren Mill. He watches Alliance operations across the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"humbert lore","who is humbert","humbert tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Humbert's sword and armor?",a="High Executor Darthalia sent Humbert to watch Dun Garok from a hidden camp. One morning, he went to gather firewood. When he returned, dwarven scouts from Dun Garok had taken his gear, including his prized sword.",al={"humberts sword stolen","who took humberts gear","why does humbert need help"}},{q="Why doesn't Humbert just recover his gear himself?",a="Dun Garok is heavily fortified, with disciplined dwarven riflemen and mountaineers. A lone scout outside its trenches has little chance, and Humbert cannot easily leave his post without answering for how he lost his kit.",al={"why cant humbert fight","humbert dun garok"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Humbert on?",a="Deathguard Humbert serves the Forsaken and, by extension, the Horde. As a member of the Deathguard, he stands as a sentry and soldier sworn to the defense of Lordaeron and the will of the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"deathguard humbert faction","humbert allegiance","who does humbert serve"},it="side",add="9e6e6cc1"},{q="What does Deathguard Humbert want?",a="Humbert wants the return of his personal military equipment, particularly his sword. Dwarven scouts from Dun Garok made off with it while he was away from his hidden camp gathering firewood, leaving him empty-handed and desperate for someone capable to venture into enemy territory and reclaim it.",al={"humbert goal","what does humbert need","why does humbert give quests"},it="wants",add="f61ba0a7"},{q="Why is Deathguard Humbert stationed here?",a="Humbert is stationed at Tarren Mill to monitor the hostile Alliance presence in the Hillsbrad Foothills, specifically keeping an eye on the dwarven forces holed up at Dun Garok. His post ensures the Forsaken settlement remains alerted to movements from the south.",al={"why is humbert in tarren mill","humbert mission","what is humbert doing here"},it="why_here",add="ed7fd663"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering Humbert's sword strikes back at the dwarven foothold in Hillsbrad and helps preserve the dignity of Tarren Mill's garrison.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken soldiers are expected to serve the Dark Lady with unyielding vigilance. Humbert's lapse against the living leaves an embarrassing blemish on the Deathguard."},kw={"deathguard humbert","dun garok","hillsbrad foothills","humbert","humbert's sword","stormpike","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:547","subzone:dun-garok","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Deathguard Humbert"}}
E["npc:deathguard-samsa"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Samsa",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Deathguard Samsa watches the tense frontier and sends travelers against threats near the settlement.",h="In Tarren Mill, Deathguard Samsa watches the tense frontier and sends travelers against threats near the...",sec={{t="Frontier Sentry of Tarren Mill",b="Deathguard Samsa keeps watch in Tarren Mill, where the Forsaken hold their ground in the contested Hillsbrad Foothills. Horde sentries face pressure from Alliance outposts such as Southshore and from savage local wildlife. Samsa guards the perimeter and directs capable adventurers against threats before they endanger the encampment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Samsa?",a="Deathguard Samsa serves the Forsaken military in Tarren Mill. He guards the town and directs visiting adventurers to help secure the region from nearby dangers.",al={"samsa","who is samsa","deathguard samsa role"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Deathguard Samsa?",a="Find Deathguard Samsa in Tarren Mill, the major Horde settlement in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"samsa location","where is deathguard samsa","tarren mill guard location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Deathguard Samsa give out?",a="Samsa sends adventurers into the Hillsbrad wilderness, including to collect the skulls of Hillsbrad humans slain during the Horde's campaign against them.",al={"samsa quests","souvenirs of death quest giver"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Deathguard Samsa on?",a="Deathguard Samsa serves the Forsaken and the Horde. As a deathguard stationed in Tarren Mill, he acts under the authority of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, guarding Forsaken holdings in the Hillsbrad Foothills and securing the region against nearby threats.",al={"deathguard samsa faction","is samsa horde","who does samsa serve"},it="side",add="97a7e196"},{q="Why is Deathguard Samsa here in Tarren Mill?",a="Deathguard Samsa is posted in Tarren Mill as part of the Forsaken military presence guarding the settlement. Tarren Mill serves as a critical northern bastion in the Hillsbrad Foothills, requiring steadfast guards to watch over the town and monitor dangerous wildlife and enemy movements in the surrounding lands.",al={"why is samsa in tarren mill","deathguard samsa purpose hillsbrad","why is deathguard samsa here"},it="why_here",add="fc9d92c7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the grim, practical defense needed to hold Lordaeron's southern border against hostile neighbors.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler in Hillsbrad Foothills, you rely on sentries like Samsa to coordinate defenses against nearby Alliance aggression from Southshore."},kw={"deathguard samsa","forsaken","hillsbrad","samsa","souvenirs of death","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:546","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:southshore"},src={"Deathguard Samsa"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-lesh"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Lesh",z="hillsbrad",s="At Southpoint Tower, Deathstalker Lesh watches the human farms in the Hillsbrad Foothills. She serves High Executor Darthalia and gauges when the Forsaken should strike.",h="At Southpoint Tower, Deathstalker Lesh watches the human farms in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Fields",b="From Southpoint Tower, Deathstalker Lesh watches the human farmers and town militia in the nearby Hillsbrad Fields. The tower stands on the southern road through the Hillsbrad Foothills. Lesh belongs to the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's covert network of scouts, spies, and assassins. She tracks enemy movements and numbers for High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill. When the moment is right, Lesh sends Darthalia a coded message: “The raven's cry from the west doth beckon.” The words signal that Hillsbrad is ripe for the Forsaken's attack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Lesh?",a="Lesh is a Forsaken scout at Southpoint Tower. She answers to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill and watches human activity across the Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"deathstalker lesh","who is lesh","lesh hillsbrad"},it="identity"},{q="What are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers serve Queen Sylvanas Windrunner as scouts, spies, and assassins. They gather intelligence for the Forsaken military and eliminate high-value targets across Lordaeron.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker order","forsaken rogues"}},{q="What is Lesh's role at Southpoint Tower?",a="Lesh keeps watch from Southpoint Tower, surveying both the Hillsbrad Fields and the town of Hillsbrad. When the moment is right, she sends a traveler to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill with a coded message signaling that Hillsbrad is ripe for attack.",al={"southpoint tower scout","lesh quest","why is lesh here"},it="why_here"},{q="Who does Lesh report to?",a="Lesh reports to High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander at Tarren Mill who oversees the offensive against the human forces in Hillsbrad.",al={"lesh boss","who commands lesh","high executor darthalia"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Lesh on?",a="Deathstalker Lesh is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, operating as part of the Horde forces in Hillsbrad Foothills. As an operative stationed at Southpoint Tower under the command of Tarren Mill, she works tirelessly to secure Forsaken supremacy in the region.",al={"deathstalker lesh faction","lesh alliance or horde","who does lesh serve"},it="side",add="5ae1cd6e"},{q="What does Deathstalker Lesh want?",a="Lesh wants to see Hillsbrad fall to the Forsaken. Stationed as a scout on the front lines, she surveys the human town, and when the moment is right she needs a fast messenger to carry her coded signal to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill so the attack can begin.",al={"what does lesh want","lesh goal","deathstalker lesh objective"},it="wants",add="024a29bd"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you as Forsaken, scouts like Lesh help secure Lordaeron from Alliance resurgents.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you share the covert work Deathstalker Lesh performs for the Horde's war effort."},kw={"deathstalker lesh","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad foothills","southpoint tower","tarren mill","time to strike"},rel={"subzone:southpoint-tower","quest:494","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken"},src={"Deathstalker Lesh"}}
E["npc:drum-fel"] = {t="npc",n="Drum Fel",z="hillsbrad",s="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel directs the Horde’s fight to hold Arathi against trolls, ogres, and human remnants. With his wife Korin, he works to secure a lasting foothold for the Horde in the region.",h="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel directs the Horde’s fight to hold Arathi against trolls, ogres, and human remnants.",sec={{t="Warden of Hammerfall",b="Drum Fel commands Hammerfall’s defenses and the Horde’s push into Arathi. From the fortified refuge, he faces rival factions on every side. The Witherbark forest trolls and the Boulderfist ogres hold Boulder'gor and Boulderfist Hall. Drum knows Hammerfall cannot thrive by keeping to itself; its neighbors’ strength must be broken. He sends veteran champions into hostile territory to disrupt these threats before they can strike the Horde encampment.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Stromgarde",b="Drum Fel carries his campaign into Stromgarde Keep, where Boulderfist ogres have made their stand among the ruins of the fallen human kingdom. Years ago, Drum defeated the ogre brute Or'Kalar, and the ogre has not forgotten. Or'Kalar now waits inside Stromgarde, seeking vengeance. Korin, Drum’s wife, quietly works to hide Or'Kalar’s presence from her husband. She relies on outside adventurers to remove the threat before Drum charges into an ambush.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Drum Fel?",a="Drum Fel leads the Horde’s military efforts from Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, directing campaigns against rival factions in the region.",al={"drum fel","who is drum fel","hammerfall drum"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Drum Fel be found?",a="Drum Fel can be found inside Hammerfall, in northeastern Arathi Highlands, just east of the main road north into the Hinterlands.",al={"drum fel location","where is drum fel","find drum fel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Korin Fel?",a="Korin Fel is Drum Fel’s wife, and she lives in Hammerfall.",al={"korin fel","drum fel wife"},it="ties"},{q="Why does the ogre Or'Kalar want Drum Fel dead?",a="Years ago, Drum Fel defeated Or'Kalar in battle. The humiliated ogre now waits in the ruins of Stromgarde Keep, seeking vengeance against Drum.",al={"orkalar grudge","why does orkalar hate drum fel","or'kalar drum fel"},it="conflict"},{q="What threats does Drum Fel target?",a="Drum Fel directs strikes against the Boulderfist ogres at Boulder'gor, Boulderfist Hall, and Stromgarde Keep, along with the nearby Witherbark troll tribe.",al={"drum fel quests","drum fel enemies","who does drum fel fight"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Drum Fel on?",a="Drum Fel is a stalwart leader within the Horde. Stationed at the outpost of Hammerfall, he directs military efforts to secure the safety and dominance of the Horde across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"drum fel faction","who does drum fel serve","drum fel horde"},it="side",add="51d7fbcd"},{q="What does Drum Fel want?",a="Drum Fel wants to ensure that Hammerfall survives and thrives amidst hostile territory. To protect the settlement, he orders decisive campaigns against rival forces threatening the region, including the Boulderfist ogres, the Witherbark trolls, and hostile occupants within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep.",al={"drum fel goals","what does drum fel need","drum fel motive"},it="wants",add="828c27d6"},{q="Why is Drum Fel in Hammerfall?",a="Drum Fel oversees military operations from Hammerfall to safeguard the Horde's foothold in the Arathi Highlands. From this bastion, he coordinates the defense of his people against surrounding threats that seek to wipe the settlement out.",al={"why is drum fel here","drum fel arathi","drum fel purpose arathi"},it="why_here",add="def003ab"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde warriors advancing through the Eastern Kingdoms, Drum Fel coordinates the military effort to secure the fragile lifeline between the Undercity and the southern territories.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Drum Fel shows the hard resolve needed to rebuild orcish lives in the Eastern Kingdoms, holding ground in the land where the internment camps once stood."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","drum fel","hammerfall","korin fel","orkalar","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","npc:tallow","subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:boulder-gor","subzone:boulderfist-hall","quest:676","topic:horde"},src={"Drum Fel"}}
E["npc:high-executor-darthalia"] = {t="npc",n="High Executor Darthalia",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia directs the Forsaken war in Hillsbrad. Under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras, she targets Southshore and the Syndicate.",h="At Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia directs the Forsaken war in Hillsbrad.",sec={{t="Commander of Tarren Mill",b="High Executor Darthalia commands Forsaken forces from Tarren Mill. She works to contain the human forces in Southshore and hunt the Syndicate brigands across the Hillsbrad Foothills. Every Forsaken offensive in southern Hillsbrad passes through her command.",sp=0},{t="The War for Hillsbrad",b="High Executor Darthalia follows orders from the Undercity's leaders, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras. She directs the war across Hillsbrad, with scouting, strikes against human leaders, and bounties on outlaws who threaten Forsaken control of northern Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Darthalia?",a="High Executor Darthalia leads Forsaken forces in the Hillsbrad Foothills. She directs their efforts against Southshore and the Syndicate.",al={"who is darthalia","darthalia identity","executor darthalia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Darthalia be found?",a="Darthalia commands Forsaken forces from Tarren Mill, coordinating troops and strikes across central Lordaeron.",al={"darthalia location","where is darthalia","executor darthalia map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who does Darthalia answer to?",a="Darthalia answers to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras, the Undercity's leaders.",al={"darthalia boss","darthalia faction","who commands darthalia"},it="ties"},{q="What tasks does Darthalia give to adventurers?",a="Darthalia sends Horde champions against human settlements and dangerous outlaws, including Syndicate members throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"darthalia quests","quests from darthalia","what does darthalia want"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Darthalia fighting the humans of Southshore?",a="Darthalia fights to contain Southshore's Alliance forces, protect Tarren Mill, and stop them from pushing north toward the Undercity.",al={"why attack southshore","southshore war","hillsbrad conflict"},it="motive"},{q="What is Darthalia's rank in the Forsaken military?",a="As a High Executor, Darthalia holds a high rank in the Forsaken military and commands regional forces, outposts, and war strategy in Hillsbrad.",al={"high executor rank","darthalia title"}},{q="Whose side is High Executor Darthalia on?",a="High Executor Darthalia serves the Forsaken and the Horde. She operates as a high-ranking military commander under the authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and Varimathras, directing Horde operations in Hillsbrad Foothills to secure the region against Alliance encroachment.",al={"darthalia faction","who does darthalia fight for","is darthalia horde"},it="side",add="c2c985e7"},{q="What does High Executor Darthalia want?",a="Darthalia seeks to halt the spread of humanity and root out Alliance influence across the Hillsbrad Foothills. She coordinates strikes against nearby human strongholds like Southshore and eliminates rival threats such as the Syndicate to ensure unchallenged Forsaken control over the territory.",al={"darthalia goals","what is darthalia trying to do","darthalia purpose"},it="wants",add="77f4a495"},{q="Why is High Executor Darthalia here?",a="She is stationed in Tarren Mill to oversee the Forsaken campaign in the Hillsbrad Foothills. From this central vanguard, she organizes war efforts against the hostile human settlements to the south and secures the southern approaches to Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity.",al={"why is darthalia in tarren mill","darthalia hillsbrad why","reason darthalia is here"},it="why_here",add="f4963853"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see Darthalia's resolve to keep Lordaeron in undead hands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you report to Darthalia to oppose the Alliance and hold Hillsbrad's contested frontier.",["faction:Alliance"]="To Southshore's humans and their allies, Darthalia leads the assaults threatening their foothold in Lordaeron."},kw={"darthalia","high executor","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","southshore","sylvanas","syndicate","tarren mill","varimathras"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","subzone:southshore","npc:varimathras","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","quest:494","quest:549"},src={"High Executor Darthalia"}}
E["npc:keeper-bel-varil"] = {t="npc",n="Keeper Bel'varil",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Keeper Bel'varil studies magic and alchemy for the Forsaken. His work with Wordeen Voidglare draws Horde adventurers into the search for relics and binding materials across Hillsbrad Foothills.",h="At Tarren Mill, Keeper Bel'varil studies magic and alchemy for the Forsaken.",sec={{t="Study in Tarren Mill",b="Keeper Bel'varil supports Forsaken magic and alchemy in besieged Tarren Mill. The royal apothecaries and soldiers focus on the Alliance garrison down the road at Southshore. Bel'varil turns to practical sorcery, sending travelers to recover stone tokens and binding bracers from nearby elemental and enchanted threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Keeper Bel'varil?",a="Keeper Bel'varil studies magic in Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He works with fellow researcher Wordeen Voidglare to examine magical artifacts and reagents found across the contested territory.",al={"keeper belvaril","who is belvaril","belvaril tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Keeper Bel'varil?",a="Keeper Bel'varil stands in Tarren Mill, the Forsaken settlement in northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"belvaril location","where is keeper bel'varil","find keeper bel'varil"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What tasks does Keeper Bel'varil offer?",a="Keeper Bel'varil sends Horde adventurers to collect magical remnants, including stone tokens and bracers of binding. He studies them to understand and manipulate elemental forces.",al={"belvaril quests","keeper bel'varil tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Keeper Bel'varil on?",a="Keeper Bel'varil is loyal to the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Stationed in Tarren Mill, he works alongside his undead brethren to secure the Hillsbrad Foothills against Alliance aggression and assist in the strategic research being carried out by his fellow Forsaken.",al={"bel'varil faction","is bel'varil horde","bel'varil allegiance"},it="side",add="07ee922c"},{q="What does Keeper Bel'varil want?",a="Bel'varil seeks mystical components and artifacts to assist with specialized arcane research. To aid Wordeen Voidglare's work in Tarren Mill, he enlists travelers to retrieve enchanted remnants, such as stone tokens and bracers of binding, from the elementals and ruins in the surrounding regions.",al={"bel'varil goal","what does bel'varil need","why help bel'varil"},it="wants",add="19ba277e"},{q="Why is Keeper Bel'varil here in Tarren Mill?",a="Keeper Bel'varil remains stationed in Tarren Mill to support the Forsaken's territorial and arcane interests in Hillsbrad Foothills. Working in concert with researchers like Wordeen Voidglare, he coordinates the gathering of magical supplies needed to bolster their hold against nearby enemies.",al={"why is bel'varil in tarren mill","bel'varil hillsbrad purpose","why is keeper bel'varil here"},it="why_here",add="4541a85d"},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'varil tied to?",a="Keeper Bel'varil works closely with Wordeen Voidglare, another Forsaken scholar stationed in Tarren Mill. Bel'varil acts as an assistant and coordinator, organizing adventurers to gather the specific materials and tokens Wordeen requires for his ongoing studies.",al={"bel'varil associates","who does bel'varil work for","bel'varil connections"},it="ties",add="b0435467"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion in Hillsbrad Foothills, you can aid Bel'varil by subduing elemental threats and recovering binding charms. He offers practical rewards for this work.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you share Bel'varil's pursuit of arcane mastery and resourcefulness. His careful study of regional relics seeks an edge for your people in Lordaeron."},kw={"bel'varil","bracers of binding","hillsbrad foothills","keeper bel'varil","stone tokens","tarren mill","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:556","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:southshore"},src={"Keeper Bel'varil"}}
E["npc:krusk"] = {t="npc",n="Krusk",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Krusk coordinates the search for his captured scouts and the Syndicate's relics. Sent by Warchief Thrall to investigate Durnholde Keep, he survived an ambush that scattered his team.",h="At Tarren Mill, Krusk coordinates the search for his captured scouts and the Syndicate's relics.",sec={{t="A Mission Gone Wrong",b="Krusk leads the effort from Tarren Mill after a failed strike at Durnholde Keep. Warchief Thrall sent him and a small team to scout Syndicate activity and recover relics tied to the fortress's grim past. The human outlaws were more entrenched and coordinated than expected, and an ambush inside the crumbling walls overwhelmed the orcish scouts. Krusk fought his way out. Drull and Tog'thar were taken captive and locked within the ruins, while Gol'dir, the expedition's leader, was moved to another Syndicate hold. Krusk now directs Horde forces to breach Durnholde, recover the lost items, and free his trapped comrades.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Syndicate",b="From Tarren Mill, Krusk tracks the Syndicate's movements in Hillsbrad. The fallen nobles of Alterac operate from Durnholde Keep, plotting against Horde outposts and their former Alliance brethren. Krusk watches leaders such as Lord Aliden Perenolde, hoping to break their command before they threaten the Horde's tenuous foothold in Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Krusk?",a="Krusk serves Warchief Thrall as an orc scout at Tarren Mill. He was sent to investigate Syndicate operations around Durnholde Keep and recover historic relics.",al={"krusk","who is krusk","krusk tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Krusk's squad?",a="The Syndicate ambushed Krusk and his team inside Durnholde Keep. Krusk escaped, while Drull and Tog'thar were imprisoned in the ruins and Gol'dir, the expedition's leader, was taken to another Syndicate hold.",al={"krusk squad","what happened to krusk","durnholde ambush"},it="conflict"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Durnholde Keep?",a="The Horde is interested in Durnholde Keep because it holds personal and historical meaning for Warchief Thrall. Aedelas Blackmoore raised him there as a captive gladiator before Thrall led the orcish rebellion that razed the keep.",al={"why durnholde","thrall durnholde","durnholde relics"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Krusk?",a="Krusk is outdoors at Tarren Mill, the Horde settlement in northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"krusk location","where is krusk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Krusk on?",a="Krusk is a loyal operative of the Horde. Dispatched directly under orders from Warchief Thrall, he operates out of Tarren Mill to serve Orgrimmar's strategic interests across the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"krusk faction","is krusk horde","who does krusk serve"},it="side",add="86db3c10"},{q="What does Krusk want?",a="Krusk needs capable champions to rescue his captured companions—Gol'dir, Drull, and Tog'thar—from the Syndicate within the ruins of Durnholde Keep. He also seeks to uncover Syndicate operations and secure an item of great importance tied to Durnholde's history.",al={"what does krusk need","krusk goals","what is krusk looking for"},it="wants",add="943a1bb4"},{q="Why is Krusk here in Tarren Mill?",a="Warchief Thrall personally sent Krusk and his squad into Hillsbrad to investigate Syndicate activities around Durnholde Keep. After an ambush left his scouts imprisoned, Krusk fell back to Tarren Mill to regroup and recruit aid to finish the mission.",al={"why is krusk in hillsbrad","krusk tarren mill why","why did thrall send krusk"},it="why_here",add="2e7680ba"},{q="Who is Krusk tied to?",a="Krusk answers to Warchief Thrall, who sent him to Hillsbrad with an expedition led by Gol'dir, alongside fellow orcs Drull and Tog'thar. From Tarren Mill, he coordinates his efforts alongside the local Horde garrison.",al={"krusk companions","krusk allies","who does krusk work with"},it="ties",add="fe85a88a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see Krusk carrying Warchief Thrall's interests into Lordaeron. He works to secure Durnholde's history and keep captured orcs from Syndicate hands.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, helping Krusk rescue his fellow scouts touches the honor and painful history of the internment camps. Durnholde is the fortress where Thrall broke his people's chains."},kw={"drull","durnholde keep","gol'dir","hillsbrad","krusk","syndicate","tarren mill","thrall","tog'thar"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:syndicate","npc:thrall","quest:498","zone:hillsbrad","topic:horde","quest:1361"},src={"Krusk"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",z="hillsbrad",s="At Southshore's inn, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle drinks and leaves his duties to others. He resents his posting in the Hillsbrad Foothills and hopes for a transfer south. Marshal Redpath has assigned him to deal with the murlocs along the coast.",h="At Southshore's inn, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle drinks and leaves his duties to others.",sec={{t="Exile in Southshore",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle spends his days at Southshore's inn, far from the Stormwind he prefers. Sent north from Stormwind City, he finds the contested shores of Hillsbrad a poor fit. Rather than patrol the fields or coordinate defenses with Marshal Redpath, he drinks, grumbles, and waits for an order transferring him south.",sp=0},{t="Outsourcing Duty",b="Marshal Redpath has tasked Lieutenant Farren Orinelle with clearing murlocs from the nearby shoreline. Orinelle leaves the muddy coast to passing travelers, asking them to kill the creatures and bring proof. He hopes the results will satisfy his superiors and hasten his return to Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle?",a="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is a Stormwind officer stationed in Southshore, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He drinks at the inn and grumbles about his posting.",al={"farren orinelle","who is orinelle","southshore lieutenant"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he in Southshore?",a="He was transferred north from Stormwind City to support Marshal Redpath and the local garrison. Orinelle dislikes the assignment and wants to return home.",al={"why is farren in southshore","orinelle transfer"},it="why_here"},{q="What is his official assignment?",a="Marshal Redpath ordered Orinelle to deal with the hostile murlocs along the Hillsbrad coast. Orinelle prefers to pay travelers to fight them.",al={"farren duty","orinelle mission","farren murlocs"},it="purpose"},{q="Does he ever leave the Southshore inn?",a="Orinelle spends almost all his time at the Southshore inn, reluctant to face the muddy beaches or hostile elements outside.",al={"where to find farren","farren location","orinelle inn"},gp=true},{q="What is Farren's ultimate goal?",a="Orinelle wants an official reassignment to Stormwind City, away from Lordaeron's coast.",al={"what does farren want","reassignment"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Orinelle's commander?",a="Orinelle reports to Marshal Redpath, who commands the Alliance detachment defending Southshore.",al={"farren superior","farren boss","who commands farren"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle on?",a="Lieutenant Orinelle serves the Grand Alliance and answers directly to the military forces of Stormwind. Though he detests his current assignment in the Hillsbrad Foothills, his post under Marshal Redpath places him squarely on the side of Southshore's defenders against both regional terrors and Horde aggression.",al={"orinelle faction","farren orinelle alliance","who does farren serve"},it="side",add="7d023078"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions, Orinelle is a disgruntled southern soldier at a lonely northern outpost, willing to offer coin and commendation to anyone who takes on his duties.",["race:Human"]="Orinelle is a Stormwind soldier far from Elwynn Forest. His disdain for northern frontier duty shows the divide between comfortable capital life and harsh overseas deployments."},kw={"farren","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","murloc","orinelle","reassignment","southshore","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:536","quest:559","quest:562","quest:563","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:murloc"},src={"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle"}}
E["npc:magistrate-henry-maleb"] = {t="npc",n="Magistrate Henry Maleb",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb keeps order in the Alliance's chief coastal stronghold in Hillsbrad Foothills. The port town faces threats from the Forsaken and the Syndicate.",h="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb keeps order in the Alliance's chief coastal stronghold in Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="Guardian of Southshore's Order",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb governs from Southshore's town hall, one of the last true Alliance settlements in Lordaeron. Forsaken forces threaten the town from the north and west, while highwaymen prowl the foothills. Maleb took office after the previous magistrate was mysteriously assassinated, an act he blames on the Syndicate. He means to avoid the same fate. His investigations seek hidden assassins, Syndicate supply networks, and the nobles directing them from the ruins of Alterac.",sp=0},{t="A Web of Noble Treachery",b="The Syndicate's reach runs through the region. Assassins moving through the orchards outside Southshore are paid operatives taking contracts from fallen Alteraci aristocrats. Maleb sends trusted Alliance scouts to intercept their coded plans and kill their leaders. He works to break the Syndicate's hold before its plots can cripple Southshore's defenses.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magistrate Henry Maleb?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb keeps civic order in Southshore, a coastal Alliance haven in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He oversees the town's civil affairs and protects it from threats within.",al={"henry maleb","southshore magistrate","who is maleb"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Maleb investigating the Syndicate?",a="Maleb took office after Southshore's previous magistrate was assassinated. His investigations point to Syndicate assassins hired by fallen Alteraci nobles, and he commissions Alliance adventurers to prevent another attempt on his life.",al={"why syndicate","maleb syndicate","southshore assassins"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Magistrate Maleb be found?",a="You can find Magistrate Henry Maleb inside Southshore's town hall, in the southern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"maleb location","where is henry maleb","find magistrate maleb"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats does Maleb face in Hillsbrad?",a="Maleb faces the threat of Forsaken expansion from the north and west, along with Syndicate killers stalking Southshore's outskirts and plotting against its leadership.",al={"southshore threats","maleb enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Magistrate Henry Maleb on?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb is devoted entirely to the Alliance. As the civil magistrate of Southshore, he serves the local township and answers to the Alliance authorities, working to keep the remaining free humans of Hillsbrad united and safe against surrounding hostiles.",al={"magistrate maleb faction","maleb alliance or horde","is henry maleb alliance"},it="side",add="078ca783"},{q="What does Magistrate Henry Maleb want?",a="Maleb wants to safeguard Southshore from destruction and bring an end to the Syndicate's predation. Having stepped into office after his predecessor was assassinated, he is determined to identify the conspirators, track down their shadowy assassins, and punish the Alteraci nobles directing the plots against the town.",al={"henry maleb goals","what does maleb need","magistrate maleb objective"},it="wants",add="b9806b6f"},{q="Why is Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore?",a="Maleb was recently assigned as the magistrate of Southshore following the assassination of the town's previous leader. He presides in the Southshore town hall to govern the settlement, oversee town defense, and coordinate Alliance investigations into the threats lurking across the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"why is maleb in southshore","maleb southshore reason","magistrate maleb town hall"},it="why_here",add="a611609c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion in Hillsbrad, you can look to Magistrate Maleb as civic authority in a lawless borderland. He offers bounties on Syndicate cutthroats destabilizing Southshore.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see why Maleb is deeply concerned with stealth and assassination. He relies on keen-eyed operatives to outmaneuver the Syndicate's concealed killers."},kw={"alterac","assassins","henry maleb","hillsbrad","magistrate maleb","southshore","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Magistrate Henry Maleb"}}
E["npc:marcus-redpath"] = {t="npc",n="Marcus Redpath",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Marshal Marcus Redpath holds Lordaeron's last southern bastion on the coast. He organizes patrols and bounty contracts against nearby ogres, murlocs, and naga.",h="In Southshore, Marshal Marcus Redpath holds Lordaeron's last southern bastion on the coast.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of Southshore",b="Marshal Marcus Redpath guards Southshore, the Alliance port on the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. The town endured the fall of Lordaeron's capital and the devastating Scourge invasion. Redpath now leads its defense, protecting the survivors who remain there.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Coast",b="Southshore stands virtually alone against hostile forces pressing in from every side. Marshal Redpath coordinates the defense across the Hillsbrad Foothills and enlists seasoned adventurers to push back the Crushridge ogres advancing from Alterac. He also sends them against dangerous naga and murloc encampments along the coast. The Forsaken occupy the north, and nearby Tarren Mill is heavily fortified. Redpath's vigilance helps keep the Alliance presence in the region from collapsing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marcus Redpath?",a="Marcus Redpath is Southshore's marshal and military authority in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He oversees the town's defense against threats from the surrounding wilderness and hostile neighbors.",al={"marcus redpath lore","who is the marshal in southshore","marcus redpath info"},it="identity"},{q="What role did he play in the Second War?",a="No account of the Second War records Redpath's part in it. Today, Southshore's marshal holds the town against the ogres, murlocs, and naga of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"second war marcus","did marcus redpath meet lothar"},it="history"},{q="What threats does he focus on fighting?",a="Redpath organizes efforts against local predators and invaders pressing toward Southshore. He issues bounties and missions targeting the Crushridge ogre tribe in the Alterac foothills, coastal murlocs, and raiding naga.",al={"marcus redpath quests","what does redpath want killed"},it="threat"},{q="Is he related to the Redpaths of Darrowshire?",a="Marcus Redpath shares the surname made famous by Captain Joseph Redpath of Darrowshire in the Eastern Plaguelands. No direct kinship has been established beyond their shared heritage in the Kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"redpath family","is marcus related to joseph redpath","redpath relatives"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Marcus Redpath be found?",a="Marshal Redpath is stationed in central Southshore, an Alliance haven on the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where is marcus redpath","marcus redpath location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Marcus Redpath on?",a="Marshal Marcus Redpath serves the Alliance and the survivors of Lordaeron who have gathered under Southshore's banner. As Southshore's town marshal, he stands staunchly with the human defenders holding the Hillsbrad line against hostile threats across the foothills.",al={"marcus redpath faction","what faction is marcus redpath","who does redpath serve"},it="side",add="0aeeadbf"},{q="What does Marcus Redpath want?",a="Redpath wants to secure Southshore and its surrounding lands from encroaching perils. He actively directs soldiers and adventurers to eliminate regional dangers, pushing back the Crushridge ogre tribes from the northern mountains and eradicating the murloc and naga infestations plaguing the coast.",al={"marcus redpath goals","what does redpath need","marcus redpath purpose"},it="wants",add="43107ef7"},{q="Why is Marcus Redpath here?",a="Marcus Redpath serves as Southshore's marshal. Since the fall of Lordaeron in the Third War, the town has been one of the Alliance's last strongholds in the region, and he organizes its defenses and keeps order there.",al={"why is marcus redpath in southshore","redpath southshore reason","what is redpath doing here"},it="why_here",add="402d4dad"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can help Marshal Redpath secure Hillsbrad against encroaching ogres and coastal hazards.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Redpath holding one of humanity's last footholds in Lordaeron. He keeps Southshore standing while the kingdom around it lies in ruin."},kw={"crushridge","hillsbrad","marcus redpath","marshal","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:559","topic:third-war"},src={"Marcus Redpath"}}
E["npc:master-apothecary-lydon"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Lydon",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon studies poisons for the Royal Apothecary Society. Bored and sunk in gloom, he takes pleasure in lethal brews and the suffering they cause. His research seeks to secure Hillsbrad for the Forsaken and advance Sylvanas's New Plague.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon studies poisons for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sec={{t="The Recluse of Tarren Mill",b="Inside Tarren Mill's chapel, now a laboratory, Apothecary Lydon carries out the cold work of the Royal Apothecary Society. Flowers in bloom and Hillsbrad Foothills' crisp air only deepen his languid melancholy. Deathcraft is the one diversion that lifts his gloom. Left alone, he poisons, dissects, and reanimates his pet frog, Umpi, again and again while he waits for new reagents.",sp=0},{t="Concoctions of Agony",b="With Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity, Lydon runs field experiments across Hillsbrad. His work advances from the Elixir of Suffering to the virulent Elixir of Agony. He sends adventurers to test the brews on local wildlife, domesticated animals, and captured human farmers. His loyalty belongs wholly to the Dark Lady, and he longs for their finished New Plague to cleanse the living world.",sp=1},{t="Venom of the Loa",b="Lydon's studies also reach into esoteric poisons. When mysterious venom bottles appear in the region, he asks troll mystics such as Master Gadrin to trace their origin. The trail leads to the spider goddess Shadra in the Hinterlands. Once gathered, the primeval venom goes to the Apothecarium in the Undercity to advance the Forsaken plague effort.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="From Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills, Lydon works as an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society. He oversees experimental plagues and toxins for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who is lydon","lydon tarren mill","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Lydon so depressed?",a="Lydon is sunk in melancholy and finds Hillsbrad's natural beauty and fresh air repulsive. Cruel experiments, the suffering of the living, and the scent of alchemical embalming fluids are the only things that lift his spirits.",al={"why is he sad","lydon depression","why is lydon gloomy"}},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is the frog Lydon keeps in his workshop and wryly calls his assistant. To relieve his boredom, he repeatedly poisons, kills, and reanimates her.",al={"lydon frog","who is the frog","umpi lore"}},{q="What is the Elixir of Agony?",a="The Elixir of Agony is an experimental poison Lydon brews from Mudsnout Blossoms, then refines with Master Apothecary Faranell's colloid of decay. He activates it with a strong troll's blood potion, daggerspine scales, and torn fin eyes, then laces a keg of stout stolen from the dwarves of Dun Garok and tests it on captive farmers in Hillsbrad.",al={"elixir of agony quest","what is elixir of agony","lydon elixir"},sp=1},{q="How did Lydon become Forsaken?",a="No record tells how Lydon died or rose. Like the other Forsaken, he broke free of the Lich King's control under Sylvanas and now devotes his undead existence to the Dark Lady and her New Plague.",al={"lydon past","was lydon human","lydon third war"},it="origin"},{q="What does Lydon send to the Undercity?",a="After finding ancient venom vessels in the Hinterlands and helping bring about the downfall of the troll spider god Shadra, Lydon gathers her concentrated, divine venom. He sends it directly to Master Apothecary Faranell to strengthen the Society's plague research.",al={"lydon undercity venom","shadra venom quest"},sp=1},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Lydon on?",a="Apothecary Lydon is fiercely loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Forsaken, and the Horde. He is a ranking researcher in the Royal Apothecary Society, taking direct guidance from Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity. Everything he concocts serves Sylvanas's grand designs to secure the realm for the undead.",al={"lydon faction","who does lydon serve","is lydon forsaken"},it="side",add="4ad88718"},{q="What does Apothecary Lydon want?",a="Lydon is consumed by the creation and perfection of the New Plague for the Dark Lady. He seeks potent toxins, predator blood, and lethal venoms from across the region to refine his brews—including the Elixir of Suffering and Elixir of Agony—aiming to bring misery and death to the living.",al={"what is lydon trying to do","lydon goal","why does lydon want poisons"},it="wants",add="64f2c0db"},{q="Why is Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill?",a="Lydon is stationed at the Tarren Mill apothecary lab to gather regional reagents and test lethal alchemical formulas close to enemy territory. Hillsbrad Foothills offers fertile testing grounds against local wildlife, hostile dwarven incursions, and the human town of Southshore just down the road.",al={"why is lydon in hillsbrad","lydon tarren mill purpose","why is apothecary lydon here"},it="why_here",add="26e1a5a5"},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon tied to?",a="Lydon answers directly to Master Apothecary Faranell and the Royal Apothecary Society. He collaborates with colleagues across Azeroth, helping Apothecary Zamah of Thunder Bluff brew a toxin for the Horde's troubles in the Stonetalon Mountains, and coordinating research with other Forsaken apothecaries stationed throughout Lordaeron.",al={"lydon connections","who works with lydon","lydon allies"},it="ties",add="19c08bcd"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, Lydon embodies the Royal Apothecary Society's mission: develop the New Plague to secure a future for the Forsaken and eradicate the living.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the humans of Southshore, Lydon is a horror who brews lethal diseases and tests them without distinction on captive Hillsbrad farmers and wildlife.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Lydon's workshop holds reagents, cauldrons, and rotting flora, showing how the Apothecary Society turns traditional gathering arts toward its work."},kw={"apothecary","elixir of agony","faranell","hillsbrad","lydon","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"npc:master-apothecary-faranell","npc:umpi","npc:master-gadrin","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:509"},src={"Master Apothecary Lydon"}}
E["npc:tallow"] = {t="npc",n="Tallow",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Tallow watches the contested front lines for the Dark Lady and the Horde. The Forsaken warrior helps organize strikes against Alliance threats in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",h="At Tarren Mill, Tallow watches the contested front lines for the Dark Lady and the Horde.",sec={{t="A Blade in Tarren Mill",b="Tallow stands with the Forsaken and Horde forces holding Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Conflict stirs across the region, with Southshore humans nearby, Syndicate outlaws on the roads, and hostile wildlife beyond the town. Tallow sends capable adventurers against the Boulderfist ogres of the Arathi Highlands to test their strength. Then he directs them to aid the besieged outpost of Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tallow?",a="Tallow is a Forsaken warrior in Tarren Mill who organizes Horde champions fighting in the area.",al={"who is tallow","tallow lore","tallow tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Tallow?",a="Tallow stands in Tarren Mill, a Forsaken-held town in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where is tallow","tallow location","find tallow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Tallow offer?",a="Tallow sends Horde adventurers to prove themselves against the Boulderfist ogres of the Arathi Highlands, then report to Drum Fel at besieged Hammerfall.",al={"tallow quests","the hammer may fall quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is Tarren Mill's role in the conflict?",a="Tarren Mill is the Horde's main stronghold in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills. It faces skirmishes and open warfare with Southshore, the human bastion to the south.",al={"why is tarren mill important","tarren mill role"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Tallow on?",a="Tallow serves the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Stationed in Tarren Mill, he stands with the undead defenders holding the line in Hillsbrad against the hostile human forces of Southshore and the regional threats pressing against the Horde's southern borders.",al={"tallow faction","is tallow horde","tallow allegiance"},it="side",add="df176dd7"},{q="What does Tallow want?",a="As a warrior stationed at the front lines of Tarren Mill, Tallow seeks to secure the Forsaken settlement and weaken their enemies across Hillsbrad. He directs capable Horde champions to strike at looming threats, including sending adventurers on dangerous missions like 'The Hammer May Fall' to undermine rival forces.",al={"tallow goal","what is tallow doing","tallow motive"},it="wants",add="cc135250"},{q="Why is Tallow in Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is the primary stronghold of the Forsaken in the Hillsbrad Foothills, constantly under pressure from the Alliance in Southshore and other hostile factions. Tallow is garrisoned here as a warrior to defend the town, coordinate martial strikes, and enlist passing Horde fighters to bolster their front lines.",al={"why is tallow here","tallow tarren mill","tallow purpose hillsbrad"},it="why_here",add="b53e5a72"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help Tallow weaken the human presence throughout the Hillsbrad Foothills.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you share Tallow's fight to extend Undercity's dominion south of the Alterac Mountains."},kw={"forsaken","hillsbrad foothills","horde warrior","tallow","tarren mill","the hammer may fall"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:676","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Tallow"}}
E["npc:umpi"] = {t="npc",n="Umpi",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Umpi endures Apothecary Lydon's experiments. The frog is kept in the Royal Apothecary Society's workshop as a test subject for toxins and plague brews.",h="In Tarren Mill, Umpi endures Apothecary Lydon's experiments.",sec={{t="A Life of Perpetual Testing",b="Umpi is a frog in Tarren Mill who bears the cost of Apothecary Lydon's experiments. For Lydon, testing his formulas requires living flesh, and he gives Umpi lethal brews such as the Elixir of Suffering and the Elixir of Agony. The poisons kill her, but Lydon re-animates her so she can face another dose for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a frog kept by Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. Lydon uses her as an assistant and as the chief subject of his alchemical experiments.",al={"umpi who","what is umpi","frog tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon keep killing Umpi?",a="Apothecary Lydon uses Umpi to measure the strength of his newly brewed toxins. He gives her fatal brews such as the Elixir of Suffering, then re-animates her for another trial.",al={"why kill umpi","umpi poisoned","lydon frog"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Umpi alive or undead?",a="Umpi is raised from the dead after each fatal poisoning. Apothecary Lydon says he re-animates her, though she functions as a beast.",al={"is umpi undead","umpi zombie","frog undead"}},{q="Where can Umpi be found?",a="Umpi is inside the apothecary workshop in Tarren Mill, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. She is beside Apothecary Lydon's workbench.",al={"where is umpi","umpi location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Umpi on?",a="Umpi is essentially the captive assistant and test subject of Apothecary Lydon and the Royal Apothecary Society. Rather than having any political loyalty to the Forsaken or the Horde, she simply endures whatever concoctions Lydon decides to pour down her throat.",al={"umpi faction","is umpi horde","who does umpi serve"},it="side",add="3625273f"},{q="Who is Umpi tied to?",a="Umpi is tied directly to Apothecary Lydon, serving as his unwilling laboratory assistant in Tarren Mill. Her entire existence revolves around testing his lethal concoctions, dying to their venomous effects, and being dragged back from death to undergo the process again.",al={"umpi apothecary lydon","who owns umpi","umpi master"},it="ties",add="d54b4816"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Royal Apothecary Society's ruthless methods firsthand: its researchers treat life and death as variables in perfecting the Forsaken arsenal."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","elixir of suffering","frog","hillsbrad foothills","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","quest:496","quest:509","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Umpi"}}
E["npc:vanndar-stormpike"] = {t="npc",n="Vanndar Stormpike",z="hillsbrad",s="At Dun Baldar, Vanndar Stormpike leads the Stormpike Expedition into Alterac Valley. He searches its frozen peaks for ancient relics and raw resources, waging an unyielding Alliance war against the Frostwolf orcs.",h="At Dun Baldar, Vanndar Stormpike leads the Stormpike Expedition into Alterac Valley.",sec={{t="Lord of Dun Baldar",b="Vanndar Stormpike leads the dwarven excavation into Alterac Valley as a veteran mountain king of Ironforge. After the Third War, he marched the Stormpike Guard into the northern mountains to seek hidden mineral riches and long-lost titan artifacts. He made Dun Baldar his fortified base, claiming the valley as ancestral ground and rightful Alliance territory. From there, he directs military outposts, defensive bunkers, and frontline pushes. Vanndar is determined that no retreat will ever be sounded under his watch.",sp=0},{t="War for the Frozen Pass",b="Vanndar's mining and prospecting reached into the Frostwolf clan's home, starting a brutal mountain war. The orcs demanded that he withdraw, but he refused to yield an inch, vowing Alterac Valley would belong to the dwarves. From his throne room deep within Dun Baldar, with marshals and bodyguards at his side, Vanndar oversees the defense against Frostwolf incursions. He also sends Alliance champions to break enemy lines and claim the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vanndar Stormpike?",a="Vanndar Stormpike commands the Stormpike Expedition as a dwarf mountain king. From Dun Baldar, he leads the Alliance war effort in Alterac Valley.",al={"who is vanndar","vanndar stormpike lore","stormpike leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Vanndar fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="Vanndar brought the Stormpike Expedition to Alterac Valley to seek ancient relics and extract natural resources. His refusal to abandon those claims drew the dwarves into bloody conflict with the native Frostwolf orcs.",al={"why are dwarves in alterac","vanndar motive","stormpike purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does Vanndar stay?",a="Vanndar commands his forces from Dun Baldar, the northern stronghold in Alterac Valley. Dwarven bunkers, marshals, and elite guards protect it.",al={"where is vanndar","vanndar location","dun baldar boss"},it="place"},{q="Who is Vanndar's main enemy?",a="Vanndar's main enemy is Drek'Thar, chieftain and elder shaman of the Frostwolf clan. Drek'Thar seeks to drive the dwarven interlopers from the Frostwolves' ancestral homeland.",al={"vanndar rival","who does vanndar fight","frostwolf leader"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Vanndar Stormpike on?",a="Vanndar Stormpike is a proud dwarven mountain king who fights fiercely for Ironforge and the Grand Alliance. As supreme commander of the Stormpike Guard and the expedition into Alterac Valley, he directs all Alliance military and excavation efforts against the Frostwolf orcs and their Horde allies.",al={"vanndar stormpike faction","is vanndar alliance","who does vanndar fight for"},it="side",add="3cffa9d0"},{q="What does Vanndar Stormpike want?",a="Vanndar wants nothing less than total dwarven dominion over Alterac Valley. His expedition came seeking natural resources, ancestral history, and titan relics buried in the mountains, but with the Frostwolf clan resisting their claim, his goal is to completely drive out the orcs and secure the entire valley for the Alliance.",al={"vanndar stormpike goal","what does vanndar want","vanndar stormpike purpose"},it="wants",add="6ebb293f"},{q="Who is Vanndar Stormpike tied to?",a="Vanndar is the head of the Stormpike Expedition and leads the Stormpike Guard, an elite dwarven military force tied directly to King Magni Bronzebeard and the kingdom of Ironforge.",al={"vanndar stormpike clan","who is vanndar related to","vanndar stormpike connections"},it="ties",add="36b37a58"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you can see Vanndar's indomitable Mountain King spirit in his fight to claim ancient heritage and honor the Explorer's Guild.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Vanndar as the leading commander on the Alterac front. He holds the northern ramparts and pushes Alliance territory into the wild mountains."},kw={"alterac","dun baldar","dwarf","frostwolf","mountain king","stormpike","vanndar"},rel={"topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:third-war"},src={"Vanndar Stormpike"}}
E["npc:warmaster-laggrond"] = {t="npc",n="Warmaster Laggrond",z="hillsbrad",s="Outside Alterac Valley, Warmaster Laggrond prepares Horde fighters for the Frostwolf clan. He commands from the valley’s entrance in the Alterac Mountains, where warriors answer the call to aid the Frostwolves.",h="Outside Alterac Valley, Warmaster Laggrond prepares Horde fighters for the Frostwolf clan.",sec={{t="Frontline Commander",b="Warmaster Laggrond directs the Horde's fight against the Stormpike Expedition at Alterac Valley's entrance. In the bitter cold, he admits only capable fighters to represent the Frostwolf clan and the wider Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Path of Honor",b="Warmaster Laggrond sends arriving combatants through the Proving Grounds before they enter battle. As warriors fight across the frozen peaks, he measures their standing and honors those who earn renown among the Frostwolves.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Warmaster Laggrond located?",a="Warmaster Laggrond is posted near the Horde encampment at Alterac Valley's entrance portal, in the snowy passes of the Alterac Mountains north of Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"laggrond location","where is laggrond","alterac valley entrance warmaster"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Warmaster Laggrond's role?",a="Warmaster Laggrond recruits for the Horde's war in Alterac Valley. He tests new fighters and honors those who earn standing with the Frostwolf clan.",al={"what does laggrond do","laggrond purpose","why talk to laggrond"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the Proving Grounds quest?",a="Warmaster Laggrond asks prospective recruits to retrieve a Frostwolf banner from the Wildpaw Den in Alterac Valley. The trial proves their resourcefulness before they join the campaign.",al={"proving grounds horde","laggrond initial quest"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="The Frostwolf clan claims Alterac Valley as its home after exile during the First War. The Stormpike Guard, an Alliance dwarven expedition, has pushed into the region in search of relics and territory, sparking a bitter territorial war.",al={"why alterac valley","frostwolf war","alterac valley conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Can Alliance players interact with Warmaster Laggrond?",a="No. Warmaster Laggrond is a devoted Horde champion and attacks Alliance trespassers who approach his mountain outpost.",al={"can alliance talk to laggrond","laggrond hostile"},gp=true},{q="Who is Warmaster Laggrond?",a="Warmaster Laggrond is an orc officer stationed at the entrance to Alterac Valley in the snowy reaches of the Alterac Mountains. He serves the Frostwolf clan and the broader Horde war effort, evaluating arriving champions and directing capable soldiers toward the battle against the Stormpike dwarves.",al={"who is laggrond","warmaster laggrond lore","laggrond alterac"},it="identity",add="050e2655"},{q="Whose side is Warmaster Laggrond on?",a="Laggrond stands firmly with the Horde, specifically representing the interests of the Frostwolf clan. He regards the Alliance—especially the encroaching Stormpike Expedition—as invaders trespassing on ancestral Frostwolf territory.",al={"is laggrond horde","warmaster laggrond faction","laggrond alliance or horde"},it="side",add="ccc612bb"},{q="What does Warmaster Laggrond want?",a="Laggrond seeks stalwart champions willing to prove themselves in the harsh conflict of Alterac Valley. He wants the Frostwolf lands defended, the dwarven expedition crushed, and Horde fighters to earn standing and honor among the clan through blood and duty.",al={"what does laggrond want","laggrond goal","laggrond objective"},it="wants",add="29764588"},{q="Why is Warmaster Laggrond here?",a="Stationed right outside the portal to the valley, Laggrond acts as a gatekeeper and recruiter for the frontline. He inspects those who answer the Frostwolves' call to arms, ensuring only determined fighters carry the clan's banner into battle.",al={"why is laggrond in alterac","laggrond location purpose","why is warmaster laggrond here"},it="why_here",add="b3dc84d2"},{q="Who is Warmaster Laggrond tied to?",a="Laggrond answers to the leadership of the Frostwolf clan, fighting on behalf of General Drek'Thar and the Horde forces committed to holding Alterac Valley against dwarven excavation and conquest.",al={"laggrond ties","laggrond frostwolf","who does laggrond work for"},it="ties",add="6fc2678d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Warmaster Laggrond is your first contact for the Alterac Valley war effort. He recognizes your battlefield achievements for the Frostwolf clan.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, answering Laggrond's summons means defending the Frostwolf clan's ancestral refuge from dwarven intrusion.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Laggrond's tests of frontline courage, meant to prove you can hold against heavy dwarven armor and vanguard charges."},kw={"alterac mountains","alterac valley","frostwolf","laggrond","proving grounds","pvp","stormpike","warmaster laggrond"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Warmaster Laggrond"}}
E["npc:winstone-wolfe"] = {t="npc",n="Winstone Wolfe",z="hillsbrad",s="At Ravenholdt Manor, Winstone Wolfe keeps watch over the estate grounds. The human operative belongs to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt's secretive organization, hidden between Hillsbrad and the Alterac Mountains.",h="At Ravenholdt Manor, Winstone Wolfe keeps watch over the estate grounds.",sec={{t="A Fixer in the Mountains",b="Winstone Wolfe works among Lord Jorach Ravenholdt's syndicate at Ravenholdt Manor. Quiet and watchful, he handles business around the manor and watches its grounds and groundskeepers. Only those with discretion and talent walk there undisturbed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Winstone Wolfe?",a="Winstone Wolfe is a human rogue working within Ravenholdt Manor, the League of Assassins' secluded headquarters high above Hillsbrad Foothills and the Alterac Mountains.",al={"who is wolfe","winstone wolfe lore","ravenholdt wolfe"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Winstone Wolfe?",a="Winstone Wolfe is at Ravenholdt Manor, reached by a hidden path winding north through the mountains from the Durnholde Keep area in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"wolfe location","where is winstone wolfe","find winstone wolfe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is his role in Ravenholdt?",a="Winstone Wolfe works as an operative and guard around the manor, watching its grounds and assisting with the syndicate's logistical affairs.",al={"what does wolfe do","wolfe purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Winstone Wolfe on?",a="Winstone Wolfe is aligned with Ravenholdt, the secretive league of thieves and assassins operating out of Ravenholdt Manor. Tucked away in the hidden foothills overlooking Hillsbrad and Alterac, he serves the guild rather than either the Alliance or the Horde.",al={"winstone wolfe faction","who does winstone wolfe work for","is winstone wolfe ravenholdt"},it="side",add="2ccf77f3"},{q="Why is Winstone Wolfe here?",a="Wolfe operates out of Ravenholdt Manor as part of the hidden league of rogues based in the mountains. Whether watching the grounds or assisting fellow guild operatives, he remains where the guild's business is conducted.",al={"why is winstone wolfe at ravenholdt","winstone wolfe ravenholdt manor why"},it="why_here",add="d63e8a08"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may recognize Winstone Wolfe as an operative at Ravenholdt Manor, where rogues travel into the mountains to hone their craft with the syndicate."},kw={"alterac","hillsbrad","ravenholdt","ravenholdt manor","rogue","winstone wolfe"},rel={"subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:ravenholdt","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac"},src={"Winstone Wolfe"}}
E["quest:2480"] = {t="quest",n="Hinott's Assistance",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, a Horde rogue seeks Serge Hinott's help against Zanzil's poison. The Forsaken chemist studies the toxin and prepares a cure.",h="At Tarren Mill, a Horde rogue seeks Serge Hinott's help against Zanzil's poison.",sec={{t="A Toxic Masterpiece",b="After a Barrens assignment leaves you suffering from a toxin that clouds the mind, you are sent north to Tarren Mill. Serge Hinott, a Forsaken chemist, studies the poison made by Zanzil, a jungle troll exile. Hinott cares little about the troll's identity or kin. He admires the brew's vicious effect and wants to understand how it works before making an antidote.",sp=0},{t="The Antidote and the Trade",b="Hinott needs time to isolate the poison's active agents. His finished remedy halts the creeping madness, though he says its lingering stench remains. Once the venom no longer weakens you, Hinott shares what he learned from Zanzil's work. You can use that knowledge to prepare tactical poisons of your own.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happens during Hinott's Assistance?",a="Wait a few moments in Tarren Mill while Serge Hinott prepares the antidote. When it is ready, speak with him to take the cure and clear Zanzil's poison.",al={"what do i do here","hinott assistance walk","how to finish quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Serge Hinott?",a="Serge Hinott is a Forsaken alchemist and poison expert at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He helps Horde rogues cure unusual afflictions and learn to prepare venom.",al={"serge hinott lore","who is hinott","tarren mill apothecary"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Serge Hinott impressed by the poison?",a="Hinott admires the craft in Zanzil's formula, which combines creeping madness with physical weakness. Though he works to stop its effects, he praises the skill behind the destructive brew.",al={"zanzil poison reaction","why does hinott like it"},it="motive"},{q="What is the lingering smell Hinott mentions?",a="Zanzil's mixture leaves a pungent, sickly odor that lingers in the victim's pores. Hinott's antidote halts the poison and clears the mind, but the stench remains for a time.",al={"why do i smell","madness smell","quest smell"}},{q="What is the reward for completing this quest?",a="The cure clears the lasting affliction from your rogue training and opens the way to learning Rogue Poisons, so you can brew debilitating coatings.",al={"what do rogues get","hinotts assistance reward"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Where is this quest turned in?",a="You meet Serge Hinott at Tarren Mill in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills, where he begins and completes the work.",al={"where is hinott","turn in location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you are cured of the affliction from your initiation and gain the knowledge to make tactical poisons.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can learn from Forsaken alchemy as it turns jungle troll toxins into field knowledge.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see Apothecary Hinott's detached admiration for poison made with skill, whatever its origin."},kw={"anti-toxin","cure","hillsbrad","hinott","poisons","rogue quest","serge hinott","tarren mill","zanzil"},rel={"npc:serge-hinott","quest:2479","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Serge Hinott",level="21",faction="Horde",id=2480},src={"Hinott's Assistance (2)"}}
E["quest:493"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills",z="hillsbrad",s="Renferrel sends his research south to Tarren Mill, where the Forsaken press on with their plague studies. You carry his notes from Silverpine Forest to Apothecary Lydon in Hillsbrad Foothills.",h="Renferrel sends his research south to Tarren Mill, where the Forsaken press on with their plague studies.",sec={{t="A Plague of Their Own",b="Since escaping the Lich King's control, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has pursued a New Plague that could destroy both the living and the Scourge. The Royal Apothecary Society works under the Banshee Queen's relentless pressure to create it. Its researchers are scattered across Lordaeron, so they share chemical data and test findings to hasten their work.",sp=0},{t="The Road South",b="Apothecary Renferrel works from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest and sends you south with his recent findings for Apothecary Lydon. Your road leaves the pine woods and crosses the open pastures of Hillsbrad Foothills. Tarren Mill lies beneath the Alterac Mountains, serving the Forsaken as an outpost and a place to stage their research.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Renferrel's findings?",a="Renferrel's notes document his experiments with local plants, animals, and biological toxins. They contribute to the Royal Apothecary Society's work on the New Plague.",al={"what are the findings","renferrel research","what am i delivering"},it="item"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society in such a rush?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner demands quick results. The Forsaken face hostile human remnants, the Scarlet Crusade, and wandering Scourge. They believe a biological weapon can secure their survival and avenge Arthas.",al={"why rush plague","why under pressure","sylvanas pressure"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a senior Royal Apothecary Society researcher stationed in Tarren Mill. Respected by Renferrel and his other peers, he oversees biological experiments in Hillsbrad Foothills, refining plague strains with local supplies and captives.",al={"who is lydon","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill lies in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, south of the Alterac Mountains and east of Silverpine Forest. Follow the main roads south from Silverpine, then turn east at the crossroads to reach it.",al={"tarren mill location","how to get to tarren mill","where is hillsbrad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken have to share findings via foot couriers?",a="Renferrel asks you to carry his written findings from the Sepulcher to Lydon in Tarren Mill. He wants the Society's distant researchers to share discoveries quickly, but gives no reason for using foot couriers instead of magical means.",al={"why foot messenger","why courier delivery"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after Lydon gets the research?",a="After receiving Renferrel's notes, Apothecary Lydon begins studying them and working their findings into his own concoctions. He later asks adventurers to test improved strains on the local human population.",al={"what next after delivering","lydon reaction"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want his findings delivered?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is under severe pressure from Lady Sylvanas to develop a New Plague to secure the Forsaken's survival. Renferrel knows that their alchemical breakthroughs can only succeed quickly if the apothecaries pool their research rather than working in isolation. By sending his latest discoveries to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, he hopes to accelerate the Society's collective progress.",al={"why send findings to lydon","renferrel motive","why deliver the plague research"},it="motive",add="c31bc166"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help advance your people's efforts to survive and avenge themselves against the living and the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help secure the Forsaken's hold in Hillsbrad and strengthen the Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms, despite orc and tauren misgivings about underhanded poisons.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know that Renferrel and Lydon study and gather virulent, mutated plants from across Lordaeron."},kw={"hillsbrad","lydon","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","silverpine","sylvanas","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:367"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="20",faction="Horde",id=493},src={"Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills"}}
E["quest:494"] = {t="quest",n="Time to Strike",z="hillsbrad",s="At the Hillsbrad border, Time to Strike carries Lesh's signal east to Tarren Mill. Her coded message moves word from a quiet watch to Forsaken plans against Hillsbrad's humans.",h="At the Hillsbrad border, Time to Strike carries Lesh's signal east to Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Watcher at the Border",b="Deathstalker Lesh watches the valley from high ground near the border of Silverpine Forest and the Hillsbrad Foothills. Below, human settlers and militia move through the valley. The Deathstalkers serve as the Undercity's eyes and ears, watching enemy settlements before troops deploy. Lesh stays at her post and asks passing Horde travelers to carry her gathered intelligence down the road to Tarren Mill.",sp=0},{t="A Coded Beckon",b="Lesh's message is veiled: “The raven's cry from the west doth beckon.” Carried east along the road, it tells High Executor Darthalia that Hillsbrad's human defenses are vulnerable. For Darthalia and the dreadlord Varimathras, the signal means the time has come to mobilize Forsaken forces and carry out campaigns against Hillsbrad's human defenders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What does Deathstalker Lesh's message mean?",a="“The raven's cry from the west doth beckon” is a coded reconnaissance update. It tells High Executor Darthalia that Hillsbrad's western approaches are poorly guarded and ripe for an immediate offensive.",al={"raven's cry meaning","what does the raven cry mean","lesh message"}},{q="Who is High Executor Darthalia?",a="High Executor Darthalia is the supreme Forsaken military commander in the Hillsbrad Foothills. From Tarren Mill, she directs attacks against the Southshore humans and works closely with Varimathras in the Undercity.",al={"who is darthalia","darthalia role"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lesh send a courier instead of going herself?",a="Lesh is on a critical reconnaissance mission at Hillsbrad's western edge. Leaving her post would leave a blind spot in Forsaken surveillance, so she asks passing Horde travelers to carry her urgent dispatches.",al={"why doesn't lesh leave","why couriers"},it="why_me"},{q="Where is this message meant to be delivered?",a="The message is meant for Tarren Mill, the main Horde stronghold in the region. Carry it east along the main road through the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where do i go","message destination"},it="place"},{q="Why is Varimathras involved in Hillsbrad's affairs?",a="Varimathras is Sylvanas Windrunner's chief lieutenant and dreadlord advisor. From Undercity's Royal Quarter, he oversees significant parts of Forsaken military and strategic planning, while High Executor Darthalia carries out his campaign orders on the regional front.",al={"varimathras hillsbrad","why varimathras"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after this message is received?",a="When Darthalia learns Hillsbrad is vulnerable, she authorizes aggressive offensive strikes. Horde champions are sent to dismantle the farms, militia, and infrastructure of Hillsbrad.",al={"what happens next","after time to strike"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deathstalker Lesh want this message delivered?",a="Deathstalker Lesh is stationed near the border on a covert reconnaissance mission to monitor the human settlement of Hillsbrad. Having observed that the town is vulnerable, she needs her coded assessment rushed immediately to High Executor Darthalia at Tarren Mill so the Forsaken leadership can initiate their coordinated offensive.",al={"why send message","deathstalker lesh motive","time to strike motive"},it="motive",add="ce3697ce"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken operatives, you help secure Lordaeron's eastern frontier against remnants of the human Alliance when you carry Lesh's dispatch.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you recognize the covert watch and coded messages used by the Deathstalkers, the Undercity's elite guild of assassins and scouts.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you are drawn deeper into the conflict between the Forsaken and the southern human settlements."},kw={"deathstalker lesh","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","scouting","tarren mill","varimathras"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-lesh","npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:silverpine","npc:varimathras","topic:horde"},m={start="Deathstalker Lesh",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="20",faction="Horde",id=494},src={"Time To Strike"}}
E["quest:496"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Suffering",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon pursues lethal brews against the living. He turns to travelers for animal reagents from the surrounding foothills.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon pursues lethal brews against the living.",sec={{t="A Toxic Enterprise",b="Tarren Mill is both a Forsaken stronghold in the Hillsbrad Foothills and a research station for the Royal Apothecary Society. Apothecary Lydon works there amid the green countryside, which he despises. He longs to see human settlements poisoned and conquered. To make his experimental Elixir of Suffering, he needs potent, virulent ingredients from nearby creatures.",sp=0},{t="Gathering Reagents",b="Apothecary Lydon sends hunters into the wilds around Tarren Mill for Gray Bear tongues and the rare ichor of Moss Creepers. Unholy alchemy refines these animal substances into the basis of a lethal mixture. He intends it to kill living trespassers across Hillsbrad.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Tarren Mill. He despises Hillsbrad's living landscape and works to make potent poisons against human populations.",al={"apothecary lydon","who gives elixir of suffering","lydon tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lydon need bear tongues and creeper ichor?",a="Apothecary Lydon needs Gray Bear tongues and Moss Creeper ichor as ingredients for his lethal brews. Their biological properties provide the alchemical base for his Elixir of Suffering.",al={"why bear tongues","what is creeper ichor for","elixir ingredients lore"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="After Apothecary Lydon receives the ingredients, he blends them into a prototype brew and demands that it be tested on living subjects for its lethal effect.",al={"next quest elixir of suffering","what happens after elixir of suffering"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the goal of the Royal Apothecary Society in Hillsbrad?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society, under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's command, seeks an alchemical plague that can wipe out humanity and the Scourge alike. Tarren Mill is a frontier outpost for gathering biological matter and testing prototypes against local Alliance forces.",al={"why are apothecaries in hillsbrad","forsaken poison goals","hillsbrad plague"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can the necessary creatures be found?",a="Gray Bears roam the central fields and forests of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Moss Creepers lurk in brush and wooded areas just outside Tarren Mill.",al={"where are gray bears","where are moss creepers","bear and spider locations"},gp=true},{q="Why is Lydon in such a bad mood?",a="Apothecary Lydon is disgusted by vitality, clean air, and thriving nature. He finds joy in death, decay, and distilling deadly toxins.",al={"why is lydon unhappy","lydon clean air"}},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want this done?",a="Apothecary Lydon despises the pristine, living landscape of Hillsbrad Foothills and longs to see the local humans wiped out. He is conducting rigorous research to develop lethal chemical agents for the Royal Apothecary Society, striving to craft a concoction potent enough to unleash widespread death across the region.",al={"why does lydon want this done","lydon motive","why make the elixir of suffering"},it="motive",add="7bd4a2da"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need you to gather the ingredients?",a="Lydon is consumed by the meticulous theoretical work of compounding and refining new killing agents at his laboratory in Tarren Mill. With his research demanding constant oversight, he lacks the time to personally scour the surrounding wilds hunting bears and tracking elusive creepers.",al={"why cant lydon gather them","why does lydon need me","why hire an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="f22d779c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken operative, you can help advance the Royal Apothecary Society's aim to create a devastating weapon for your people's survival against living humanity.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally, you may balk at the Forsaken's ruthless biological experiments. Tarren Mill's frontier against Southshore depends on their alchemical warfare."},kw={"apothecary lydon","creeper ichor","elixir of suffering","gray bear tongue","hillsbrad foothills","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="22",faction="Horde",id=496,ri={"Creeper Ichor","Gray Bear Tongue"}},src={"Elixir of Suffering (quest)"}}
E["quest:498"] = {t="quest",n="The Rescue",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Krusk seeks help after Syndicate bandits capture the orc scouts sent into Durnholde Keep. Thrall had sent the party to investigate the growing threat and retrieve an object from the keep.",h="In Tarren Mill, Krusk seeks help after Syndicate bandits capture the orc scouts sent into Durnholde Keep.",sec={{t="A Scout Mission Gone Wrong",b="Warchief Thrall sent a band of orc warriors to the Hillsbrad Foothills to investigate the growing Syndicate threat and retrieve an object from Durnholde Keep. Gol'dir led the scouts toward the fortress ruins, where the Syndicate's numbers overwhelmed them in an ambush. Krusk broke free and limped back across the river to Tarren Mill. Drull, Tog'thar, and Gol'dir were captured by the human bandits.",sp=0},{t="Chains in the Ruins",b="Durnholde carries bitter memories for the orcs. It once housed Aedelas Blackmoore's internment camps, where captive orcs were kept lethargic and forced into gladiatorial slavery. Now Drull and Tog'thar are bound in iron within the keep's cracked stone walls, another insult to the Horde. Free the two scouts from the Syndicate jailors who hold the keys to their shackles, then learn what became of their commander, Gol'dir.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why were orcs sent into Durnholde Keep in the first place?",a="Warchief Thrall sent Gol'dir and his scout cadre to investigate Syndicate bandits and retrieve an object from Durnholde Keep.",al={"why were they there","why durnholde","krusk mission"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the captives being rescued?",a="Drull and Tog'thar are orc scouts sent by the Horde under Gol'dir's command. Syndicate brigands overwhelmed them and bound them in ball and chain inside the ruins.",al={"who is drull","who is togthar","who are the hostages"},it="people"},{q="Where is the squad's leader, Gol'dir?",a="After Drull and Tog'thar are freed, Krusk discovers that the Syndicate separated Gol'dir from the main party and moved him to an unknown second location.",al={"where is goldir","find goldir","what happened to goldir"},sp=1},{q="Who is holding the scouts captive?",a="The Syndicate holds the scouts. This aristocratic criminal network operates from the ruins of Lordaeron and Alterac, and its jailors guard the captives inside Durnholde.",al={"who captured them","who are the jailors","who runs durnholde"},it="target"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead?",a="Freeing the scouts leads to a search for Gol'dir, with a mission to track down and infiltrate the Syndicate. The trail eventually reaches deeper into the Syndicate's affairs.",al={"what comes next","after the rescue","rescue chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Durnholde Keep hold special meaning to the Horde?",a="Durnholde was where Aedelas Blackmoore raised Thrall as a gladiator and commanded the Alliance internment camps after the Second War. Thrall later led a rebellion and laid waste to the keep.",al={"history of durnholde","why horde cares about durnholde"},it="history"},{q="Why does Krusk need the captives rescued?",a="Krusk was part of the very reconnaissance squad ambushed inside Durnholde Keep. While he managed to fight his way free and flee back to Tarren Mill, his comrades Drull and Tog'thar were captured alive. He fears the Syndicate plans to reduce them to slaves—an intolerable fate in the very fortress where orcs were once held in bondage—and cannot abandon his fellow warriors to captivity and torture.",al={"why rescue drull and tog'thar","krusk motive","why help krusk"},it="motive",add="95bc386b"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, seeing your warriors shackled in Durnholde cuts straight to the painful history of internment. Freeing them is personal.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you take part in an early effort to counter the Syndicate's expansion across the contested hills of Lordaeron.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you stand with fellow fighters by breaking them out of captivity from dishonorable human bandits."},kw={"drull","durnholde keep","gol'dir","hillsbrad","krusk","syndicate","tarren mill","tog'thar"},rel={"npc:krusk","subzone:durnholde-keep","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:syndicate","quest:549","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Krusk",level="22",faction="Horde",id=498},src={"The Rescue"}}
E["quest:499"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Suffering",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon prepares a poison for the Royal Apothecary Society. He wants to know how swiftly it kills before using it more widely.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon prepares a poison for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sec={{t="A Toxic Test",b="Apothecary Lydon works in Tarren Mill to make chemical weapons for the Dark Lady's ambitions. His blight is meant to destroy both the living humans of the Alliance and the undead horrors of the Scourge. Once he has the needed reagents, Lydon mixes them into a foul brew he calls the Elixir of Suffering. He is eager to see its power before the Society uses it on a wider scale.",sp=0},{t="The Fate of Umpi",b="Apothecary Lydon turns to the creature beside him for a trial. He asks you to give the fresh poison to his assistant, Umpi, a harmless toad sitting at his feet. One dose kills the amphibian on the spot, showing Lydon that his formula works as intended.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is an alchemist with the Royal Apothecary Society, stationed in Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He spends his days refining poisons and mixtures meant to wipe out the Forsaken's enemies.",al={"lydon","who is lydon","apothecary lydon tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is a toad beside Apothecary Lydon's work table in Tarren Mill. Lydon jokingly calls the toad his assistant.",al={"what is umpi","umpi the toad","who is the assistant"},it="target"},{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Suffering?",a="The Elixir of Suffering is an experimental chemical weapon meant to test toxins designed to eradicate living humans and the undead Scourge for Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"what does the elixir do","why make elixir of suffering"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens when you feed the potion to Umpi?",a="Lydon asks you to give Umpi a taste of the newly mixed elixir. The test reveals whether it has the intended effect.",al={"does umpi die","what happens to the toad"},sp=1},{q="Where does this test take place?",a="The test takes place at Lydon's brewing station in Tarren Mill, a Forsaken town in northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where is lydon located","where do i find umpi"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society test poisons on small animals?",a="Forsaken apothecaries test chemical compounds on small creatures and vermin to learn how quickly and lethally they act before trying them on larger targets or living captives.",al={"why test on toads","apothecary society animal testing"},it="history"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want to test the Elixir of Suffering?",a="Apothecary Lydon seeks to verify whether his newly brewed concoction achieves its intended lethal effect. The Royal Apothecary Society works tirelessly under Lady Sylvanas to develop plagues capable of annihilating both the Scourge and living humanity, and field tests like this confirm whether their dark formulas are progressing as planned.",al={"why test the elixir of suffering","apothecary lydon motive","why does lydon want this done"},it="motive",add="ac622650"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, testing lethal toxins is essential to Lady Sylvanas's decree to eradicate both the Scourge and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally visiting Tarren Mill, you see the Royal Apothecary Society's ruthless alchemical methods firsthand.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may find the casual poisoning of a harmless amphibian for Forsaken warfare deeply unsettling."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of suffering","hillsbrad foothills","poison","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","toad","umpi"},rel={"quest:496","npc:umpi","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:scourge"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Umpi",level="22",faction="Horde",id=499},src={"Elixir of Suffering (2)"}}
E["quest:501"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Pain",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon seeks mountain lion blood for a lethal brew. His work serves the Royal Apothecary Society’s drive to perfect the New Plague.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon seeks mountain lion blood for a lethal brew.",sec={{t="A Bitter Outlook in Tarren Mill",b="Apothecary Lydon finds little joy in Tarren Mill’s surroundings. From his window, the blooming meadows and brisk mountain air of Hillsbrad seem an offense to him. Like many in the Royal Apothecary Society, Lydon devotes himself to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the New Plague. The Society seeks to perfect this engineered scourge, meant to kill the living and bring retribution to its enemies.",sp=0},{t="Ingredients for Misery",b="Lydon seeks ingredients for his latest poisonous mixture among the animals prowling the foothills and the slopes toward the Alterac Mountains. He believes mountain lion blood has properties needed to make what he calls an Elixir of Pain. So he sends agents into the wilds to collect ten vials. The blood will support the Society’s continuing chemical trials along the contested southern front.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Elixir of Pain?",a="Apothecary Lydon, a Forsaken alchemist in Tarren Mill, gives the assignment. The settlement lies in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"quest giver elixir of pain","who starts elixir of pain","apothecary lydon quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need mountain lion blood?",a="Lydon believes mountain lion blood is needed to brew a lethal mixture. He hopes the elixir will advance the Royal Apothecary Society’s plague experiments against their living enemies.",al={"why mountain lion blood","lion blood purpose","what is the blood for"},it="item"},{q="Where can the mountain lions be found?",a="Mountain lions roam the open fields and rolling hills of Hillsbrad Foothills, and the higher bluffs leading toward the Alterac Mountains.",al={"where are mountain lions","mountain lion locations hillsbrad","lion blood farming"},gp=true},{q="What is the New Plague Lydon mentions?",a="The New Plague is a biological weapon the Forsaken’s Royal Apothecary Society is developing under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner’s orders. It is meant to eradicate both the Scourge and the living.",al={"what is the new plague","royal apothecary society plague","forsaken plague"},it="purpose"},{q="What comes next after completing this quest?",a="After you hand over ten vials of mountain lion blood, Apothecary Lydon begins testing his newly brewed elixir.",al={"elixir of pain next quest","follow up elixir of pain","what follows elixir of pain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Lydon despise Hillsbrad's scenery?",a="As an undead servant of the Dark Lady, Lydon resents Hillsbrad’s blooming plants, fresh air, and enduring life. He wants the Society’s toxic creations to smother the living world.",al={"why does lydon hate hillsbrad","why is lydon brooding","lydon window quote"},it="motive"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken traveler, you gather reagents for Apothecary Lydon in service of the Dark Lady and the Royal Apothecary Society as they claim their place in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally, you face the grim methods of Tarren Mill’s alchemists. You help gather wild beasts’ blood to strengthen Horde footholds against nearby human threats."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of pain","hillsbrad foothills","mountain lion blood","new plague","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:alterac","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="24",faction="Horde",id=501,ri={"Mountain Lion Blood"}},src={"Elixir of Pain (quest)"}}
E["quest:502"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Pain",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon prepares the Elixir of Pain for a field trial. Stanley, Farmer Ray’s dog in Hillsbrad Fields, is the chosen subject.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon prepares the Elixir of Pain for a field trial.",sec={{t="Apothecary Science",b="Apothecary Lydon works in Tarren Mill for the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. He gathers fresh blood from local wildlife and uses it to brew a volatile mixture called the Elixir of Pain. The Society seeks field evidence of how its experimental poisons and mutagens affect living bodies.",sp=0},{t="Testing on Stanley",b="Lydon sends his agents to the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields, away from the human defenders. Farmer Ray keeps a pet dog there named Stanley. With the draught poured into an open hand, an agent offers it to the unsuspecting dog as an ordinary treat.",sp=0},{t="Violent Mutation",b="The Elixir of Pain brings Stanley immediate agony and a violent change. The brew is a mutagen, not a simple lethal toxin: it warps the dog into a savage, enraged wolf. The beast attacks whatever is nearby, revealing the force of Lydon’s alchemical formula.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Elixir of Pain?",a="Apothecary Lydon brewed the Elixir of Pain for the Royal Apothecary Society’s effort to create biological weapons and potent mutagens for Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken.",al={"elixir of pain goal","why make elixir of pain","lydon elixir purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Stanley?",a="Stanley is Farmer Ray’s pet dog, living outside the large farmhouse at the northern end of Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"who is stanley","farmer ray dog","stanley the dog"},it="identity"},{q="What happens when you feed Stanley the elixir?",a="Lydon wants to see how Stanley likes his “treat.” The elixir’s effect becomes clear when Stanley eats it.",al={"stanley transformation","what does elixir do to dog","stanley wolf"},sp=1},{q="Where is Stanley located?",a="Stanley wanders outside the large house on the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields, southwest of Tarren Mill.",al={"find stanley","stanley location","where is farmer ray dog"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to test the elixir?",a="Apothecary Lydon, in the Forsaken settlement of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, asks you to test the elixir after you gather the needed reagents.",al={"elixir of pain questgiver","who gives elixir of pain","apothecary lydon quest"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="Why test the potion on a farmer's dog instead of humans?",a="A domestic pet in Hillsbrad Fields offers a quiet, accessible trial without immediately alerting the town militia or armed guards to the alchemical test.",al={"why test on dog","why stanley","why poison dog"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want the Elixir of Pain tested?",a="Apothecary Lydon believes this concoction could be the start of something monumental for Lady Sylvanas and the Royal Apothecary Society. Having mixed fresh mountain lion blood with his own vile additives, he needs practical field testing to prove whether his calculations hold true and see how living flesh reacts to the brew.",al={"why test the elixir of pain","apothecary lydon motive","why does lydon want this done"},it="motive",add="0d6659fd"},{q="Who are you sent to target with the elixir?",a="Your target is Stanley, a small pet dog belonging to Farmer Ray. Stanley resides on the northern homestead within the contested Hillsbrad Fields southwest of Tarren Mill. Instead of striking at the human farmers directly, Lydon has chosen this unsuspecting pet as an expendable subject to observe the elixir's volatile effects.",al={"who do i give the elixir to","elixir of pain target","who is the target"},it="target",add="fad857e3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see the Royal Apothecary Society’s ruthless approach: it seeks biological weapons for Forsaken survival, whatever the collateral damage.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally, you are drawn into the Forsaken’s grim chemical trials against the neighboring human farmlands of Hillsbrad.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see how little Forsaken alchemists care for the beasts caught in their trials when they feed an experimental brew to a farmer’s trusting dog."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of pain","farmer ray","hillsbrad fields","royal apothecary society","stanley","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:501","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Stanley",level="24",faction="Horde",id=502},src={"Elixir of Pain (2)"}}
E["quest:503"] = {t="quest",n="Gol'dir",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Krusk has found where Gol'dir is held. The documents point to a large Syndicate base up north, possibly in the Alterac Mountains, and Gol'dir has been captive too long.",h="In Tarren Mill, Krusk has found where Gol'dir is held.",sec={{t="A Trail to the North",b="In Tarren Mill, Krusk has studied the documents you brought back after Infiltration. They point to a large Syndicate base up north, possibly in the Alterac Mountains. Gol'dir has been held too long, and Krusk wants him freed.",sp=0},{t="The Inn at Strahnbrad",b="Gol'dir is held in the top room of the inn at Strahnbrad, where Syndicate fill the building. A Rusted Iron Key opens the lock. Jailor Borhuin carries it and may be in any building in town.",sp=0},{t="What Gol'dir Says",b="Gol'dir says the Warchief's orders sent him leading an expedition out of Durotar, but the plans went awry. The Syndicate kept him in Strahnbrad, forcing him to haul burdens and dig. He brushes aside his suffering; important information must reach whoever now leads the group.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is holding Gol'dir captive?",a="The Syndicate holds Gol'dir in a large base to the north.",al={"who captured goldir","who has goldir","goldir captors"}},{q="Where is Gol'dir imprisoned?",a="Gol'dir is imprisoned in the top room of the inn at Strahnbrad, which is packed with Syndicate.",al={"goldir location","where is goldir","find goldir"}},{q="How is Gol'dir's lock opened?",a="A Rusted Iron Key opens Gol'dir's lock. Jailor Borhuin carries it and may be in any building in Strahnbrad.",al={"rusted iron key","how to unlock goldir","goldir key"}},{q="What came before this step in the chain?",a="Before this step, you procured documents during Infiltration that point to where Gol'dir is held.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before goldir","chain before goldir"}}},kw={"alterac","borhuin","gol'dir","key","krusk","strahnbrad","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:533","quest:506","subzone:strahnbrad","zone:alterac","npc:krusk","topic:syndicate","zone:durotar"},m={start="Krusk",["end"]="Gol'dir",level="36",faction="Horde",id=503},src={"Gol'dir (quest)"}}
E["quest:506"] = {t="quest",n="Blackmoore's Legacy",z="hillsbrad",s="Gol'dir is free and carries news to Krusk in Tarren Mill. The Syndicate's leader, Aliden Perenolde, visited him and spoke of enslaving orcs who resist him. Perenolde also brought Elysa, a girl wearing the pendant the Warchief desires.",h="Gol'dir is free and carries news to Krusk in Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Visit to the Prisoner",b="Gol'dir has news for Krusk after a visit from Aliden Perenolde, head of the Syndicate. Perenolde called himself lord of the land and said he meant to enslave the orcs who resist him. His father and his mentor, the despised Blackmoore, had planned the same. Gol'dir sends you to carry this news to Krusk in Tarren Mill. He will follow after settling his own business where he is.",sp=0},{t="Elysa's Pendant",b="Perenolde also brought his mistress, a slight girl named Elysa. Around her neck hung the pendant the Warchief desires.",sp=0},{t="Krusk's Answer",b="Krusk answers Perenolde's threat with anger and vows the orcs will never submit. He sets resistance alongside the effort to recover the trinket the Warchief desires. Achieving either goal, he says, will bring the other within reach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="The orc Gol'dir gives this to you after you free him from the Syndicate.",al={"who gives blackmoore's legacy","quest giver","goldir"}},{q="Who should receive the news?",a="Bring the news to Krusk in Tarren Mill.",al={"where do i go","who to talk to","turn in location"}},{q="What did Aliden Perenolde reveal to Gol'dir?",a="Aliden Perenolde, head of the Syndicate, told Gol'dir he meant to enslave the orcs who resisted him, following plans made by his father and his mentor, the despised Blackmoore.",al={"perenolde plan","syndicate plans","what did perenolde say"}},{q="What else did Gol'dir notice during the visit?",a="Perenolde brought his mistress, a girl named Elysa, who wore the pendant the Warchief desires around her neck.",al={"elysa necklace","warchief pendant","mistress"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="You freed Gol'dir from the Syndicate.",al={"previous quest","what came before"}}},kw={"aliden","blackmoore","elysa","goldir","krusk","legacy","pendant","perenolde","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:krusk","quest:503","quest:507","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:syndicate"},m={start="Gol'dir",["end"]="Krusk",level="36",faction="Horde",id=506},src={"Blackmoore's Legacy"}}
E["quest:507"] = {t="quest",n="Lord Aliden Perenolde",z="hillsbrad",s="Krusk wants Lord Aliden Perenolde dead, and the Warchief's pendant recovered. Perenolde's manor lies north, on Lordamere Lake; his mistress Elysa knows about the pendant.",h="Krusk wants Lord Aliden Perenolde dead, and the Warchief's pendant recovered.",sec={{t="The Lord of the Syndicate",b="After Blackmoore's Legacy, Krusk says Perenolde must die and his foulness be ended. His manor lies north, on the shores of Lordamere Lake at Dandred's Fold. Once the deed is done, ask his mistress Elysa about Taretha's pendant, which the Warchief desires.",sp=0},{t="A Frightened Mistress",b="When you come to Elysa, she is terrified. She cries that she never meant your people harm, says Perenolde kept her against her will, and begs you to spare her.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to kill Lord Aliden Perenolde?",a="Krusk sends you after you finish Blackmoore's Legacy.",al={"who gives lord aliden perenolde quest","where do i get lord aliden perenolde"}},{q="Where is Lord Aliden Perenolde located?",a="Perenolde is upstairs in his manor at Dandred's Fold, on the shores of Lordamere Lake, a way to the north.",al={"where is perenolde","lord aliden perenolde location","dandred's fold manor"}},{q="Who is Lord Aliden Perenolde?",a="He leads the Syndicate.",al={"who is aliden perenolde","perenolde lore"}},{q="What item are you sent to retrieve after killing Perenolde?",a="You are sent to retrieve Taretha's pendant, which the Warchief desires. Ask Perenolde's mistress, Elysa, about it.",al={"what pendant does thrall want","what does perenolde have"}},{q="What comes after this quest?",a="Taretha's Gift comes next in the chain.",al={"what is after lord aliden perenolde","next quest after perenolde"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","dandred's fold","elysa","krusk","lord aliden perenolde","lordamere lake","syndicate","taretha's pendant"},rel={"quest:506","quest:508","npc:krusk","subzone:dandred-s-fold","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Krusk",["end"]="Elysa",level="42",faction="Horde",id=507},src={"Lord Aliden Perenolde (quest)"}}
E["quest:508"] = {t="quest",n="Taretha's Gift",z="hillsbrad",s="After the step with Lord Aliden Perenolde, Elysa gives up Taretha's pendant and asks only to be left in peace. You carry it back to Krusk in Tarren Mill.",h="After the step with Lord Aliden Perenolde, Elysa gives up Taretha's pendant and asks only to be left in peace.",sec={{t="The Pendant",b="Elysa has no wish to hold on to any memory of Lord Aliden Perenolde. You may take the pendant, Elysa says, and begs only that you then go in peace. It once belonged to Taretha Foxton, a childhood friend of Thrall's. You are to bring it to Krusk in Tarren Mill, so that it returns to the orcs.",sp=0},{t="Krusk's Verdict",b="Krusk finds it odd that the Warchief would go to such lengths for a trinket. Krusk does not pretend to understand Thrall, but will follow his orders all the same, and praises your work, sure that Thrall will be pleased to hear it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who hands over Taretha's necklace?",a="Elysa gives it up without argument, wanting no memory of Lord Aliden Perenolde and asking only to be left in peace.",al={"who gives the pendant","where do you get taretha's necklace","who starts taretha's gift"}},{q="To whom must the necklace be returned?",a="Krusk, in Tarren Mill.",al={"who turns in taretha's gift","where do i bring the pendant","krusk location"}},{q="Whose pendant was it?",a="It belonged to Taretha Foxton, Thrall's childhood friend, and bringing it back returns a keepsake of hers to the orcs.",al={"why does thrall want the pendant","taretha foxton necklace significance","what is taretha's gift"}},{q="What comes before this in the chain?",a="The step involving Lord Aliden Perenolde. This is the last part of the chain.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite for taretha's gift"}}},kw={"aliden perenolde","elysa","hillsbrad foothills","krusk","taretha's gift","taretha's necklace","tarren mill","thrall"},rel={"quest:507","npc:krusk","npc:thrall","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","topic:horde"},m={start="Elysa",["end"]="Krusk",level="40",faction="Horde",id=508},src={"Taretha's Gift"}}
E["quest:509"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad Foothills, you gather toxic fungi from an overrun farmstead for Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. The Mudsnout Blossoms will fuel the Royal Apothecary Society’s experiments, as Lady Sylvanas seeks a plague against the living and the Scourge.",h="In Hillsbrad Foothills, you gather toxic fungi from an overrun farmstead for Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Plague in the Making",b="The Scourge ravages the north, while the Alliance clings to towns like Southshore. In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon works under the Dark Lady’s command to develop a plague against both. He finds alchemy tedious, yet gathers potent organic toxins from the countryside to brew elixirs meant to hasten the destruction of Sylvanas’s enemies.",sp=0},{t="The Fields of Nethander Stead",b="Nethander Stead lies south of Tarren Mill and east of the river. The abandoned human farmstead is overrun by vicious Mudsnout gnolls. Mudsnout Blossoms, foul-smelling mushrooms, grow among its filth and neglected soil. Their concentrated organic poisons are prized by the Royal Apothecary Society. You can cut through the gnoll packs or weave quietly past their ramshackle camps to gather them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a Royal Apothecary Society alchemist stationed at Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills. He serves Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, refining lethal mixtures and developing a new plague to defeat the living and the Scourge.",al={"lydon","who is lydon","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="What are Mudsnout Blossoms used for?",a="Mudsnout Blossoms are foul-smelling mushrooms from Nethander Stead. Lydon uses their potent natural toxins to brew the Elixir of Agony, part of the Forsaken’s chemical and biological warfare research.",al={"mudsnout blossoms","what are the mushrooms for","blossom use"},it="item"},{q="Where is Nethander Stead located?",a="Nethander Stead is an overgrown farmstead south of Tarren Mill and east of the major river that runs past Southshore. Aggressive Mudsnout gnolls have claimed the farm and guard the fields where the mushrooms grow.",al={"nethander stead location","where is nethander stead","where are the gnolls"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to create a new plague?",a="Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken seek a weapon to eliminate both the Scourge and the Alliance’s hostile living races. The Royal Apothecary Society works to secure the Forsaken’s sovereignty and survival in Lordaeron with a plague of their own.",al={"why make a plague","forsaken plague reason","sylvanas plague"},it="history"},{q="Why does Lydon complain about having to brew these elixirs?",a="Lydon is weary and morbid; he observes that humans and the Scourge already slaughter one another without help. Still, he obeys Lady Sylvanas’s wish to hasten their mutual destruction and continues brewing deadly mixtures.",al={"lydon attitude","why is lydon cynical"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after collecting the blossoms?",a="After Lydon receives the Mudsnout Blossoms, he brews the toxic mixture and soon needs more ingredients and field testing to make the elixir as lethal as possible.",al={"next quest","what follows elixir of agony"},it="next_step"},{q="Who guards the Mudsnout Blossoms at Nethander Stead?",a="The fields of Nethander Stead have been overrun by Mudsnout gnolls. These filthy creatures cultivate or fiercely guard the pungent fungi growing across the farmstead, making any gathering run a hazardous venture into their claimed territory.",al={"what guards mudsnout blossoms","nethander stead enemies","mudsnout gnolls"},it="target",add="744a331d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help the Royal Apothecary Society defend Lordaeron from humanity and the Lich King.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist or forager, you may recognize the Mudsnout Blossom as a rare, extraordinarily toxic fungus that grows in unworked soil tainted by gnoll habitation.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde emissary in Tarren Mill, you assist your Forsaken allies while facing their unsettling chemical experiments."},kw={"apothecary lydon","elixir of agony","hillsbrad","mudsnout blossom","nethander stead","new plague","royal apothecary society","tarren mill"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:nethander-stead","quest:367","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","subzone:southshore","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="28",faction="Horde",id=509,ri={"Mudsnout Blossom"}},src={"Elixir of Agony"}}
E["quest:517"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="hillsbrad",s="Apothecary Lydon’s work in Tarren Mill reaches a deadly test. His Elixir of Agony is ready, and he sends Horde champions to Dun Garok for a keg of Shindigger Stout.",h="Apothecary Lydon’s work in Tarren Mill reaches a deadly test.",sec={{t="A Bitter Brew",b="Apothecary Lydon serves the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas in Tarren Mill. He has gathered lethal ingredients from across Hillsbrad and finished a new concoction. Frogs and stray dogs are no test for its strength. Lydon wants to see what it does to living adversaries.",sp=0},{t="Infiltrating Dun Garok",b="Lydon needs a quiet way to carry his experiment. South of Hillsbrad, Ironforge dwarves hold the fortified stronghold of Dun Garok. He sends Horde agents into its underground barracks and mess halls to slip past dwarven rifles and axes and steal a keg of Shindigger Stout.",sp=0},{t="A Recipe for Disaster",b="Apothecary Lydon plans to mix his toxin into the dwarves’ favorite brew. The stolen keg can carry the elixir to an unwitting target, disguised as festive refreshment. A beloved dwarven stout becomes a vessel for agony.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a Forsaken alchemist stationed in Tarren Mill. He represents the Royal Apothecary Society and experiments with deadly plagues and elixirs for the Banshee Queen, Lady Sylvanas.",al={"lydon","who gives this quest","apothecary lydon lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lydon need a keg of Shindigger Stout?",a="Lydon wants to test his finished Elixir of Agony on living targets. Mixing it into a keg of popular dwarven ale gives him a covert way to poison his victims.",al={"why dwarven beer","why shindigger stout","purpose of the keg"},it="item"},{q="Where is Dun Garok located?",a="Dun Garok lies in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen man the fortified redoubt and guard their northern interests.",al={"where is dun garok","dun garok location","where do i find the keg"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Umpi?",a="Umpi is Apothecary Lydon’s assistant in Tarren Mill. Lydon says that opening jars of formaldehyde around the lab makes Umpi visibly nervous.",al={"umpi","who is umpi","lydon assistant"},it="allies"},{q="What is the ultimate goal of the Elixir of Agony?",a="The Elixir of Agony is an experimental poison the Royal Apothecary Society made to eradicate the living. It serves the Forsaken campaign to secure Lordaeron from human and dwarven footholds.",al={"what does elixir of agony do","plague purpose","forsaken poison goal"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next after retrieving the keg?",a="With the keg in hand, Lydon mixes the toxic elixir into the Shindigger Stout and sends you to deliver the tainted ale to an unsuspecting test subject.",al={"next quest","what after dun garok","elixir part 5"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are you sent against at Dun Garok?",a="You are sent to infiltrate Dun Garok, a heavily fortified dwarf outpost in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. The Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen stationed there belong to the Alliance, defending dwarven interests in the region and posing an ongoing threat to the Forsaken presence in Tarren Mill.",al={"dun garok dwarves","who is at dun garok","who guards the stout"},it="target",add="9a9bdb3b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see each batch Lydon perfects bring the Forsaken closer to using death against the living enemies encroaching on Lordaeron.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a Dwarf, you know that turning traditional dwarven ale into a vessel for chemical slaughter insults Ironforge craftsmanship.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help undermine the Alliance presence at Dun Garok, where Tarren Mill holds a delicate foothold against relentless southern threats.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you slip through Dun Garok’s crowded mess halls unseen, stealing under the mountaineers’ noses."},kw={"apothecary lydon","dun garok","dwarves","elixir of agony","hillsbrad","shindigger stout","tarren mill","umpi"},rel={"quest:509","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dun-garok","zone:hillsbrad","npc:umpi","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="30",faction="Horde",id=517,ri={"Keg of Shindigger Stout"}},src={"Elixir of Agony (4)"}}
E["quest:518"] = {t="quest",n="The Crown of Will",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Melisara prepares to weaken Mug'Thol's ogres before striking at their hold in the Ruins of Alterac. She sends you after the Crushridge maulers.",h="In Tarren Mill, Melisara prepares to weaken Mug'Thol's ogres before striking at their hold in the Ruins of...",sec={{t="Softening the Crushridge",b="Mug'Thol and the Crushridge ogres hold the Ruins of Alterac. Melisara sees little chance of punishing Mug'Thol while so many ogres remain around him. First, their numbers must fall; only then can the next move begin. You are sent to hunt the Crushridge maulers.",sp=0},{t="No Rest Yet",b="Melisara sees ogre blood staining the snow after the maulers fall. The fighting will continue until the Crushridge are broken in spirit as well as in number.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this part of The Crown of Will?",a="Melisara gives you this work in Tarren Mill, and she is the one you return to.",al={"who gives the crown of will","melisara quest giver","crown of will 2 quest giver"}},{q="Where are the Crushridge ogres located?",a="Mug'Thol and his ogres have overrun the Ruins of Alterac, where the Crushridge now hold their ground.",al={"crushridge maulers location","where are crushridge ogres","ruins of alterac ogres"}},{q="Why is Melisara targeting the maulers first?",a="Melisara says Mug'Thol will be hard to punish while his ogres remain so numerous. Their numbers must be thinned before her plan can go further.",al={"why kill crushridge maulers","why thin the ogres"}}},kw={"crushridge maulers","melisara","mug'thol","ruins of alterac","sharlindra","tarren mill","the crown of will"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Melisara",["end"]="Melisara",level="39",faction="Horde",id=518},src={"The Crown of Will (2)"}}
E["quest:519"] = {t="quest",n="The Crown of Will",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Melisara seeks the heads of three ogres before Mug'Thol.",h="In Tarren Mill, Melisara seeks the heads of three ogres before Mug'Thol.",sec={{t="Sniping at the Leadership",b="Melisara names Targ, Muckrake and Glommus as Mug'Thol's loyal lieutenants, though she wonders what could make an ogre loyal. You are to kill all three and bring their heads to Tarren Mill. Then only Mug'Thol's head, crown and all, remains to be taken.",sp=0},{t="What Becomes of the Heads",b="Melisara remarks on the ogres' foul smell. When Mug'Thol's head arrives, all four will be set on pikes over Alterac as a warning to anyone who crosses the Dark Lady.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this part of The Crown of Will?",a="Melisara gives you this part in Tarren Mill, where you bring the heads to her.",al={"who starts the crown of will","melisara location","where to turn in the crown of will"}},{q="Who are Targ, Muckrake, and Glommus?",a="Targ, Muckrake and Glommus are Mug'Thol's loyal lieutenants. Melisara wants their heads.",al={"mugthol lieutenants","who are the ogre lieutenants","targ muckrake glommus"}},{q="What came before this part?",a="Before this part, the ogres' numbers were thinned in the second part of The Crown of Will.",al={"crown of will chain","what quest comes before this","previous crown of will"}}},kw={"alterac","crown of will","glommus","hillsbrad","melisara","muckrake","mug'thol","targ","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Melisara",["end"]="Melisara",level="41",faction="Horde",id=519},src={"The Crown of Will (3)"}}
E["quest:520"] = {t="quest",n="The Crown of Will",z="hillsbrad",s="With Mug'Thol's lieutenants dead, Melisara in Tarren Mill sends you after him. Bring back his head and the Crown of Will, and the Crushridge resistance will be over.",h="With Mug'Thol's lieutenants dead, Melisara in Tarren Mill sends you after him.",sec={{t="The Last Head",b="Only Mug'Thol remains. Melisara expects him to resist giving up the Crown of Will. After his lieutenants fell, he likely expects you. Find him, kill him, and bring his head and the Crown back to Tarren Mill.",sp=0},{t="Melisara's Reply",b="Melisara is pleased with your work. Mug'Thol's head will adorn the highest peak of the Ruins of Alterac, and the Deathguard will crush what remains of the Crushridge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to kill Mug'Thol?",a="Melisara in Tarren Mill sends you to kill Mug'Thol, and you bring his head back to her.",al={"crown of will quest giver","who gives the crown of will","melisara quest"}},{q="What does Melisara require from Mug'Thol?",a="Melisara requires Mug'Thol's head and the Crown of Will.",al={"mugthol objectives","what do i get from mugthol","mug'thol items"}},{q="Why does Melisara think Mug'Thol expects trouble?",a="With his lieutenants dead, Melisara suspects Mug'Thol expects you and will resist giving up the Crown.",al={"why is mugthol ready","mugthol expecting fight","mug'thol alerted"}},{q="Where does this fall in The Crown of Will?",a="This comes after the third part, in which Mug'Thol's lieutenants were hunted, and is followed by a fifth part.",al={"crown of will chain","what quest comes before crown of will 4","crown of will progression"}}},kw={"alterac","crown of will","crushridge","hillsbrad foothills","melisara","mug'thol","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Melisara",["end"]="Melisara",level="43",faction="Horde",id=520},src={"The Crown of Will (4)"}}
E["quest:521"] = {t="quest",n="The Crown of Will",z="hillsbrad",s="Only one step remains: the Crown is bound for Sharlindra in the Undercity, who will see that it reaches Lady Sylvanas.",h="Only one step remains: the Crown is bound for Sharlindra in the Undercity, who will see that it reaches Lady...",sec={{t="To the Undercity",b="Melisara sends you to take the Crown to Sharlindra in the Undercity, where she will pass it on to Lady Sylvanas. She warns you not to use it for your own purposes. Mug'Thol's fate is warning enough.",sp=0},{t="Sharlindra's Reaction",b="Sharlindra recognizes the Crown as the relic the ogre used to escape the Dark Lady's will. She finds it odd that so plain an object held such power, and that it fell into such clumsy hands. Sharlindra will take it to Lady Sylvanas and tell her what you did.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who receives the Crown of Will in the Undercity?",a="Sharlindra receives the Crown in the Undercity. Melisara says she will see that Lady Sylvanas gets it.",al={"who gets crown of will","where do i take the crown","sharlindra turn in"}},{q="Why does Melisara warn against using the crown?",a="Melisara warns you not to use the Crown for your own ends. She points to Mug'Thol's fate as warning enough.",al={"can i equip the crown","why not use crown of will","mugthol fate warning"}},{q="Who sends you with the crown?",a="Melisara sends you with the Crown as the fifth and final part, after the fourth.",al={"crown of will final part","who gives crown of will 5"}}},kw={"crown of will","hillsbrad","melisara","mugthol","sharlindra","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Melisara",["end"]="Sharlindra",level="43",faction="Horde",id=521},src={"The Crown of Will (5)"}}
E["quest:524"] = {t="quest",n="Elixir of Agony",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon prepares a deadly poison for a cruel test. He plans to disguise it as stolen dwarven ale and use it on human prisoners.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon prepares a deadly poison for a cruel test.",sec={{t="A Deadly Vintage",b="Apothecary Lydon gathers foul ingredients across the Hillsbrad Foothills and steals dwarven ale from Dun Garok. The Royal Apothecary Society has charged him with making a deadly brew called Elixir of Agony. Once mixed, the poison waits inside a keg that appears to hold ordinary mountain stout.",sp=0},{t="Unfortunate Guests",b="Deathguards in Tarren Mill recently seized local human farmers, suspecting that a military strategist from Stormwind was hiding among them. Word came that the strategist had died in the Plaguelands. High Executor Darthalia then judged the surviving farmers useless for military intelligence and handed them to Lydon for his chemical trials.",sp=1},{t="Testing the Brew",b="Lydon’s tainted keg is carried upstairs to the holding room and set on a dusty rug before the thirsty captives. Unaware of the danger, the farmers hurry to drink. The poison takes hold within moments, and they collapse dead, showing how lethal the brew is.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why were the human farmers captured in the first place?",a="Deathguards captured the farmers because they suspected a military strategist from the Kingdom of Stormwind was hiding among them. After the strategist died in the Plaguelands, High Executor Darthalia no longer considered the captives useful for intelligence.",al={"why prisoners","why farmers locked up","tarren mill prisoners"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon belongs to the Forsaken’s Royal Apothecary Society and works in Tarren Mill. He develops and tests lethal blights and poisons meant to eradicate the living, often on captured locals.",al={"apothecary lydon lore","who is lydon","lydon tarren mill"},it="identity"},{q="Where did the ale inside the keg come from?",a="The ale came from the dwarves of Dun Garok, a stout mountain stronghold in the southern Hillsbrad Foothills. Lydon tainted the stolen keg with his reagents so its deadly poison would seem to be ordinary dwarven brew.",al={"source of the ale","dun garok ale","keg origin"},it="item"},{q="What happens when you deliver the tainted keg?",a="Lydon asks you to place the tainted keg on the rug in the prisoners’ room for his experiment.",al={"what happens to the farmers","farmers drink keg","plagued brew result"}},{q="Who authorized using the prisoners as test subjects?",a="High Executor Darthalia, commander of the Forsaken forces in Tarren Mill, gave the surviving prisoners to Apothecary Lydon after they no longer had military value.",al={"who let lydon test on farmers","darthalia role","darthalia prisoners"},sp=1,it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to achieve here?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society seeks to make a deadly blight that can destroy both the Scourge and the living. Field trials such as Elixir of Agony test new ways to deliver chemicals and measure their effects on human bodies.",al={"apothecary goals hillsbrad","why make elixir of agony","forsaken blight testing"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want to poison the prisoners?",a="Apothecary Lydon needs live human subjects to verify the lethal efficacy of his newly completed Elixir of Agony. The Royal Apothecary Society constantly strives to refine deadly plagues and toxins to eradicate humanity and the Scourge alike. Now that High Executor Darthalia no longer needs the captured farmers for interrogation, Lydon views them as convenient, expendable test subjects to confirm that his brew functions as intended before reporting his success.",al={"why poison the farmers","lydon motive","why test the elixir of agony","why does lydon want this done"},it="motive",add="34bdf792"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the Royal Apothecary Society’s poisons are vital to survival. They seek to secure the Hillsbrad Foothills from a human resurgence by any means.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see the Forsaken’s cold ruthlessness in the slaughter of helpless Lordaeron farmers, their former kin.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you witness the harsher side of Forsaken operations in Tarren Mill, where they test the limits of what others are willing to accept."},kw={"apothecary lydon","captured farmers","dun garok","elixir of agony","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad","tainted keg","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:509","npc:high-executor-darthalia","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:dun-garok","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Dusty Rug",level="30",faction="Horde",id=524},src={"Elixir of Agony (5)"}}
E["quest:527"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad, the Forsaken strike at the farms that feed the human town. High Executor Darthalia orders the attack from Tarren Mill under Varimathras's command.",h="In Hillsbrad, the Forsaken strike at the farms that feed the human town.",sec={{t="Starving the Resistance",b="High Executor Darthalia directs the Forsaken campaign from Tarren Mill. Varimathras in the Undercity has ordered her to break the human resistance in Hillsbrad Foothills. Before attacking the defended town, Darthalia targets its northern fields. The farms feed the town, and disrupting them cuts provisions to the human militia while bringing disorder to the homesteads.",sp=0},{t="A Delaying Action",b="The Forsaken press the human defenders while the Royal Apothecary Society works on a plague meant to destroy the living and the Scourge. Darthalia sees the fighting as a way to hold the humans down until the plague is ready. Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz are among the landowners killed in these early attacks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking simple farmers?",a="The farmers and farmhands in Hillsbrad Fields help supply the town of Hillsbrad. Killing landowners such as Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz and disrupting the farms cuts food to the human garrison and weakens its defenses before a direct assault.",al={"why kill farmers","hillsbrad farm targets","why attack farms"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders this attack?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander at Tarren Mill, orders the attack. She answers to Varimathras and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who gives quest","darthalia orders","who is darthalia"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society's role in this campaign?",a="Darthalia says the fighting holds back the living while Forsaken apothecaries prepare a plague to destroy their enemies.",al={"why the new plague","apothecaries hillsbrad","forsaken plague plan"},it="ties"},{q="Where are Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz located?",a="Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz oversee the northern Hillsbrad Fields. Farmer Ray is near the large farmhouse or in the garden just east of it. Farmer Getz is at the barn, the secondary house, or the surrounding fields.",al={"find farmer ray","find farmer getz","ray and getz location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after completing this raid?",a="After you return victorious to Darthalia, the assault moves to the southern fields and Hillsbrad. Other operations also open, including the gathering of grim trophies in Souvenirs of Death.",al={"battle of hillsbrad follow up","what comes next","chain progression"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Darthalia threaten her soldiers?",a="Darthalia demands strict discipline and ruthlessness. She treats hesitation or levity about the war with the Alliance as treason, punishable by immediate execution.",al={"darthalia dialogue","darthalia beheading threat"}},{q="Who are you sent against in Hillsbrad Fields?",a="You are dispatched against the human farmers and farmhands working the northern plots of Hillsbrad Fields, specifically targeting landowners Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz. These residents form the backbone of the region's agricultural infrastructure, cultivating crops and livestock that sustain the nearby human settlement of Hillsbrad and the Alliance forces holding the area.",al={"battle of hillsbrad targets","who are we attacking in hillsbrad","who are farmer ray and getz"},it="target",add="a66392fb"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you fight to reclaim Lordaeron by wiping out the living who claim your homeland as stolen ground.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you see the brutality of Sylvanas's war against the Alliance in the northern campaign from Tarren Mill, even as Thrall preaches honor.",["faction:Alliance"]="As Alliance, you face the danger to Lordaeron's remaining human enclaves in the slaughter of the northern homesteaders."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","farmer getz","farmer ray","hillsbrad fields","new plague","tarren mill","varimathras"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","npc:varimathras","quest:546","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="24",faction="Horde",id=527},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (quest)"}}
E["quest:528"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad, Forsaken forces press their assault south. After strikes on the northern farms, Horde operatives hunt the peasants fleeing to the orchards.",h="In Hillsbrad, Forsaken forces press their assault south.",sec={{t="Sowing Terror in the Fields",b="The attack on Hillsbrad's human farms drives laborers south into the fields. After the northern farms are struck, many flee to the orchards and pastures of Hillsbrad Fields, hoping to escape the advancing undead. High Executor Darthalia sees their flight as a chance to break the township's remaining labor force and morale.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Lady's Advance",b="From Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia orders Horde forces to hunt the displaced laborers in the fields. The peasants have no protection, and their deaths choke Hillsbrad's food supply and weaken civilian resolve. For Darthalia and the Forsaken, each human killed tightens their hold over the surviving township and helps keep Lordaeron in Forsaken hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Forsaken targeting simple peasants?",a="The Forsaken target the peasants to destroy the labor force that feeds Hillsbrad. By killing those hiding in the southern orchards, High Executor Darthalia deepens the town's panic and hunger, making conquest easier.",al={"why kill peasants","why target farmers","darthalia peasant plan"},it="motive"},{q="Who orders this assault?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander at Tarren Mill, orders the assault on local human settlements in the name of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who gives battle of hillsbrad 2","quest giver battle of hillsbrad","darthalia orders"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where did these peasants flee from?",a="The peasants fled the northern farms after earlier Horde strikes. In panic, they sought refuge among the trees and pastures of southern Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"where are peasants coming from","northern farms hillsbrad"},it="origin"},{q="Where can the fleeing peasants be found?",a="The peasants are scattered through the southern orchards and pastures of Hillsbrad Fields, just south of the main road through the foothills.",al={"hillsbrad peasant location","where are hillsbrad peasants"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes after killing the peasants?",a="After the laborers are cleared from the southern fields, High Executor Darthalia turns the campaign toward Blacksmith Verringtan and the smithy arming Hillsbrad's defenders. The fighting moves closer to the town center.",al={"what is next after peasants","battle of hillsbrad next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde fighting so ruthlessly here?",a="The human town of Hillsbrad is one of the last Alliance strongholds in Lordaeron. The Forsaken claim the region as their sovereign territory and seek to drive out or kill Alliance enclaves that threaten their southern border.",al={"why horde attacking hillsbrad","forsaken vs hillsbrad war"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the Hillsbrad Peasants?",a="They are the human commoners of Hillsbrad who fled the initial assault on the northern farms. Terrified by the advancing Forsaken, they scattered south into the orchards of the Hillsbrad Fields hoping to hide from the slaughter, but Darthalia's scouts quickly uncovered their refuge.",al={"hillsbrad peasants","who are the peasants","peasants in orchards"},it="target",add="cca64c76"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, killing the living laborers is practical and absolute. It denies the Alliance sustenance and strengthens the Dark Lady's rule over southern Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill is the Horde's stronghold in the foothills. Breaking Hillsbrad keeps Horde lines of communication and supply secure against Alliance incursions.",["faction:Alliance"]="The killing of unarmed refugees in the southern orchards shows the Forsaken's ruthless war against Lordaeron's remaining living subjects."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","dark lady","darthalia","deathstalkers","forsaken","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad peasants","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="25",faction="Horde",id=528},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (2)"}}
E["quest:529"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="In the Hillsbrad Foothills, the Forsaken move against the humans resisting their advance. High Executor Darthalia orders the smithy in Hillsbrad Fields destroyed, hoping to cut off the weapons arming the local people.",h="In the Hillsbrad Foothills, the Forsaken move against the humans resisting their advance.",sec={{t="Breaking the Anvil",b="The Forsaken meet fiercer resistance in the Hillsbrad Foothills than High Executor Darthalia expected. Rural humans refuse to scatter or yield to the Deathstalkers and soldiers sent from Tarren Mill. The Forsaken learn that the peasantry are not fighting with pitchforks and scythes alone. In the fields, they are being armed for war.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Supply Line",b="At the southwest edge of Hillsbrad Fields, Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices forge blades and armor for the militia from raw ore. Darthalia sends an operative to kill Verringtan, butcher his apprentices, and seize their stockpiled iron shipment. She aims to weaken the settlement's defense and use the metal in the eventual assault on Southshore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia target the blacksmith specifically?",a="The human townsfolk and farmers are resisting the Forsaken advance with arms. Darthalia learns that Blacksmith Verringtan and his apprentices are forging weapons for the militia, arming the peasants.",al={"why kill verringtan","blacksmith objective","verringtan quest"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the smithy located?",a="The smithy is on the southwestern side of Hillsbrad Fields, where apprentices work amid guards and local patrols.",al={"verringtan location","where is the blacksmith","hillsbrad smithy"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the shipment of iron used for?",a="Darthalia takes the iron to supply the Forsaken war effort. She plans to forge weapons and supplies for the assault on Southshore.",al={"what happens to the iron","iron shipment lore"},it="item"},{q="How does this fit into the broader Battle of Hillsbrad campaign?",a="The strike is the third stage in Darthalia's effort to dismantle the human presence in the foothills. After culling rural laborers and farmers, she turns to their leadership, logistics, and production.",al={"battle of hillsbrad chain","darthalia campaign"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the people in Hillsbrad Fields part of the Alliance military?",a="The people in Hillsbrad Fields are mainly local farmers, laborers, and townsfolk, not Alliance soldiers. Though aligned with Southshore and the Alliance, they have formed an ad hoc militia to defend their homes from the Forsaken.",al={"are hillsbrad farmers alliance","hillsbrad militia"},it="people"},{q="Who orders this strike?",a="High Executor Darthalia orders the strike. She commands Forsaken operations from Tarren Mill.",al={"quest giver","who is darthalia"},it="leader"},{q="Who is Blacksmith Verringtan?",a="Blacksmith Verringtan is the local metalworker stationed at the smithy on the southwest edge of the Hillsbrad Fields. Alongside his apprentices, he manufactures weapons and tools for the local human populace, fueling their fierce resistance against the Forsaken push into the foothills.",al={"who is verringtan","blacksmith verringtan","hillsbrad blacksmith"},it="target",add="c3d79e95"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know breaking the human smithy can help secure Lordaeron's southern borders and stockpile metal for your struggling war effort.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Verringtan's slaughter and the theft of the settlement's iron leave Southshore's outlying farms without their only means of self-defense.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know Verringtan's forge fueled local resistance. An anvil can threaten an invading army as much as a regiment of footmen."},kw={"apprentice blacksmith","battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad fields","shipment of iron","tarren mill","verringtan"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="26",faction="Horde",id=529,ri={"Shipment of Iron"}},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (3)"}}
E["quest:532"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="Forsaken forces strike Hillsbrad town, aiming to break its human rule. High Executor Darthalia directs the assault from Tarren Mill.",h="Forsaken forces strike Hillsbrad town, aiming to break its human rule.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Town Council",b="Hillsbrad's human defenders cling to their remaining authority despite heavy losses in the fields and patrols. High Executor Darthalia knows that peasants and militia rally behind the town's leaders. She sends Forsaken operatives into the Town Hall to kill Magistrate Burnside and five councilmen, cutting off the town's command.",sp=0},{t="Erasing the Civic Record",b="Darthalia aims to break Hillsbrad's civic life as well as its leadership. She orders operatives to burn the Hillsbrad Proclamation, a political document tied to the settlement's charter and pride. They also seize the town registry, taking official records and citizen rolls from surviving Alliance loyalists. The registry gives Undercity's intelligence a detailed view of the local people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders this strike?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander at Tarren Mill, directs the assault as part of her campaign against Alliance settlements in the foothills.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver battle of hillsbrad","darthalia hillsbrad"},it="in_charge"},{q="Who is Magistrate Burnside?",a="Magistrate Burnside leads Hillsbrad's human government. He is in the Town Hall with his councilors and uses arcane magic to defend the town's remaining authority.",al={"magistrate burnside","who is burnside","hillsbrad leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Hillsbrad Proclamation?",a="The Hillsbrad Proclamation is a political charter kept in the Town Hall. It embodies the town's law and civic pride, so its destruction strikes at local morale.",al={"what is the proclamation","hillsbrad proclamation lore","destroy proclamation"}},{q="Why does Darthalia want the town registry?",a="The town registry holds a census and civic records for Hillsbrad's people. Taking it deprives surviving humans of their records and gives the Forsaken information about who remains nearby.",al={"why steal registry","hillsbrad town registry","what does registry do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does this fight take place?",a="The targets are in and around Hillsbrad's large Town Hall, in the human settlement in the southern foothills between Tarren Mill and Southshore.",al={"where is magistrate burnside","hillsbrad town hall location","where are councilmen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role do the councilmen play?",a="The Hillsbrad Councilmen help Magistrate Burnside govern the town. They are spellcasters who defend the Town Hall and its surrounding grounds.",al={"hillsbrad councilmen","who are councilmen"},it="threat"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want this done?",a="The town of Hillsbrad is in disarray after repeated Forsaken strikes, but its human defenders refuse to surrender so long as their local leadership holds. High Executor Darthalia intends to break their spirit entirely and wipe them from the foothills forever. By assassinating Magistrate Burnside and the council, destroying their revered Hillsbrad Proclamation, and seizing their records, she aims to shatter the remaining structure keeping Hillsbrad Fields organized.",al={"why attack hillsbrad leadership","darthalia motive battle of hillsbrad","why does darthalia want burnside dead"},it="motive",add="1e1aeb4f"},{q="Who are you sent against in Hillsbrad?",a="You are sent to assassinate Magistrate Burnside and five of his councilmen within the Hillsbrad town hall. Despite severe casualties across the fields and orchards, Burnside and his council continue to organize the local defense and rally the human populace against Tarren Mill. Striking down their magistrate and political council strips the town of its governing authority.",al={"who are we killing in hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad target","who is magistrate burnside and council"},it="target",add="acee9bfa"},{q="What is the Hillsbrad Town Registry for?",a="The Hillsbrad Town Registry is the official civic record documenting the local populace and property of Hillsbrad. Seizing it deprives the surviving humans of their administrative census while granting High Executor Darthalia comprehensive intelligence on every resident, property owner, and taxpayer in the settlement.",al={"what is hillsbrad town registry","hillsbrad registry purpose","why steal town registry"},it="item",add="827d131a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, striking the Town Hall weakens the Alliance's ability to coordinate local militia and helps secure Tarren Mill's southern frontier from human counterattacks.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see the Forsaken's campaign against Hillsbrad's human rule as both expansion and retribution against the living who dispute Lordaeron's borders.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Magistrate Burnside's death and the burning of the town charter mark the fall of Hillsbrad's last legitimate local government."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","hillsbrad councilmen","hillsbrad proclamation","hillsbrad town registry","magistrate burnside","tarren mill","town hall"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="26",faction="Horde",id=532,ri={"Hillsbrad Town Registry"}},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (4)"}}
E["quest:533"] = {t="quest",n="Infiltration",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Krusk has at last heard word and rumor of Gol'dir. The Syndicate keeps moving the orc prisoner, and Krusk sends you to its large camp just north of town to bring back whatever information you can find.",h="In Tarren Mill, Krusk has at last heard word and rumor of Gol'dir.",sec={{t="Word of Gol'dir",b="Krusk has at last heard word and rumor of Gol'dir, an orc prisoner held by the Syndicate. Its humans keep moving him, but the search has narrowed to their large camp just north of Tarren Mill. Krusk sends you there to find whatever information you can and carry it back. With each day, he fears Gol'dir's prospects grow darker.",sp=0},{t="News for Krusk",b="The information you bring back tells Krusk where Gol'dir is held. The camp lies not far from Tarren Mill, and Krusk hopes its defenders are less prepared than the captors who took him and the others the first time.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Krusk looking for?",a="Krusk is looking for Gol'dir, an orc held prisoner by the Syndicate. Its humans keep moving him about.",al={"who is krusk looking for","who is goldir","who needs to be rescued"}},{q="Where does Krusk send you to find the information?",a="Krusk sends you to the Syndicate's large camp just north of Tarren Mill to bring back whatever information you can find about Gol'dir's whereabouts.",al={"where do i go for infiltration","syndicate camp location","where is the syndicate missive"}},{q="What information is needed to locate Gol'dir?",a="Anything that shows where Gol'dir is can help locate him. A Syndicate missive is what you bring back to Krusk.",al={"what do i need to find","what item is krusk looking for","what is the missive"}},{q="Who is holding Gol'dir?",a="The Syndicate is holding Gol'dir, and its humans keep moving him about.",al={"who captured goldir","who is holding the orc captive"}}},kw={"alterac","gol'dir","hillsbrad","infiltration","krusk","missive","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:503","npc:krusk","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","topic:horde"},m={start="Krusk",["end"]="Krusk",level="34",faction="Horde",id=533},src={"Infiltration (Classic)"}}
E["quest:536"] = {t="quest",n="Down the Coast",z="hillsbrad",s="Along Hillsbrad's coast, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle leaves Southshore's defense to passing adventurers. Sent from Stormwind, he would rather drink ale than patrol, even as Torn Fin murlocs gather along the Western Strand.",h="Along Hillsbrad's coast, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle leaves Southshore's defense to passing adventurers.",sec={{t="A Reluctant Posting",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle left Stormwind's city guard for a post in Southshore. The port feels dreary to him, and he cannot bear the fishy harbor odor. He spends his days drinking at the inn instead of patrolling the frontlines. Marshal Redpath has ordered him to protect Southshore from the dangers nearby, but Orinelle hires passing sellswords to do the work.",sp=0},{t="The Torn Fin Threat",b="The Western Strand runs along the coast west of Southshore. Orinelle scoffs at the murlocs as overgrown fish, but the Torn Fin tribe threatens coastal travel and local shipping. Its tidehunters and oracles gather in camps along the breakers and ambush anyone who strays too far from town walls. Clearing the shoreline means facing them there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Farren Orinelle deal with the murlocs himself?",a="Farren sees Southshore as an unwanted exile from his former life in Stormwind's city guard. Resentful of his posting and disgusted by the coastal town, he would rather drink ale at the inn than fight murlocs, so he pays adventurers to do the work.",al={"why is farren drinking","farren orinelle personality","why hire adventurers"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is 'ol Redpath' mentioned by Orinelle?",a="He means Marshal Redpath, Southshore's marshal. Redpath is responsible for order and defense in the embattled settlement, and issues military orders that Lieutenant Orinelle tries to evade.",al={"who is redpath","magistrate redpath","orinelle commander"}},{q="Where are the Torn Fin murlocs located?",a="The Torn Fin murlocs live along the Western Strand, the coastal beaches west of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where are torn fin","murloc location hillsbrad","western strand location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kinds of murlocs need to be eliminated?",a="The order calls for killing Torn Fin Tidehunters, the tribe's frontline fighters, and Torn Fin Oracles, who use elemental and aquatic magic to aid their kin.",al={"murloc targets","which murlocs kill","tidehunter oracle"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens after clearing the beach for Orinelle?",a="After the sweep, Orinelle sees that he needs evidence to satisfy Marshal Redpath's scrutiny. He then seeks physical proof of the slain murlocs.",al={"next quest after down the coast","down the coast chain","farrens proof next"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is the murloc threat actually serious or just an excuse?",a="Farren mocks them as harmless overgrown fish, but the Torn Fin are numerous and aggressive, and live close to Southshore's docks. They threaten trade routes and fishermen.",al={"are murlocs dangerous hillsbrad","southshore murloc danger"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Farren Orinelle want the murlocs killed?",a="Lieutenant Orinelle despises Southshore and feels exiled after being transferred from the Stormwind city guard. His superior, Marshal Redpath, ordered him to secure the coastline against the local murlocs. Farren considers the assignment beneath him and mocks the overgrown fish as a trivial chore. By having you thin out their ranks, he hopes to present the illusion that he is actively obeying orders and keeping Southshore safe, all while nursing his ale and longing for a transfer back to the capital.",al={"farren motive","why kill murlocs farren","why does farren want murlocs dead"},it="motive",add="dc8aa8a8"},{q="What are the Torn Fin murlocs along the coast?",a="The Torn Fin are an aggressive tribe of murlocs infesting the Western Strand and southern shores of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Clustered in fishing encampments along the water, their tidehunters and mystic oracles raid the shoreline and pose a persistent annoyance to the town of Southshore. Though Lieutenant Orinelle scoffs at them as mere fish, their sheer numbers along the surf make them a continuous nuisance to the local harbor and travelers venturing along the coast.",al={"who are torn fin","torn fin murlocs","hillsbrad murlocs"},it="target",add="11ea9e8a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you know Southshore is a key coastal stronghold in the north. Negligence among its garrison can put the town at risk.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see the gulf between Stormwind's sheltered heart and the hard lives of northern settlements in Orinelle's neglect."},kw={"down the coast","farren orinelle","hillsbrad","murloc","redpath","southshore","torn fin","western strand"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:559","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:murloc","quest:562","quest:563","topic:alliance"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=536},src={"Down the Coast"}}
E["quest:539"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="Horde forces strike at Azurelode Mine in the Battle of Hillsbrad. High Executor Darthalia orders them to kill Foreman Bonds and his crew, cutting iron shipments to Alliance armories.",h="Horde forces strike at Azurelode Mine in the Battle of Hillsbrad.",sec={{t="Severing the Iron Supply",b="High Executor Darthalia marked Azurelode Mine as vital to human strength after Horde forces seized the Hillsbrad Town Registry in earlier raids. The mine lies just south of Hillsbrad Fields, where workers keep extracting rich iron ore for Alliance weaponsmiths and armories. If the mine keeps operating, Southshore can rearm and strengthen its garrisons, undoing Tarren Mill's earlier victories.",sp=0},{t="A Decisive Message",b="Darthalia orders Horde forces to kill Foreman Bonds, the human overseer, and a significant part of his workforce. The assault reaches into the mine's dark shafts to break production. It sends Southshore a clear warning: the Forsaken can reach its supply lines and isolated labor camps.",sp=0},{t="Spoils for the Dark Lady",b="Sylvanas Windrunner's forces also seek the mine's rich ore veins for their own foundries. Tarren Mill needs a steady supply of metal to make weapons and plate for the war across Lordaeron. The ore can turn a former human asset into a source of Forsaken arms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Azurelode Mine so important to the Forsaken?",a="Azurelode Mine supplies high-grade iron ore to Alliance armories. Taking it deprives garrisons such as Southshore of materials for forging and puts the ore in the Undercity's hands to equip Forsaken forces.",al={"why attack azurelode","azurelode mine purpose","why target the mine"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Foreman Bonds?",a="Foreman Bonds is the human overseer of the Azurelode excavation. He manages the miners and can call on stalwart dwarven defenders when cornered deep in the lower chambers.",al={"foreman bonds","who is bonds","who leads the mine"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Azurelode Mine located?",a="Azurelode Mine lies in the hills south of Hillsbrad Fields, west of Southshore along the coastline bluffs.",al={"where is azurelode mine","azurelode location","how to find the mine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How did Darthalia find out about the mine's operations?",a="Darthalia learned the mine was active and important to supply lines by reviewing the Hillsbrad Town Registry. Horde operatives recovered it in earlier strikes on human settlements.",al={"how did darthalia know","town registry mine","hillsbrad intel"},it="history"},{q="What happens after Foreman Bonds is slain?",a="With the mine crippled and its resources marked for Forsaken control, High Executor Darthalia widens the offensive against Hillsbrad's remaining infrastructure and presses closer to Southshore.",al={"what next battle of hillsbrad","after killing bonds","quest aftermath"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does the Alliance defend the mine?",a="Yes. Armed Alliance guards watch the entrance, and human miners work the shafts. Foreman Bonds can also call on tough dwarven reinforcements deep in the tunnels.",al={"mine guards","alliance presence in azurelode","dwarves in mine"},it="danger"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, taking Azurelode Mine secures iron for the Deathguard and turns human industry toward arming Sylvanas's armies across Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, disrupting Hillsbrad's main metal supply eases pressure on the Tarren Mill frontline and makes it harder for human troops to replace their equipment.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can see why Azurelode Mine's rich iron veins make it a point of conflict for those seeking valuable ore."},kw={"azurelode","bonds","darthalia","hillsbrad","iron","miners","southshore","tarren mill","undercity"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:azurelode-mine","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="28",faction="Horde",id=539},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (5)"}}
E["quest:540"] = {t="quest",n="Preserving Knowledge",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Loremaster Dibbs sends you to recover books from the Ruins of Alterac. Ogres have settled among the precious volumes left there, and one worn leather book matters most: it holds The Arm of Gri'lek, a work of ancient troll lore.",h="In Southshore, Loremaster Dibbs sends you to recover books from the Ruins of Alterac.",sec={{t="Books in Ogre Hands",b="Loremaster Dibbs fears for the books in the Ruins of Alterac, where ogres have made their home. You are to search for the tomes they have looted and recover what you can. Dibbs would climb into the mountains to search as well, but fears old bones would not survive the journey.",sp=0},{t="The Arm of Gri'lek",b="Among the tomes, Loremaster Dibbs most wants a worn leather book containing The Arm of Gri'lek. Dibbs is bent on learning the ancient troll lore inside, and the Ruins of Alterac were the last known home of an intact copy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where are they?",a="Loremaster Dibbs, in Southshore, offers it.",al={"who gives preserving knowledge","where is loremaster dibbs","preserving knowledge quest giver"}},{q="What specific book is Loremaster Dibbs searching for?",a="Dibbs seeks the worn leather volume containing The Arm of Gri'lek, a work of ancient troll lore.",al={"which book does dibbs want","what tome do i need","arm of gri'lek book"}},{q="Where are the books located?",a="The books are in the Ruins of Alterac, where ogres have settled and looted the tomes. The ruins were the last known home of an intact copy of The Arm of Gri'lek.",al={"where to find the tomes","where are the ruins","where is the arm of gri'lek"}},{q="Why does Dibbs want books from Alterac?",a="Dibbs fears what the ogres may be doing to the precious books in the ruins and wants to recover what can be saved. Dibbs wants The Arm of Gri'lek most, to learn its ancient troll lore.",al={"why preserve knowledge","why alterac books","what does dibbs want with books"}}},kw={"arm of gri'lek","hillsbrad foothills","loremaster dibbs","ogres","preserving knowledge","ruins of alterac","southshore","troll lore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:troll","zone:hillsbrad"},m={id=540},src={"In-game quest text: Preserving Knowledge"},fv=true}
E["quest:541"] = {t="quest",n="Battle of Hillsbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad, the Forsaken turn their campaign on Dun Garok. High Executor Darthalia sends Horde champions to break the dwarven garrison aiding local humans and kill its commander, Captain Ironhill.",h="In Hillsbrad, the Forsaken turn their campaign on Dun Garok.",sec={{t="Testing the Alliance",b="High Executor Darthalia has already pressed the human farmers and town militia across the foothills. Now she turns Tarren Mill's fury on Ironforge's troops. Dwarven soldiers have taken up arms for Southshore, strengthening the human presence in Lordaeron. Darthalia sees that alliance as an obstacle to be broken. She means to show the Alliance that helping the human survivors will bring devastation.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Dun Garok",b="Dun Garok is built against Thoradin's Wall in southeastern Hillsbrad. The fortified stronghold is held by disciplined mountaineers, skilled riflemen, and battle-hardened priests. To take it, Horde forces must break through those defenders and kill Captain Ironhill. His death breaks Ironforge's forward command in the region and leaves the remaining human enclaves isolated.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are dwarves fighting in Hillsbrad?",a="Ironforge sent its soldiers north to Dun Garok because the dwarves support the Alliance and want to aid the human survivors in Southshore and Hillsbrad against Forsaken expansion.",al={"why are there dwarves in hillsbrad","dwarves dun garok","why dwarves helping humans"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Dun Garok located?",a="Dun Garok lies in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills, built into the foundations of Thoradin's Wall.",al={"dun garok location","where is dun garok","find dun garok"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Captain Ironhill?",a="Captain Ironhill commands Dun Garok's dwarven garrison and keeps its mountaineers organized and ready to fight in the region.",al={"captain ironhill","who is ironhill","dun garok leader"},it="target"},{q="Who gives this order?",a="High Executor Darthalia, the Forsaken commander stationed at Tarren Mill, orders the attack on the dwarven garrison.",al={"who gives quest","questgiver darthalia","darthalia hillsbrad"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens if Horde forces fail here?",a="Darthalia warns that failure will not be tolerated. Those who cannot break Dun Garok will be sent back to Tirisfal Glades to dig graves.",al={"what if fail","darthalia threat","consequences"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Dun Garok so difficult to assault?",a="Dun Garok is held by trained dwarven soldiers, rifle squads, and holy priests. They fight in tight formations inside the fortified underground and elevated bunker.",al={"dun garok elite","why is dun garok hard","dun garok defense"}},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want Dun Garok attacked?",a="The Forsaken are waging an all-out campaign to break human control over Hillsbrad Foothills, but the dwarves of Ironforge have intervened to bolster their Alliance allies. High Executor Darthalia intends to break the Alliance's resolve by showing them the cost of coming to Southshore's defense. By crushing their barracks at Dun Garok and slaying their commander, she aims to sever human reinforcements and secure the region entirely under the Dark Lady's dominion.",al={"why attack dun garok","darthalia motive","why kill the dwarves"},it="motive",add="b055c9ea"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Striking Dun Garok cuts off Ironforge's military reinforcements sent to aid the beleaguered humans of Southshore.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, destroying the dwarven garrison secures southeastern Lordaeron and makes it harder for an Alliance vanguard to march south through Thoradin's Wall.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dun Garok shows Ironforge's loyalty to its human allies. The dwarves endure the Forsaken siege to hold the northern frontier."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","captain ironhill","dun garok","high executor darthalia","mountaineer","rifleman","tarren mill","thoradin's wall"},rel={"subzone:dun-garok","npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:thoradin-s-wall","zone:tirisfal","topic:alliance"},m={start="High Executor Darthalia",level="30",faction="Horde",id=541},src={"Battle of Hillsbrad (6)"}}
E["quest:544"] = {t="quest",n="Prison Break In",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare faces a crisis during his research. Months ago, four Forsaken fled the Undercity with artifacts stolen from a secure vault, and Sylvanas wants them back.",h="In Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare faces a crisis during his research.",sec={{t="Thieves of the Dark Lady",b="Magus Wordeen Voidglare came to Tarren Mill to research, but now a crisis demands his attention. Four Forsaken turned from their brethren and stole from the Dark Lady. They broke into a secure vault and took four artifacts the apothecaries need for certain studies. Sylvanas wants them returned.",sp=0},{t="The Internment Camp",b="The thieves fled the Undercity for Dalaran, where its wizards placed them in quarantine at the Lordamere Internment Camp. You are sent to find the traitors, recover the artifacts and report to Voidglare in Tarren Mill. There are four: a Bloodstone Wedge, Marble, Shard and Oval. Dermot holds the wedge, Ricter the marble, Alina the shard and Kegan Darkmar the oval.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magus Wordeen Voidglare?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare came to Tarren Mill to research, but now faces a crisis over four artifacts stolen from the Dark Lady.",al={"magus voidglare","wordeen voidglare","quest giver"}},{q="What did the Forsaken thieves steal?",a="The Forsaken stole four artifacts from a secure vault, needed by the apothecaries for certain studies: a Bloodstone Wedge, Marble, Shard and Oval.",al={"what was stolen","bloodstones","stolen artifacts"}},{q="Where are the thieves being held?",a="The Dalaran wizards are holding the thieves in quarantine at the Lordamere Internment Camp.",al={"internment camp location","where are the traitors","where is kegan"}},{q="Who are the four traitors?",a="The four traitors are Dermot, who holds the Bloodstone Wedge; Ricter, who holds the Marble; Alina, who holds the Shard; and Kegan Darkmar, who holds the Oval.",al={"thieves names","four forsaken","who stole the bloodstones"}}},kw={"alina","bloodstone","dalaran","dermot","kegan darkmar","lordamere internment camp","ricter","tarren mill","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:lordamere-internment-camp","subzone:tarren-mill","quest:545","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","subzone:dalaran","zone:hillsbrad","topic:mage"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",["end"]="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",level="34",faction="Horde",id=544},src={"Prison Break In"}}
E["quest:545"] = {t="quest",n="Dalaran Patrols",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare turns his attention to Dalaran's outskirts. Beyond the city's great dome, ruined streets may hold treasures of magical worth, but wizards and their elemental slaves patrol them. Voidglare wants the patrols thinned.",h="In Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare turns his attention to Dalaran's outskirts.",sec={{t="Treasures in the Ruins",b="After Prison Break In, Voidglare turns his attention to the wizards of Dalaran. They raised a great dome of magic over their city's heart. Some say it protects them from the violence of the age; others say they sought solitude to study and plot. Voidglare cares nothing for their reason. Beyond the dome, the ruined outskirts may hold treasures of real magical worth, but wizards and their elemental slaves patrol the area. You are sent to hunt six Dalaran Summoners and twelve Elemental Slaves, then return to Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Magus Voidglare want the patrols thinned?",a="Voidglare believes the ruined outskirts beyond Dalaran's dome may hold treasures of real magical worth, but wizards and their elemental slaves patrol the area.",al={"why kill dalaran patrols","magus voidglare goal","dalaran patrols motive"}},{q="What is the magical dome around Dalaran?",a="The wizards of Dalaran raised a great dome of magic over their city's heart. Some say it shields them from the violence of the age; others say they sought solitude to study and plot.",al={"what is the dalaran dome","why is dalaran in a bubble","dalaran shield"}},{q="What patrols the outskirts of Dalaran?",a="The wizards of Dalaran and their elemental slaves patrol the outskirts. Voidglare wants you to hunt six Dalaran Summoners and twelve Elemental Slaves.",al={"who guards dalaran","dalaran ruins enemies","who is patrolling dalaran"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="Prison Break In came before this, and it also came from Voidglare in Tarren Mill.",al={"previous quest","what comes before dalaran patrols"}}},kw={"dalaran","dalaran summoners","elemental slaves","hillsbrad foothills","magical dome","tarren mill","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"quest:544","subzone:dalaran","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",["end"]="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",level="35",faction="Horde",id=545},src={"Dalaran Patrols"}}
E["quest:546"] = {t="quest",n="Souvenirs of Death",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, Deathguard Samsa envies those sent against the human settlements of the Hillsbrad Foothills. He asks for thirty human skulls taken in battle for his collection.",h="At Tarren Mill, Deathguard Samsa envies those sent against the human settlements of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Guard's Envy",b="High Executor Darthalia directs the Forsaken campaign against Hillsbrad's human settlements. Deathguard Samsa remains on sentry duty in Tarren Mill, while others are sent to raid, burn, and pillage. He envies their chance to slaughter the living, a privilege denied to a guard fixed in place.",sp=0},{t="A Gruesome Trophy",b="Samsa hates the humans of Hillsbrad and collects the skulls of those slain in the campaign. He asks for thirty, not for an arcane rite or military plan, but as trophies from a war he longs to fight himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where are they located?",a="Deathguard Samsa offers it from his sentry post in Tarren Mill, the main Forsaken stronghold in northern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"quest giver","who gives souvenirs of death","samsa location"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What does Deathguard Samsa want?",a="Samsa asks for thirty Hillsbrad Human Skulls from human combatants and townsfolk across Hillsbrad Fields and the town of Hillsbrad.",al={"quest goal","what items needed","skulls required"},it="wants"},{q="Why does Samsa want human skulls?",a="Samsa collects macabre trophies. Confined to garrison duty in Tarren Mill while others wage war, he gathers skulls to share in the slaughter of the living from afar.",al={"why collect skulls","samsa motivation","what are skulls for"},it="motive"},{q="When does this quest become available?",a="Samsa approaches you after you enlist with High Executor Darthalia and complete the opening assault in the Battle of Hillsbrad campaign.",al={"quest prerequisites","how to unlock","prereqs for souvenirs"},gp=true},{q="Are the skulls used for Forsaken alchemy or magic?",a="No. Samsa's request is personal, unlike Royal Apothecary Society assignments that seek biological reagents for the New Plague. He finds the severed skulls beautiful and cherishes them as souvenirs of war.",al={"are skulls for apothecary","magic skulls","necromancy use"},it="item"},{q="Which humans provide the skulls?",a="The skulls come from human farmers, peasants, militia, and defenders in Hillsbrad Fields or the town of Hillsbrad, where you fight for Tarren Mill.",al={"where to farm skulls","which mobs drop skulls","hillsbrad humans"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Deathguard Samsa need an adventurer instead of hunting skulls himself?",a="Deathguard Samsa is bound to his post in Tarren Mill. While the Forsaken wage an active campaign against Hillsbrad, Samsa is stuck standing guard instead of participating in the raid. Since High Executor Darthalia has already enlisted you to join the frontline fighting, Samsa asks you to take pity on an old soldier and collect macabre trophies on his behalf.",al={"why me deathguard samsa","why cant samsa get skulls","why doesnt samsa hunt"},it="why_me",add="0c405e10"},{q="Who are the humans in Hillsbrad that you are fighting?",a="The targets are the human citizens, laborers, and defenders of Hillsbrad Fields and the town of Hillsbrad. As one of the remaining sovereign human strongholds in Lordaeron, Hillsbrad directly opposes the Forsaken outpost of Tarren Mill. The Forsaken consider their continued existence and Alliance allegiance an unacceptable threat to their territorial dominance.",al={"who are hillsbrad humans","hillsbrad target","hillsbrad humans why here"},it="target",add="3446168a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you take part in the push against Alliance strongholds in Lordaeron, securing northern supply routes for Tarren Mill.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead champion, you see the casual cruelty and deep animosity many Forsaken hold toward living humans who view them as monsters.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you face the brutal, existential threat the Forsaken pose to Hillsbrad's surviving townsfolk, marked by their systematic collection of severed human heads."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","deathguard samsa","forsaken","hillsbrad","hillsbrad human skull","souvenirs of death","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:deathguard-samsa","quest:527","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Deathguard Samsa",level="25",faction="Horde",id=546,ri={"Hillsbrad Human Skull"}},src={"Souvenirs of Death"}}
E["quest:547"] = {t="quest",n="Humbert's Sword",z="hillsbrad",s="Near Dun Garok, Humbert's Sword is missing from its owner's camp. Deathguard Humbert had left to gather firewood while scouting the dwarven stronghold on High Executor Darthalia's orders. Ironforge scouts took his weapon, and he fears Darthalia will learn of his failure.",h="Near Dun Garok, Humbert's Sword is missing from its owner's camp.",sec={{t="A Scout's Negligence",b="Deathguard Humbert watches Dun Garok for High Executor Darthalia. He keeps a hidden post near the dwarven fortress. One morning, he leaves the camp briefly to gather firewood for boiling water. Ironforge scouts find the camp unguarded and loot it. When Humbert returns, his sword is gone, carried into the heavily defended bunker.",sp=0},{t="Fear of the Rafters",b="Humbert knows losing his weapon to the enemy he was sent to watch could cost him his life under Forsaken command. If High Executor Darthalia learns what happened, he fears she will hang him from the rafters in Tarren Mill. He cannot storm Dun Garok alone, so he relies on passing Horde adventurers to recover his blade before his commander notices anything amiss.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Humbert?",a="Deathguard Humbert is a Forsaken soldier stationed at Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills. High Executor Darthalia assigned him to watch Dun Garok, the fortified dwarven outpost in the southeastern foothills.",al={"deathguard humbert","who is humbert","humbert"},it="identity"},{q="How did Humbert lose his sword?",a="Humbert left his post near Dun Garok one morning to gather firewood for boiling water. While he was away, dwarven scouts found his camp, took his belongings, and carried off his sword.",al={"how did humbert lose his weapon","who stole humbert's sword","stolen sword"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Humbert so desperate to get his sword back quietly?",a="Humbert fears High Executor Darthalia will execute him if she learns he lost his equipment to the dwarves he was sent to watch. He expects her to hang him from the rafters in Tarren Mill.",al={"why humbert worried","darthalia punishment","why fear darthalia"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the sword located?",a="The dwarven scouts carried Humbert's sword into Dun Garok. It is among the Ironforge mountaineers, riflemen, and officers in the bunker.",al={"sword location","where is humbert's sword","dun garok sword"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did the dwarves steal anything else from Humbert?",a="Yes. Humbert found his gear missing from camp, including his sword. The sword is the only thing he asks you to recover from Dun Garok.",al={"humbert other gear","humbert armor pieces","humbert's pants"}},{q="What is Dun Garok?",a="Dun Garok is an Ironforge dwarven stronghold in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. Its dwarves help protect the humans of Hillsbrad and nearby Azurelode Mine, and its Alliance garrison is in direct conflict with the Forsaken of Tarren Mill.",al={"dun garok fortress","dun garok lore","dwarves in hillsbrad"},it="place"},{q="Why is Humbert's sword so important to him?",a="To Deathguard Humbert, the weapon is both his personal pride and the badge of his duty. Without it, he stands unarmed while on scout duty for Tarren Mill, completely exposed to the wrath of High Executor Darthalia. It holds no magical powers or grand enchantments; it is simply his prized blade, and having it back restores his dignity and conceals a humiliating blunder from his commander.",al={"what is humbert's sword","why does humbert need his sword","humbert sword purpose"},it="item",add="65d1b07f"},{q="Who are the dwarves holding Humbert's sword?",a="The thieves belong to the dwarven forces stationed at Dun Garok, an Alliance stronghold nestled in southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. These Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen regularly send scouts through the hills to contest Forsaken expansion. A patrol stumbled upon Humbert's unguarded camp while he gathered firewood, looting his weaponry and carrying it back behind their fortified walls.",al={"who stole humbert's sword","dun garok dwarves","who has the sword"},it="target",add="c70ad326"},{q="Why does Humbert need you to recover his sword instead of doing it himself?",a="Humbert cannot storm a heavily fortified dwarven bastion alone, nor can he ask his fellow Deathguards for assistance without admitting he abandoned his post to boil water and let his equipment get stolen. If word reaches High Executor Darthalia that he lost his weapon to dwarven thieves, she would make a brutal example of him. An independent adventurer can slip in and recover the blade discreetly.",al={"why can't humbert get his sword","why ask me humberts sword","why humbert needs help"},it="why_me",add="6c936ae5"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken soldier in Hillsbrad, you know the brutal discipline High Executor Darthalia enforces. In Tarren Mill, failure or negligence can bring execution, not mercy.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a mountaineer of Dun Garok, you have no love for the Forsaken on your doorstep. Every chance to harass Tarren Mill's sentries and strip their camps bare matters.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you strike at Dun Garok to weaken Ironforge's military hold on Hillsbrad Foothills and protect Tarren Mill from incursions from the south."},kw={"darthalia","deathguard","dun garok","firewood","hillsbrad","humbert","sword","tarren mill"},rel={"npc:deathguard-humbert","subzone:dun-garok","npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:527","quest:509","topic:horde"},m={start="Deathguard Humbert",level="30",faction="Horde",id=547,ri={"Humbert's Sword"}},src={"Humbert's Sword (quest)"}}
E["quest:549"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Syndicate Personnel",z="hillsbrad",s="On Tarren Mill's bounty board, Lady Sylvanas's decree condemns every Syndicate member to death. The Forsaken seek to clear the brigands from Durnholde Keep's ruins before they threaten Horde operations in the foothills.",h="On Tarren Mill's bounty board, Lady Sylvanas's decree condemns every Syndicate member to death.",sec={{t="A Standing Execution Order",b="The Syndicate's sudden arrival southeast of Tarren Mill has drawn the Forsaken's attention. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her commanders see the Syndicate as an active pestilence, not displaced nobles to bargain with. The bounty orders immediate death. Any prisoners brought in will be executed without trial.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Durnholde",b="Durnholde Keep, once an infamous internment fortress, now lies shattered and lawless. Syndicate Rogues and Watchmen have taken its crumbling ramparts and towers as an operations hub. High Executor Darthalia needs the armed bandits driven from the ruins to secure the road and protect Tarren Mill's southeastern approach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the bounty for Syndicate personnel?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner issued the bounty under her direct authority, and it is posted on Tarren Mill's notice board. High Executor Darthalia, the settlement's military commander, collects proof of execution.",al={"who posted wanted syndicate personnel","who wants syndicate dead","bounty poster"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these Syndicate members located?",a="Syndicate members gather among Durnholde Keep's shattered stones, southeast of Tarren Mill across the river, and around the ruined guard tower just south of the fortress.",al={"where are syndicate rogues","durnholde syndicate location","where to find watchmen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Forsaken want them dead instead of captured?",a="The Forsaken see the Syndicate as treacherous pests and an armed threat on their territory. The decree orders any captured members executed without trial, so there is no point in taking them alive.",al={"why kill syndicate","why no prisoners","darthalia syndicate"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Syndicate doing in Durnholde Keep?",a="Made up mostly of disgraced Alteraci nobles and mercenaries, the Syndicate uses abandoned keeps, ruins, and towers across Lordaeron as bases to raid settlements, rob travelers, and rebuild its shattered power.",al={"why syndicate in durnholde","syndicate purpose hillsbrad","durnholde keep occupiers"},it="target"},{q="What happens after culling these Syndicate operatives?",a="Once the local Rogues and Watchmen are thinned, High Executor Darthalia issues a high-priority bounty on their leader, Baron Vardus.",al={"what quest is next","after wanted syndicate personnel","next bounty"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia rely on adventurers for this bounty?",a="High Executor Darthalia oversees Tarren Mill under direct mandate from Lady Sylvanas, but her standing garrison is stretched thin defending Forsaken territory against Southshore and the regional threats of Hillsbrad. As she bluntly reminds visitors, she has far more pressing matters of command than personally handling every encampment of thieves. Offering public bounties draws willing mercenaries and Horde champions to purge pests from Durnholde Keep without depleting the town's front-line defenses.",al={"why send adventurers","why darthalia bounty","why not tarren mill guards"},it="why_me",add="6d6e03d8"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, clearing Alterac's living noble remnants is a practical need if they are to hold the hills of Lordaeron without challenge.",["faction:Horde"]="Durnholde Keep carries grim memories for the Horde as the internment fortress where orcs were once held captive. Clearing the brigands from its ruins carries symbolic weight.",["class:Rogue"]="The Syndicate has skilled cutpurses and ambushers throughout Durnholde, bringing rival practitioners of stealth into direct conflict."},kw={"durnholde keep","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad foothills","syndicate","syndicate rogue","syndicate watchman","tarren mill","wanted"},rel={"subzone:durnholde-keep","npc:high-executor-darthalia","topic:syndicate","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:498","topic:horde"},m={start="WANTED",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="22",faction="Horde",id=549},src={"WANTED: Syndicate Personnel"}}
E["quest:552"] = {t="quest",n="Helcular's Revenge",z="hillsbrad",s="Novice Thaivand in Tarren Mill means to avenge Master Helcular, a great wizard on the brink of becoming a lich, who was killed by a human lynch mob after it found his ritual lair. Before vengeance can fall on Southshore, Thaivand needs Helcular's Rod, which one of the yeti there must hold.",h="Novice Thaivand in Tarren Mill means to avenge Master Helcular, a great wizard on the brink of becoming a...",sec={{t="A Master Interrupted",b="Master Helcular was on the brink of becoming a lich when he was found and killed by a human lynch mob, who had discovered the ritual lair he kept in the hills. They then buried the body in the Southshore cemetery. His apprentice, Thaivand, finds this disregard for a great wizard unacceptable and vows that the rains of vengeance will fall upon the town of Southshore.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Rod",b="Thaivand says Helcular's Rod is needed first. Yeti have overtaken the ritual lair, and Thaivand is sure one of the beasts has the rod. There are so many yeti in the region that finding it will be difficult. Growless Cave and Darrow Hill are among the places they can be found.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Master Helcular?",a="A great wizard on the brink of becoming a lich, killed by a human lynch mob that found his ritual lair in the hills. His body was buried in the Southshore cemetery.",al={"who is helcular","helcular lore","helcular backstory"}},{q="Why does Novice Thaivand want Helcular's Rod?",a="Thaivand, Helcular's apprentice, plans vengeance upon the town of Southshore and says the rod is needed first.",al={"why need rod","helculars rod purpose","thaivand goal"}},{q="Where did the rod go?",a="Yeti have overtaken Helcular's ritual lair, and Thaivand is sure one of them has the rod. Yeti can be found in places such as Growless Cave and Darrow Hill.",al={"where is the rod","how did yeti get rod","rod location"}},{q="Where is Novice Thaivand located?",a="In Tarren Mill, in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"thaivand location","where to turn in helculars revenge","novice thaivand"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This is for Horde adventurers; Thaivand in Tarren Mill is the one who calls on you."},kw={"alterac","helcular","hillsbrad","lich","rod","southshore","tarren mill","thaivand","yeti"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:southshore","subzone:growless-cave","subzone:darrow-hill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","topic:horde","topic:human"},m={start="Novice Thaivand",["end"]="Novice Thaivand",level="33",faction="Horde",id=552},src={"Helcular's Revenge"}}
E["quest:553"] = {t="quest",n="Helcular's Revenge",z="hillsbrad",s="Novice Thaivand hands you the Rod of Helcular. Three ceremonial pyres that Helcular fashioned for his most powerful spell must each charge it, and then it is to be driven into Helcular's grave in Southshore.",h="Novice Thaivand hands you the Rod of Helcular.",sec={{t="The Three Flames",b="Helcular fashioned three ceremonial pyres for his most powerful spell, and the rod must be charged from each one. The flames of Azel and Veraz lie within the Foothill Caverns, in the yeti cave at Darrow Hill. The third, the Flame of Uzel, is found in a small cave above the caverns, farther north in the mountains, near Growless Cave.",sp=0},{t="The Grave in Southshore",b="Once the rod is charged from all three flames, it is to be driven into Helcular's grave at Southshore, a heavily guarded human town. The graveyard sits in the northeast corner of the town, by the river, and the grave lies at the graveyard's southeastern corner.",sp=0},{t="After the Ritual",b="When the charged rod is driven into the grave, a great rumbling comes from the ground, and Helcular returns, wandering the Southshore graveyard and attacking people nearby.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the three ceremonial flames located?",a="Azel's flame and Veraz's flame are within the Foothill Caverns, in the yeti cave at Darrow Hill, in Hillsbrad Foothills. Uzel's flame is in a small cave above those caverns, farther north in the mountains near Growless Cave, in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"flame locations","where is flame of azel","where is flame of uzel","find the pyres"}},{q="Where is Helcular's grave?",a="At Southshore, a heavily guarded human town. The graveyard sits in the northeast corner of the town, by the river, and the grave lies at the graveyard's southeastern corner.",al={"helcular grave location","where is the grave","southshore graveyard"}},{q="Who provides the Rod of Helcular?",a="Novice Thaivand gives you the rod.",al={"who gives the rod","quest giver","novice thaivand"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="Helcular's Revenge, in which Novice Thaivand needed Helcular's Rod found. Thaivand is Helcular's apprentice, and Helcular was killed by a human lynch mob and buried in the Southshore cemetery.",al={"previous quest","helcular chain part 1"}}},kw={"alterac","azel","darrow hill","growless cave","helcular","hillsbrad","southshore","thaivand","uzel","veraz"},rel={"quest:552","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","subzone:darrow-hill","subzone:growless-cave","zone:alterac","topic:horde","topic:human"},m={start="Novice Thaivand",["end"]="Helcular's Grave",level="33",faction="Horde",id=553},src={"Helcular's Revenge (2)","In-game quest text: Helcular's Revenge"}}
E["quest:555"] = {t="quest",n="Soothing Turtle Bisque",z="hillsbrad",s="Southshore's Chef Jessen wants Soothing Turtle Bisque back on his tavern menu. Unrest has cut off his supply of snapjaw turtle meat, so he asks cooks to brave the northern waters near Dalaran and Lake Lordamere.",h="Southshore's Chef Jessen wants Soothing Turtle Bisque back on his tavern menu.",sec={{t="A Northern Delicacy",b="Southshore is one of the Alliance's last intact coastal towns in Lordaeron, holding to civilian life amid growing strife. Chef Jessen says his cooking rivals any tavern north of Stormwind. Patrons supposedly travel from Darkshire in Duskwood to taste his Soothing Turtle Bisque. The rich soup depends on fresh meat from snapjaw turtles native to the rivers and lakes of the northern mountains.",sp=0},{t="Peril on Lordamere",b="In calmer years, Jessen gathered turtle meat himself, traveling past Dalaran to Lordamere Lake's eastern shore. Rising tensions, hostile wildlife, the Syndicate, and Forsaken incursions have made the lands beyond town deadly for ordinary townsfolk. To keep the bisque on his menu, Jessen depends on armed travelers willing to gather meat from snapjaws along the riverbanks and northern shores.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest for Soothing Turtle Bisque?",a="Chef Jessen, a cook in the Alliance coastal town of Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills, makes the request to visiting cooks.",al={"who gives soothing turtle bisque","where do i start soothing turtle bisque","chef jessen quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Chef Jessen need outside help gathering turtle meat?",a="Jessen once hunted snapjaw turtles near Dalaran and Lordamere Lake, but unrest and dangerous beasts now make the region too perilous for him to gather meat himself.",al={"why cant jessen get meat","why does jessen need turtles"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are snapjaw turtles found in the region?",a="Snapjaw turtles live along the freshwater river between Hillsbrad Foothills and the Alterac Mountains, and along Lordamere Lake's shores north of Dalaran.",al={"turtle meat location","where are snapjaws","where to farm turtle meat"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do you need to know Cooking to take this quest?",a="Yes. Chef Jessen shares the request and his cooking knowledge only with travelers trained in Cooking, though no particular skill rank is needed.",al={"is cooking required","cooking profession required","can anyone take soothing turtle bisque"},gp=true},{q="Why is Southshore's cuisine famous?",a="Chef Jessen claims Southshore has the finest cuisine north of Stormwind. His turtle bisque supposedly draws diners from as far away as Darkshire.",al={"southshore food","why is jessen famous","darkshire travel for bisque"},it="fame"},{q="What is the unrest Chef Jessen laments?",a="Hillsbrad and Alterac are caught in open conflict with the Forsaken from the north, Syndicate outlaws in the ruins, and wild predators displaced by Lordaeron's fall. Civilian travel has become dangerous.",al={"hillsbrad unrest","why is it dangerous now","what unrest"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Chef Jessen want this done?",a="Chef Jessen takes immense pride in Southshore's culinary reputation, boasting that the town offers some of the finest cuisine north of Stormwind. His famed secret recipe for Soothing Turtle Bisque attracts travelers from as far away as Darkshire, but recent violence in the region has cut off his ingredient supply. By gathering the necessary turtle meat, you enable him to resume serving his signature dish and bring comfort to the beleaguered town.",al={"why make turtle bisque","chef jessen motive","why does jessen want turtle meat"},it="motive",add="d8a3c1e1"},{q="What is the Turtle Meat for?",a="The meat is the essential ingredient in Chef Jessen's secret recipe for Soothing Turtle Bisque. Harvesters typically gather it from snapjaw turtles found in the northern waters, such as Lake Lordamere, allowing the chef to simmer his beloved regional specialty once again.",al={"what is turtle meat used for","why turtle meat","purpose of turtle meat"},it="item",add="bb599998"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Chef Jessen shares his craft only with fellow cooks, teaching you to prepare your own Soothing Turtle Bisque.",["faction:Alliance"]="Restoring Southshore's comforts helps keep local spirits up as the town stands isolated against Syndicate outlaws and Forsaken expansion.",["race:Human"]="As a human from the southern kingdoms, you may find a rare taste of home and hospitality in Jessen's cooking, here in the embattled north."},kw={"chef jessen","cooking","dalaran","hillsbrad","lordamere lake","snapjaw","soothing turtle bisque","southshore","turtle meat"},rel={"npc:chef-jessen","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","subzone:dalaran","subzone:darkshire","topic:alliance"},m={start="Chef Jessen",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=555,ri={"Turtle Meat"}},src={"Soothing Turtle Bisque (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:556"] = {t="quest",n="Stone Tokens",z="hillsbrad",s="Stone Tokens is a Horde assignment issued by Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill to retrieve magical binding artifacts from Dalaran agents in the Alterac region. The Forsaken seek to study the arcane methods Dalaran's mages use to enslave and command powerful elementals. Gathering these inert tokens serves as the foundation for the Magus's research into elemental subjugation.",h="Stone Tokens is a Horde assignment issued by Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill to retrieve magical binding...",sec={{t="Arcane Subjugation",b="The magi of Dalaran have long possessed a formidable command over elemental entities, using specialized conduits and enchanted foci to bind creatures from other dimensions into servitude. While the city itself is still rebuilding, its agents and remnant forces patrol the surrounding territory, relying on elementals as laborers and defensive shock troops. Magus Voidglare, an arcane researcher working on behalf of the Forsaken in Tarren Mill, seeks to dissect the precise sorcery Dalaran uses to compel these entities into obedience.",sp=0},{t="Inert Specimen Gathering",b="Rather than demanding potent and volatile magical instruments right away, Keeper Bel'varil directs agents to secure worn and faded tokens. By gathering these exhausted charms from Dalaran personnel stationed around the outskirts and the nearby internment camp, Voidglare can safely analyze the lingering enchantments without risking uncontrolled planar backlash. These weathered tokens provide the baseline theoretical knowledge needed before testing more potent binding mechanisms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the stone tokens used for?",a="The wizards of Dalaran craft and carry these stone tokens as magical foci to command and subjugate elementals, forcing creatures from other dimensions to serve as guards, sentries, and laborers.",al={"stone token purpose","why do dalaran wizards have stone tokens","what do the tokens do"},it="item"},{q="Why does Magus Voidglare want worn tokens specifically?",a="Worn stone tokens retain the foundational magical matrix of Dalaran's binding spells while having faded in active arcane power. This makes them far safer for Magus Voidglare to dissect and study without risking violent elemental retaliation or explosive magical feedback during his initial experiments.",al={"why worn stone tokens","why not active tokens"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Keeper Bel'varil?",a="Keeper Bel'varil is a Forsaken questgiver stationed at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He assists the researcher Magus Voidglare by procuring magical artifacts and reagents from nearby territories.",al={"belvaril","who gives stone tokens quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Dalaran forces holding these tokens?",a="The tokens are carried by Dalaran wizards and their personnel occupying the frontier borders between western Hillsbrad and the Alterac Mountains, particularly near Dalaran itself and the nearby ruins of the old orc internment camp.",al={"where to find stone tokens","dalaran forces location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after these tokens are delivered?",a="Once Bel'varil inspects the inert specimens, Magus Voidglare advances his research from theoretical study to physical containment, commissioning the procurement of heavier Bracers of Binding directly from the elementals themselves.",al={"what comes after stone tokens","stone tokens follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Horde studying Dalaran's magic?",a="The Forsaken view the surviving mages of Dalaran as a direct territorial and magical threat in the Lordaeron region. Deciphering their arcane methods allows Forsaken spellcasters to counter Kirin Tor operations, protect their borders, and potentially turn elemental forces to their own advantage.",al={"why horde wants dalaran magic","forsaken dalaran interest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Keeper Bel'varil want these stone tokens collected?",a="Keeper Bel'varil acts on behalf of Magus Voidglare, a Forsaken mage in Tarren Mill seeking to unravel the arcane practices of Dalaran. The Kirin Tor wizards are renowned for their mastery over extra-dimensional elementals, commanding them through enchanted stones. Voidglare intends to study the tokens to unlock their binding secrets, advancing the Forsaken's understanding of elemental control.",al={"why does keeper bel'varil want stone tokens","bel'varil motive stone tokens","why collect worn stone tokens"},it="motive",add="618b6456"},{q="Who are the Dalaran forces guarding the internment camp?",a="You are sent against the Kirin Tor wizards and guards occupying the ruined internment camps and lands west of Hillsbrad, along the Alterac border. In the aftermath of the Third War and Dalaran's destruction, these human remnants maintain a stubborn enclave, utilizing elemental servants and wards to secure their holdings against the Forsaken and other regional threats.",al={"who are dalaran forces hillsbrad","why are dalaran wizards at internment camp","dalaran target stone tokens"},it="target",add="4e88982b"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Dalaran's conjurers are renowned for binding elementals to their will; examining these tokens reveals how human magi tether extraplanar spirits to material foci.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken of Tarren Mill, unraveling Dalaran's arcane secrets is vital to securing Lordaeron from human sorcerers lurking just beyond the walls of Dalaran.",["class:Shaman"]="While shaman revere elementals through reciprocal pacts, Dalaran's wizards use arcane tokens to dominate and enslave them, a practice antithetical to spiritual harmony."},kw={"alterac mountains","binding","dalaran","elementals","hillsbrad foothills","keeper bel'varil","magus voidglare","stone tokens","tarren mill","worn stone token"},rel={"npc:keeper-bel-varil","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dalaran","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac"},m={start="Keeper Bel'varil",level="32",faction="Horde",id=556,ri={"Worn Stone Token"}},src={"Stone Tokens"}}
E["quest:557"] = {t="quest",n="Bracers of Binding",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Keeper Bel'varil looks ahead to what the Magus may need next. The Magus studies the stone tokens you gathered, and Bel'varil sends you to the ruins of Dalaran for four Bracers of Earth Binding.",h="In Tarren Mill, Keeper Bel'varil looks ahead to what the Magus may need next.",sec={{t="Bracers of Earth Binding",b="As the Magus studies the stone tokens you gathered, Keeper Bel'varil expects another need to follow. Bracers of binding are worn on an elemental's wrists, where they bind the creature to a mage's service. Elementals wear them among the ruins of Dalaran. Bel'varil wants you to bring four Bracers of Earth Binding back to Tarren Mill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Keeper Bel'varil in Tarren Mill gives it to you after you gathered the stone tokens.",al={"quest giver","who gives bracers of binding","keeper bel'varil quest"}},{q="What are the bracers used for?",a="Bracers of binding are worn on an elemental's wrists to bind it to a mage's service.",al={"what do bracers of binding do","purpose of bracers","why get bracers"}},{q="Where are the elementals found?",a="You find the elementals in the ruins of Dalaran, in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"elemental location","where to find bracers","where are elemental slaves"}},{q="Why does Keeper Bel'varil want them?",a="Bel'varil expects the Magus will eventually want examples of the bracers, which are the counterpart to the stone tokens the Magus is studying.",al={"why does belvaril want bracers","who wants the bracers"}},{q="What came before this quest?",a="Before this, you gathered the stone tokens in Stone Tokens. The Magus is now studying them.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","stone tokens follow up"}}},kw={"alterac","bel'varil","binding","bracers","dalaran","earth binding","elementals","magus","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:556","npc:keeper-bel-varil","subzone:dalaran","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:mage"},m={start="Keeper Bel'varil",["end"]="Keeper Bel'varil",level="34",faction="Horde",id=557},src={"Bracers of Binding"}}
E["quest:559"] = {t="quest",n="Farren's Proof",z="hillsbrad",s="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle sends Alliance recruits along Southshore's coast to prove his patrol's success. Marshal Redpath wants evidence that the murlocs have been cleared from the Western Strand.",h="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle sends Alliance recruits along Southshore's coast to prove his patrol's success.",sec={{t="A Grudging Request",b="After the first coastal sweeps in Down the Coast, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle faces scrutiny from Marshal Redpath and Southshore's leaders. Farren claims the local murlocs have been cleared, but his superiors want proof. He leaves the grim work to wandering Alliance adventurers and sends them back to the shore for evidence of the kills.",sp=0},{t="Grisly Evidence",b="The Western Strand lies west of Southshore, where coastal murlocs live along the shallows. Farren asks for ten severed murloc heads to satisfy the garrison's officers. He detests the creatures and says their repulsive sight and smell have ruined his appetite for Southshore's chief export and staple food.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Farren Orinelle?",a="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle is an Alliance officer stationed in Southshore. He wants to report success to his superiors and leaves the violent, filthy work of shoreline security to adventurers.",al={"farren orinelle","who gives farren's proof","lieutenant farren"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Farren need severed murloc heads?",a="Marshal Redpath and Southshore's officials wanted physical proof of dead murlocs before accepting reports that the Western Strand had been cleared.",al={"why murloc heads","farren proof reason","why collect heads"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these murlocs located?",a="The murlocs live along the Western Strand, west of Southshore, toward the border of Silverpine Forest.",al={"murloc head location","where is western strand","murloc spots hillsbrad"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after turning in Farren's Proof?",a="Farren asks you to report the murloc deaths to Marshal Redpath. After accepting the proof, Redpath turns his attention to threats on the Eastern Strand and later passes along Stormwind's reassignment orders for Farren.",al={"next quest after farren's proof","farren quest chain","farren's proof followup"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Farren disgusted by the murlocs?",a="Farren finds walking, bipedal fish repulsive. Handling their cold, slimy remains has put him off eating fish, making life in Southshore's fishing community miserable.",al={"farren fish","why doesn't farren like fish"}},{q="Who is Marshal Redpath?",a="Marshal Redpath commands Southshore's town defenses. He holds junior officers like Farren Orinelle accountable for regional security.",al={"captain redpath","who is redpath"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lieutenant Farren have you collect the heads instead of doing it himself?",a="Lieutenant Farren is utterly revulsed by murlocs. While he is quick to take credit for clearing the coastline, the thought of hacking off cold, slimy heads turns his stomach so badly that he hasn't been able to bring himself to eat fish in weeks. He would rather hire an adventurer to endure the grisly butchery than soil his own hands.",al={"why does farren need me","why doesnt farren get the heads","farren proof why me"},it="why_me",add="fff9ab4a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help secure Southshore's coast against native predators, leaving the outpost to focus on threats from the Syndicate and the Horde.",["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook in Southshore, you may find Farren's aversion to seafood baffling. Fighting along the beach can also yield spare raw catches."},kw={"farren","heads","hillsbrad","murloc","orinelle","redpath","southshore","strand"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:536","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:murloc","quest:562","quest:563","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=559,ri={"Murloc Head"}},src={"Farren's Proof"}}
E["quest:560"] = {t="quest",n="Farren's Proof",z="hillsbrad",s="At Southshore, Farren's Proof brings Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's report to Marshal Redpath. The murloc heads prove the work is done, though Farren will not carry them himself.",h="At Southshore, Farren's Proof brings Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's report to Marshal Redpath.",sec={{t="A Squeamish Officer",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle patrols and secures Hillsbrad Foothills' southern coast, but the brutal work of frontier warfare turns his stomach. After you cull the murlocs along the beaches, he cannot bring himself to touch the severed heads you bring back as proof. He sends you across Southshore to deliver them to the town's command.",sp=0},{t="Report to Redpath",b="Marshal Redpath oversees Southshore's defenses and military readiness as threats rise from Tarren Mill and wild beasts. He receives the sack of murloc heads from you instead of directly from Farren. Redpath knows you have become Farren's errand runner, but accepts the help. Southshore needs every willing hand to keep its borders safe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Lieutenant Farren deliver the murloc heads himself?",a="Lieutenant Farren has no wish to handle a sack of severed murloc heads. After sending you to fight, he leaves the delivery to you as well.",al={"why farren not go","farren proof why deliver","why errand boy"},it="why_me"},{q="Who is Marshal Redpath?",a="Marshal Redpath is Southshore's senior Alliance military commander. He oversees local defense, coordinates the town guards, and handles threats to the human settlement in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who is redpath","marshal redpath lore","southshore marshal"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this delivery lead next in the quest chain?",a="The delivery leads to more duties from Marshal Redpath and Lieutenant Farren, then official dispatches about troop deployments and paperwork sent to Stormwind.",al={"what comes next","farren's proof next quest","redpath next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are murlocs a priority for Southshore's garrison?",a="Murloc tribes gather densely along Hillsbrad's beaches. They threaten coastal supply routes, harass local fishermen, and endanger Southshore's southern approach while the town faces the Forsaken to the north.",al={"why kill murlocs","murloc problem southshore","hillsbrad murlocs"},it="danger"},{q="What does Marshal Redpath think of Lieutenant Farren's conduct?",a="Marshal Redpath knows Farren's habits and dryly remarks that you have become Farren's errand runner. He welcomes the help because Southshore is hard-pressed and needs capable hands.",al={"redpath opinion on farren","does redpath like farren"}},{q="Where is Marshal Redpath located in Southshore?",a="Marshal Redpath is near Southshore's town center and council building, overseeing the settlement's daily defenses.",al={"find redpath","where is marshal redpath","redpath location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Lieutenant Farren want the murloc heads delivered to Marshal Redpath?",a="Lieutenant Farren needs concrete proof that the murloc threat along Southshore's coast is actively being dealt with. Presenting the severed heads to Marshal Redpath demonstrates that Farren's patrol orders are being carried out and Southshore's shores are being defended, even if the lieutenant would rather avoid carting a foul-smelling sack across town himself.",al={"farren motive","why deliver murloc heads","farren's proof purpose"},it="motive",add="8013187e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every small duty in Southshore helps keep the Alliance's main stronghold in Lordaeron fortified against threats from the north and sea.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you see the strained bureaucracy and frontier weariness of Hillsbrad's garrison in your dealings with Farren and Redpath."},kw={"alliance","errand boy","farren orinelle","farren's proof","hillsbrad foothills","marshal redpath","murloc heads","southshore"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:559","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:536","quest:562","quest:563","topic:murloc"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",["end"]="Marshal Redpath",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=560},src={"Farren's Proof (2)"}}
E["quest:561"] = {t="quest",n="Farren's Proof",z="hillsbrad",s="At Southshore, Farren's Proof carries Marshal Redpath's orders to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle. The Marshal wants him to turn his attention to the naga pressing along the Eastern Strand.",h="At Southshore, Farren's Proof carries Marshal Redpath's orders to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle.",sec={{t="A Shift in Command",b="Marshal Redpath sends word across Southshore to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle. Fresh reports speak of naga incursions on the Eastern Strand, and the Marshal wants Orinelle to focus on that threat. He orders the lieutenant to set aside other concerns, drive back the naga, and report his progress in person.",sp=0},{t="Rivalry on the Coast",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle suspects Marshal Redpath wants credit for calming the Eastern Strand. He believes Redpath is using intelligence they both received to claim the work of the garrison. Unwilling to let his commander earn a promotion through his soldiers' labor, Orinelle begins devising another way to win favor with the crown.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this delivery?",a="Marshal Redpath's orders redirect Lieutenant Farren Orinelle's attention to the naga on Hillsbrad's Eastern Strand and require him to report progress directly to the Marshal.",al={"what does redpath want","why send message to farren","farren proof 3 objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Farren Orinelle react bitterly to Redpath's orders?",a="Orinelle believes Redpath is acting on the same military intelligence they both received. He fears the Marshal means to claim credit for clearing the coast and gain a promotion through Orinelle's hard work.",al={"farren redpath rivalry","why is orinelle mad","orinelle promotion"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is the Eastern Strand located?",a="The Eastern Strand runs along the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, southeast of Southshore, where naga have made encampments on the sand.",al={"eastern strand location","where are the naga","hillsbrad coast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What comes next after delivering this message?",a="After the delivery, Orinelle devises his own scheme instead of simply following Redpath's authority. His plan sends couriers down the coast toward high command in 'Stormwind Ho!'.",al={"next quest","what happens next","stormwind ho follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the leaders involved in this exchange?",a="Marshal Redpath commands Southshore's garrison, and Lieutenant Farren Orinelle serves under him as a field lieutenant overseeing coastal defense.",al={"who are farren and redpath","southshore officers","farren orinelle and redpath"},it="leader"},{q="Does this assignment require any combat?",a="No. The delivery is an exchange between officers in Southshore, though it concerns the military response to naga along the shore.",al={"is there fighting","do i fight naga","farrens proof combat"},gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Redpath send you to Lieutenant Farren?",a="Marshal Redpath oversees Southshore's defense and wants Lieutenant Farren Orinelle to stop wasting time on murlocs and turn his attention to the naga threatening the Eastern Strand. He needs Farren to produce real tactical results and answer directly to him rather than pursuing petty personal initiatives.",al={"why does redpath send this message","redpath motive farren","why refocus on naga"},it="motive",add="4fc43d37"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The exchange reveals rivalries over rank and recognition within Southshore's garrison, even as the northern outpost faces threats.",["class:Warrior"]="As an Alliance warrior, you may recognize the strain between proving yourself in battle and navigating officers' ambitions."},kw={"eastern strand","farren orinelle","farren's proof","hillsbrad","marshal redpath","naga","promotion","southshore"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:562","quest:559","subzone:southshore","subzone:eastern-strand","zone:hillsbrad","topic:naga","quest:536"},m={start="Marshal Redpath",["end"]="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=561},src={"Farren's Proof (3)"}}
E["quest:562"] = {t="quest",n="Stormwind Ho!",z="hillsbrad",s="Alliance High Command fears the naga threat, and Stormwind Ho! gives Farren Orinelle a chance to leave Southshore. He hopes to take credit for their defeat and win a reassignment to Stormwind City.",h="Alliance High Command fears the naga threat, and Stormwind Ho!",sec={{t="A Ticket Out of Southshore",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle finds his Southshore posting miserable. The town sits on Lordaeron’s edge, hemmed in by Forsaken forces, syndicate brigands, and sea fiends. A city guardsman used to drunks and petty brawls in Stormwind, Farren longs to return south. His former mentor tells him Alliance High Command is increasingly anxious about naga encroaching on the coasts. Farren sees a chance to leave the north behind.",sp=0},{t="Stolen Valor on the Coast",b="Farren admits he lacks the courage and skill to face Daggerspine sirens and shorehunters in open combat. He commissions you to scour the beaches southeast of Southshore and cull the naga ranks. He needs your martial feats to write an impressive dispatch to Major Samuelson in Stormwind, and hopes the credit will help him secure a reassignment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Farren Orinelle want to kill the naga?",a="Farren wants to escape Southshore, not because he personally cares about the naga. His mentor told him Alliance High Command fears their rising threat, so success against them could bring promotion or a transfer back to Stormwind City.",al={"why naga","farren motive","why kill naga in southshore"},it="motive"},{q="Can Lieutenant Farren Orinelle fight the naga himself?",a="No. Farren is an urban guardsman used to breaking up drunken tavern brawls and arresting rowdy beggars. The savage Daggerspine naga frighten him, so he relies on visiting adventurers to fight them.",al={"why doesn't farren fight","is farren weak","farren combat"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the Daggerspine naga located?",a="Daggerspine shorehunters and sirens have encampments along the coast southeast of Southshore. They prowl the shores of the Great Sea in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"where are naga","daggerspine location","southshore naga beach"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Major Samuelson?",a="Major Samuelson is Farren Orinelle’s former mentor in the Stormwind City Guard. Farren hopes Samuelson will pull the strings to secure his transfer south as he prepares a report about the naga.",al={"major samuelson","samuelson stormwind","who gets the letter"},it="people"},{q="What happens after completing this task?",a="After the naga threat is reduced, Farren takes credit for your work and sends you south to Stormwind Keep. You deliver his report and reassignment plea to Major Samuelson in person.",al={"what comes next","next quest after stormwind ho","reassignment quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Farren hate Southshore so much?",a="Farren sees Southshore as a dangerous frontier outpost, far from Stormwind’s safety. With undead neighbors and coastal monsters all around, he bitterly calls it a “Light-forsaken port.”",al={"why does farren hate southshore","light forsaken port"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Daggerspine naga threatening Southshore?",a="The Daggerspine are serpentine monstrous humanoids encroaching along the eastern coastline of Hillsbrad Foothills. Alliance High Command has grown increasingly alarmed by their organized presence along the shores. Ferocious shorehunters patrol the beaches alongside sirens wielding ocean magics, harassing the regional fisheries and threatening to overwhelm Southshore's fragile defenses if left unchecked.",al={"daggerspine naga","who are the naga in southshore","daggerspine shorehunters"},it="target",add="d5622c58"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance command in Hillsbrad is stretched thin, leaving ordinary city watchmen out of their depth against monstrous threats like the Daggerspine naga.",["race:Human"]="As a human serving in Lordaeron, you see Southshore as a grim reminder of lost northern glory, far from Stormwind’s rebuilt grandeur and safety."},kw={"daggerspine","farren orinelle","hillsbrad foothills","naga","reassignment","samuelson","southshore","stormwind ho"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","quest:563","quest:559","npc:major-samuelson","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:naga","zone:stormwind"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=562},src={"Stormwind Ho!"}}
E["quest:563"] = {t="quest",n="Reassignment",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle seeks a way back to Stormwind. He has compiled an exaggerated report of his deeds against the coastal naga and sends an adventurer to Stormwind Keep to deliver it to his former mentor, Major Samuelson.",h="In Southshore, Lieutenant Farren Orinelle seeks a way back to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Ticket Out of Southshore",b="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle resents his posting in the Hillsbrad Foothills. In Southshore, far from the capital and under Marshal Redpath's stern watch, he spends his days plotting a transfer south. He takes credit for clearing out the nearby Daggerspine naga to make himself look like an indispensable, battle-hardened officer ready for promotion.",sp=0},{t="Keep Connections",b="Farren wants a transfer without drawing Marshal Redpath's suspicion, so he goes around the local chain of command. He turns to Major Samuelson, a senior officer in Stormwind Keep who mentored him in the past. A report delivered straight to Samuelson puts Farren's claimed deeds before someone with authority over garrison assignments.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucracy at Work",b="Major Samuelson receives the dossier in Stormwind Keep and gives mild approval to his former pupil's initiative against the naga menace. But military decisions move slowly. He promises only to weigh the report during next month's routine personnel review, leaving Farren's future in Southshore uncertain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Farren Orinelle want a reassignment?",a="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle wants to leave Southshore, a remote northern outpost he sees as dull, dangerous, and beneath him. He longs for Stormwind City's relative luxury and safety, and hopes his reports on the naga will justify a transfer.",al={"why leave southshore","farren motive","why does farren want to leave"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Major Samuelson?",a="Major Samuelson is a senior officer in Stormwind Keep who oversees city guard assignments. He mentored Lieutenant Farren Orinelle during Farren's early career in the capital.",al={"who is samuelson","samuelson lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Farren deliver the report himself?",a="Farren is on active duty in Southshore and cannot leave his post without permission. He is also trying to bypass Marshal Redpath, his immediate superior, who would likely obstruct a transfer request made for Farren's own benefit.",al={"why do i have to deliver it","why not deliver himself"},it="why_me"},{q="Did Farren actually defeat the naga himself?",a="No. Farren sent adventurers to kill Daggerspine naga along the Eastern Strand, then used their success in the report backing his request for reassignment.",al={"did farren kill naga","farren report truth"},it="history"},{q="Does Farren actually get transferred back to Stormwind?",a="Not immediately. Major Samuelson promises only to consider the report at next month's personnel review. Farren remains stationed in Southshore for the foreseeable future as the kingdom's military bureaucracy turns slowly.",al={"does farren get reassigned","does transfer work"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Major Samuelson located?",a="Major Samuelson is inside Stormwind Keep, the fortress at the heart of Stormwind City, where the high command and regency council reside.",al={"samuelson location","where is major samuelson"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The delivery shows the everyday politics of the Alliance military, where frontier garrisons such as Southshore can be far from the ambitions of officers hoping to return to Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="The delivery shows the divide between human refugees and defenders holding the line in Lordaeron and the political maneuvering inside Stormwind Keep's high halls."},kw={"daggerspine","farren orinelle","major samuelson","reassignment","redpath","southshore","stormwind keep"},rel={"quest:562","npc:lieutenant-farren-orinelle","npc:major-samuelson","subzone:southshore","subzone:stormwind-keep","quest:559","quest:536","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Lieutenant Farren Orinelle",["end"]="Major Samuelson",level="32",faction="Alliance",id=563},src={"Reassignment"}}
E["quest:564"] = {t="quest",n="Costly Menace",z="hillsbrad",s="In Southshore, Darren Malvew fears the mountain lions coming down from Alterac. Undead, the Syndicate gang, and other scoundrels have cost the town horses, but Darren says the lions are the greatest threat.",h="In Southshore, Darren Malvew fears the mountain lions coming down from Alterac.",sec={{t="Horses Lost",b="Darren Malvew of Southshore cannot bear losing the town's beautiful horses. Undead, the Syndicate gang, and scoundrels in the region have already cost the town quite a few. Darren says the greatest danger comes from mountain lions in Alterac, which keep descending from the hills.",sp=0},{t="Lions of the Hills",b="Darren wants eight Mountain Lions and ten Hulking Mountain Lions dealt with. Mountain Lions are found in the lower hills of the Alterac Mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Darren Malvew?",a="Darren Malvew lives in Southshore, in Hillsbrad Foothills, and is tired of losing the town's horses.",al={"darren malvew","who gives costly menace","darren malvew southshore horses"}},{q="Where are the mountain lions coming from?",a="The mountain lions come down from the hills of Alterac. Mountain Lions are found in the lower hills of the Alterac Mountains.",al={"mountain lion location","where are mountain lions","where to find lions"}},{q="What threats to the horses does Darren mention?",a="Undead, the Syndicate gang, and other scoundrels in the region have cost Southshore horses, but Darren says the mountain lions of Alterac are the greatest threat.",al={"southshore threats","what attacks southshore horses","darren malvew enemies"}},{q="What specific beasts need to be culled?",a="Eight Mountain Lions and ten Hulking Mountain Lions.",al={"which lions to kill","hulking mountain lion costly menace","costly menace targets"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","costly menace","darren malvew","hillsbrad foothills","horses","hulking mountain lion","mountain lion","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","topic:syndicate"},m={start="Darren Malvew",["end"]="Darren Malvew",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=564},src={"Costly Menace"}}
E["quest:566"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Baron Vardus",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia calls for Baron Vardus's death. The human is a high-ranking member of the Syndicate, wanted for crimes against the Forsaken; bring proof of his death to Darthalia.",h="In Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia calls for Baron Vardus's death.",sec={{t="A Price on the Baron",b="High Executor Darthalia has put a price on Baron Vardus, a human accused of crimes against the Forsaken and counted among the Syndicate's high-ranking members. The last word placed him in the Uplands of the Alterac Mountains, north of Tarren Mill. Darthalia's order calls for his death, and payment awaits whoever brings her proof.",sp=0},{t="Where He Might Be",b="Baron Vardus may be at any of the Syndicate camps across the Uplands. He may also be hiding in the cellar of the inn at Strahnbrad.",sp=0},{t="Darthalia's Verdict",b="With Baron Vardus dead, High Executor Darthalia declares that the Syndicate's leaders are fewer. She expects their anger and resistance to be short-lived.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Baron Vardus?",a="Baron Vardus is a human and a high-ranking member of the Syndicate, wanted for crimes against the Forsaken.",al={"baron vardus","who is vardus","who is the baron"}},{q="Where can Baron Vardus be found?",a="Baron Vardus was last seen north of Tarren Mill, in the Uplands of the Alterac Mountains. He may be at one of the Syndicate camps there or hiding in the cellar of the Strahnbrad inn.",al={"baron vardus location","where is vardus","find baron vardus"}},{q="Who offers the bounty on Baron Vardus?",a="High Executor Darthalia offers the bounty on Baron Vardus. Bring proof of his death to her in Tarren Mill.",al={"who posted the bounty","who wants vardus dead","darthalia bounty"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","baron vardus","darthalia","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad foothills","strahnbrad","syndicate","tarren mill","uplands","vardus"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:uplands","subzone:strahnbrad","zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","topic:forsaken"},m={start="WANTED",["end"]="High Executor Darthalia",level="40",faction="Horde",id=566},src={"WANTED: Baron Vardus"}}
E["quest:567"] = {t="quest",n="Dangerous!",z="hillsbrad",s="At Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia has marked four Hillsbrad humans for execution. She calls them enemies of the Forsaken for killing their people and striking at supplies.",h="At Tarren Mill, High Executor Darthalia has marked four Hillsbrad humans for execution.",sec={{t="A Matter of Retribution",b="Across the Hillsbrad Foothills, the fighting is brutal and personal. High Executor Darthalia and the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill see ordinary Hillsbrad citizens as deadly foes. A wanted notice names four people whose resistance has killed Forsaken and cost them valuable shipments from the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Targets of Tarren Mill",b="The bounty names Clerk Horrace Whitesteed, who killed Deathguard Toma; Citizen Wilkes, who murdered Apothecary Eli; Miner Hackett, who killed Deathstalker Fry; and Farmer Kalaba, who sabotaged supply convoys from the Undercity. Each works from a different pocket of Hillsbrad resistance and remains elusive amid the wider conflict.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the Dangerous! bounty?",a="High Executor Darthalia, commander of the Forsaken forces at Tarren Mill, issued the bounty against four prominent Hillsbrad humans.",al={"who posted dangerous","who gave dangerous quest","darthalia bounty"},it="identity"},{q="Why are these specific humans wanted?",a="Each has struck the Forsaken: Clerk Horrace Whitesteed killed Deathguard Toma, Citizen Wilkes murdered Apothecary Eli, Miner Hackett killed Deathstalker Fry, and Farmer Kalaba ambushed essential supplies from the Undercity.",al={"why are they dangerous","what did they do","hillsbrad targets crime"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the targets located?",a="All four are scattered across Hillsbrad Foothills, among the human settlements, farms, and mines.",al={"where to find targets","dangerous quest locations","hackett location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the strategic purpose of this contract?",a="The contract answers the killings and aims to cripple local human resistance, protecting Forsaken patrols and supply lines between Tarren Mill and the Undercity.",al={"why kill them","hillsbrad bounty goal","tarren mill strategy"},it="purpose"},{q="Does this connect to the Battle of Hillsbrad?",a="Yes. The targets live in the farms, mines, and town centers Forsaken forces assault during the wider Battle of Hillsbrad offensive.",al={"battle of hillsbrad connection","darthalia battle","hillsbrad offensive"},it="conflict"},{q="Who turns in the bounty once they are slain?",a="Bring proof of their deaths directly to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill.",al={"who completes dangerous","dangerous turn in","darthalia turn in"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia want these four humans eliminated?",a="High Executor Darthalia posted the bounty because these four individuals struck direct, crippling blows against Tarren Mill's key operations. Clerk Whitesteed, Citizen Wilkes, and Miner Hackett each assassinated vital Forsaken personnel—a Deathguard, an Apothecary, and a Deathstalker scout. Farmer Kalaba intercepted crucial supply caravans arriving from the Undercity. Eliminating them avenges fallen comrades, secures the supply lines, and removes dangerous guerrilla threats from the Hillsbrad front.",al={"why kill them","darthalia motive","why are they wanted dead"},it="motive",add="ed73acb1"},{q="Who are the targets marked on the Dangerous! bounty?",a="Your targets are four influential Hillsbrad residents who have taken up arms against the Forsaken: Clerk Horrace Whitesteed, Citizen Wilkes, Miner Hackett, and Farmer Kalaba. While they appear to be ordinary townsfolk, miners, and laborers, each has proven exceptionally deadly and resourceful, operating from concealment across the foothills and fields to wage irregular warfare against Tarren Mill.",al={"who are the targets","dangerous bounty targets","who to kill"},it="target",add="4592bc02"},{q="Why does High Executor Darthalia rely on adventurers instead of her own Deathguards?",a="Tarren Mill's military forces are already stretched thin holding defensive perimeters and waging pitched skirmishes across Hillsbrad. Furthermore, the targets are not marching in the open; they have gone into hiding across civilian farms, mines, and backroads. Darthalia relies on roving bounty hunters and capable adventurers who can move independently, track down evasive targets, and root them out behind enemy lines without drawing away entire garrison units.",al={"why not use guards","why me dangerous","why send adventurers"},it="why_me",add="7da50b6a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, avenging fallen Deathguards, Apothecaries, and Deathstalkers is a grim point of pride for a loyal servant of the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help secure Hillsbrad Foothills by breaking the human militia's fiercest figures and making Horde movements through the region safer.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, tracking concealed leaders in hostile territory echoes the covert work of Deathstalker Fry, whose death this contract avenges."},kw={"apothecary eli","citizen wilkes","clerk horrace whitesteed","dangerous","deathguard toma","deathstalker fry","farmer kalaba","high executor darthalia","hillsbrad","miner hackett","tarren mill","undercity"},rel={"npc:high-executor-darthalia","subzone:tarren-mill","quest:527","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity"},m={start="Dangerous!",level="28",faction="Horde",id=567},src={"Dangerous! (quest)"}}
E["quest:657"] = {t="quest",n="Hints of a New Plague?",z="hillsbrad",s="Kinelory needs your protection while she seeks Jorell’s remaining research at Go'Shek Farm. Quae has learned from the folder that Apothecary Jorell is conducting deadly experiments there, but she is too hurt to help after clashing with orcs.",h="Kinelory needs your protection while she seeks Jorell’s remaining research at Go'Shek Farm.",sec={{t="Jorell's Experiments",b="The folder reveals Jorell’s deadly experiments at Go'Shek Farm. Quae does not know how they affect Hillsbrad, but Phin would not want them to continue. Some of Jorell’s research has already reached Tarren Mill.",sp=0},{t="Kinelory's Protector",b="Quae clashed with some orcs while you were away and cannot help Kinelory. Kinelory plans to go to the farm and steal the research Jorell has not yet sent to Tarren Mill. She will need your protection.",sp=0},{t="Kinelory's Resolve",b="Kinelory says she will destroy every one of the Forsaken herself if that brings Phin peace. Since the plague, Phin has done so much for Kinelory and the others, who never thought they would find friends or family again. Kinelory asks you to tell her when you are ready, and you will set out together right away.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why can't Quae accompany Kinelory?",a="Quae clashed with some orcs while you were away and is in no shape to help Kinelory.",al={"why is quae staying","why won't quae help","why escort kinelory alone"}},{q="What was discovered in the folder?",a="The folder reveals that Apothecary Jorell is conducting deadly experiments at Go'Shek Farm.",al={"what was in the folder","jorell experiments","what is jorell doing"}},{q="Why are Quae and Kinelory investigating this?",a="Quae and Kinelory are Phin’s companions. Phin leads a band of adventurers investigating odd happenings and would not want Jorell’s experiments to continue.",al={"who is phin","why do they care about the plague","why help phin"}},{q="Where is the research being sent?",a="Some of Jorell’s research has already gone to Tarren Mill. Kinelory plans to steal what he has not yet sent.",al={"where are the notes going","tarren mill research"}}},kw={"apothecary jorell","forsaken","go'shek farm","kinelory","phin","plague","quae","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","topic:forsaken","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Quae",["end"]="Kinelory",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=657},src={"Hints of a New Plague? (3)"}}
E["quest:658"] = {t="quest",n="Hints of a New Plague?",z="hillsbrad",s="At Go'Shek Farm, Quae and Kin have watched for days. Kin saw a courier leave a small house to the south, and they suspect she carries notes to Tarren Mill. Quae asks if you are a skilled tracker and wants the documents.",h="At Go'Shek Farm, Quae and Kin have watched for days.",sec={{t="Watching the Farm",b="Quae expected Phin Odelic to send you, since he worries too much. Quae and Kin have watched the farm for days. Kin recently saw a courier leave a small house to the south. Kin talks often, but Quae trusts Kin's senses in dangerous places.",sp=0},{t="The Courier's Folder",b="Quae asks if you are a skilled tracker. The courier may carry notes bound for Tarren Mill, and the documents could shed light on what is happening in Hillsbrad. You are to find the Forsaken Courier and bring her Sealed Folder to Quae near Go'Shek Farm. While you search, Kin spots an apothecary leaving that same house. Quae suspects the apothecary is up to no good, but needs proof before anyone acts rashly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sent you to find Quae and Kin?",a="Phin Odelic sent you to check on Quae and Kin. Quae expected it, since Phin worries too much.",al={"who sent me to quae","who started hints of a new plague","phin odelic quest"}},{q="Where did the courier come from?",a="Kin saw the courier leave a small house to the south.",al={"where is the courier from","courier location","house south of farm"}},{q="Where is the courier heading?",a="Quae and Kin suspect the courier carries notes bound for Tarren Mill.",al={"courier destination","where is courier going"}},{q="What item are you sent to retrieve?",a="You are to bring the Forsaken Courier's Sealed Folder to Quae near Go'Shek Farm.",al={"what item does the courier have","sealed folder"}},{q="Who else was spotted at the house?",a="While you were away, Kin spotted an apothecary leaving the same house to the south.",al={"apothecary at the farm","who came out of the house"}},{q="Why does Quae want the documents?",a="The documents might shed light on what is happening in Hillsbrad. Quae needs proof before anyone acts rashly.",al={"why get the documents","what are the notes for"}}},kw={"apothecary","arathi highlands","forsaken courier","go'shek farm","kin","phin odelic","quae","sealed folder","tarren mill"},rel={"quest:657","subzone:go-shek-farm","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Quae",["end"]="Quae",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=658},src={"Hints of a New Plague? (2)"}}
E["quest:659"] = {t="quest",n="Hints of a New Plague?",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad, Phin Odelic's companions search for signs of trouble. Quae and Kinelory have been missing for days since heading to Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands.",h="In Hillsbrad, Phin Odelic's companions search for signs of trouble.",sec={{t="Odd Happenings",b="Phin Odelic's cousin in Hillsbrad had to put down his dog, Stanley. The beast had mystically grown huge and savagely attacked anyone who came near. Phin believes the undead are involved in these odd happenings, and his band searches for signs to prove it.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Companions",b="Quae and Kinelory, Phin Odelic's companions, headed to Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands. They have not checked in for days, and Phin fears for them. He wants you to find them near the farm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Phin Odelic?",a="Phin Odelic leads a band of adventurers investigating odd happenings in the area.",al={"phin odelic","who gives hints of a new plague","quest giver"}},{q="What happened to Stanley?",a="Stanley was Phin's cousin's dog in Hillsbrad. The beast mystically grew huge and attacked anyone who came near, so the cousin put him down.",al={"stanley dog","what happened to the dog","stanley hillsbrad"}},{q="Where are Quae and Kinelory supposed to be?",a="Quae and Kinelory set out for Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands. Phin has heard nothing from them for days.",al={"where is quae","where is kinelory","quae location","find quae"}},{q="Why is Phin investigating?",a="Phin believes the undead are involved in the odd happenings, and his band searches for signs to prove it.",al={"why go shek farm","go shek farm undead","investigate go shek"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","go'shek farm","hillsbrad foothills","kinelory","phin odelic","quae","stanley"},rel={"subzone:go-shek-farm","zone:arathi","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Phin Odelic",["end"]="Quae",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=659},src={"Hints of a New Plague?"}}
E["quest:660"] = {t="quest",n="Hints of a New Plague?",z="hillsbrad",s="Kinelory is ready to return to Quae, and asks you to go with her to the farm. She fears the undead may harm Hillsbrad while they wait, and she needs you to see her safely back.",h="Kinelory is ready to return to Quae, and asks you to go with her to the farm.",sec={{t="Watching Kinelory's Back",b="Kinelory is ready to act after the earlier steps of the investigation. She asks you to go with her down to the farm, then see her safely back to Quae. Anyone who cares about the people of Hillsbrad is urged to protect her.",sp=0},{t="A Safe Return",b="Quae thanks you when Kinelory returns. Quae admits to hoping Kinelory was not too much of a handful: Kinelory is very friendly, but just as deadly when you are her enemy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this escort?",a="Kinelory asks you to go with her when she is ready to set out.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","who starts hints of a new plague 4"}},{q="Where does Kinelory need to go?",a="Kinelory goes down to a farm, then makes her way back to Quae.",al={"escort route","where does kinelory go","kinelory destination"}},{q="Who do you report to when finished?",a="You report to Quae once Kinelory has made it back to her.",al={"turn in","who completes quest","where to turn in"}},{q="What came right before this part of the investigation?",a="The third part of Hints of a New Plague? leads straight into this part of the investigation.",al={"previous quest","prereq","what comes before"}},{q="What follows after returning safely?",a="The investigation continues with the fifth part of Hints of a New Plague?.",al={"next quest","what comes next","follow up"}},{q="Why must Kinelory be protected?",a="Anyone who cares about the people of Hillsbrad is urged to see Kinelory safely through.",al={"why protect kinelory","why care about kinelory"}}},kw={"escort","hillsbrad foothills","hints of a new plague","kinelory","plague","quae"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Kinelory",["end"]="Quae",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=660},src={"Hints of a New Plague? (4)"}}
E["quest:661"] = {t="quest",n="Hints of a New Plague?",z="hillsbrad",s="In Arathi, Quae and Kinelory stay while you carry news to Southshore. Quae has the items from the farm, and Kinelory has returned safely.",h="In Arathi, Quae and Kinelory stay while you carry news to Southshore.",sec={{t="Word for Southshore",b="Quae is pleased with how you cared for Kinelory. She says Kinelory is in better shape than after a night at the tavern. The items from the farm should help Phin Odelic understand what is happening in Arathi. Since the farm was attacked, Quae and Kinelory plan to stay there a little longer in case anyone retaliates. They ask you to return to Southshore and speak with Phin.",sp=0},{t="Phin's Answer",b="Phin is glad to hear that Quae and Kinelory are alive and well. He calls them irreplaceable friends and travelling companions. On behalf of the whole group, Phin thanks you with a gift. He hopes that, with luck, they will learn what the Forsaken are planning and bring it to an end.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Phin Odelic?",a="Quae asks you to go to Southshore once Kinelory is safely back from the farm.",al={"who gives hints of a new plague 5","who starts hints of a new plague","quae quest"}},{q="Why aren't Quae and Kinelory returning to Southshore themselves?",a="Quae and Kinelory plan to stay in Arathi a little longer in case anyone retaliates for the attack on the farm.",al={"why is quae staying in arathi","why stay behind","quae staying"}},{q="Where can Phin Odelic be found?",a="Phin Odelic is in Southshore.",al={"phin odelic location","where is phin","phin odelic southshore"}},{q="What is the purpose of bringing news to Phin Odelic?",a="The items Kinelory brought from the farm should help Phin Odelic understand what is happening in Arathi.",al={"why visit phin","phin odelic purpose","what does phin want"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","forsaken","hillsbrad","kinelory","phin odelic","plague","quae","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","topic:forsaken","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Quae",["end"]="Phin Odelic",level="37",faction="Alliance",id=661},src={"Hints of a New Plague? (5)"}}
E["quest:676"] = {t="quest",n="The Hammer May Fall",z="hillsbrad",s="Tallow sends fighters from Tarren Mill across the mountains to relieve Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. Before reporting to Drum Fel, you prove your battle readiness against Boulderfist ogres near the ruins of Stromgarde.",h="Tallow sends fighters from Tarren Mill across the mountains to relieve Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Gruff Summons",b="In Tarren Mill, Tallow has little patience for untested fighters wandering the Foothills. While recruits stand idle, allies are under attack far away. He sends capable fighters east through Thoradin's Wall into the Arathi Highlands, where Hammerfall is besieged from several sides. Tallow wants them to prove their worth against a strong foe before he sends them to the outpost.",sp=0},{t="Trial by Boulderfist",b="Tallow demands a display of strength at the ogre mound northeast of the ruins of Stromgarde. Boulderfist ogres and their enforcers hold much of Arathi, threatening travelers on the highland trails. Fighting them thins the hostile forces flanking the road and proves you can stand against the danger before reaching Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Hammerfall",b="After the Boulderfist camp is cleared, the road leads northeast to Hammerfall, named for Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. Commander Drum Fel receives the new arrivals with weary skepticism. Whether Tallow meant to strengthen the garrison or send fools to their deaths, Drum Fel quickly turns proven fighters toward the skirmishes threatening the outpost.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this quest begin and end?",a="Tallow offers this assignment in Tarren Mill, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. After you defeat the required ogres in the Arathi Highlands, you report to Drum Fel at Hammerfall, the Horde outpost.",al={"where do i start the hammer may fall","quest turn in location","who gives the hammer may fall"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where are the Boulderfist ogres located?",a="The Boulderfist ogres live at a prominent dirt mound and camp northeast of the ruins of Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"boulderfist ogre location","where are the ogres in arathi","boulderfist mound"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the outpost of Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is a fortified Horde settlement in northeastern Arathi Highlands. It honors former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell nearby during the liberation of the orc internment camps.",al={"what is hammerfall","hammerfall lore","who founded hammerfall"},it="place"},{q="Why does Tallow make you fight ogres before reporting to Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is under constant attack and desperate for capable fighters. Tallow sends you against the Boulderfist ogres to prove you can fight before you reinforce Drum Fel, rather than arrive as a burden.",al={"why kill ogres first","tallow motive","why test me"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Drum Fel?",a="Drum Fel is a veteran orc warrior and commander at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. He organizes defenses against hostile wildlife, ogres, trolls, and Alliance remnants.",al={"drum fel identity","hammerfall commander","who is drum fel"},it="identity"},{q="What follows this assignment?",a="Reporting to Drum Fel leads to the Call to Arms campaign, a series of military operations against surrounding threats, including the Witherbark troll tribes threatening the highlands.",al={"next quest","hammer may fall followup","what comes after"},it="next_step"},{q="Who are the Boulderfist ogres you are sent against?",a="The Boulderfist tribe is a brutish clan of ogres claiming territory across the Arathi Highlands, centered around their mound northeast of the ruins of Stromgarde. Fierce, stubborn, and physically imposing, they dominate the highlands' rocky hills and contest the surrounding territory. Tallow sends you to their mound to see if you can survive their frontline enforcers, ensuring you have the strength required before you throw yourself into the meat grinder of the Arathi war zone.",al={"boulderfist ogres","who are boulderfist","ogres arathi"},it="target",add="b3b0715a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This assignment carries you from Hillsbrad's local disputes into the wider defense of the Arathi Highlands, where Hammerfall holds a vital foothold.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Hammerfall carries deep meaning and history. It was founded where Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer gave his life during the liberation campaigns.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face hulking Boulderfist enforcers to prove yourself to veteran orc commanders like Drum Fel."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist enforcer","boulderfist ogre","drum fel","hammerfall","hillsbrad foothills","stromgarde","tallow","tarren mill","the hammer may fall"},rel={"npc:tallow","npc:drum-fel","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:arathi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:troll"},m={start="Tallow",["end"]="Drum Fel",level="32",faction="Horde",id=676},src={"The Hammer May Fall"}}
E["quest:7162"] = {t="quest",n="Proving Grounds",z="hillsbrad",s="In Alterac, recruits face a trial before joining the Stormpike Guard. Lieutenant Haggerdin sends them into Icewing Caverns to recover a planted battle standard. Success earns an official Stormpike Insignia and begins their rise through the expedition’s ranks.",h="In Alterac, recruits face a trial before joining the Stormpike Guard.",sec={{t="A Measure of Courage",b="The Stormpike Guard fights the Frostwolf Clan in Alterac Valley. Lieutenant Haggerdin directs Alliance forces from their encampment in the Alterac Mountains. He tests new recruits before sending them to the battlefield, demanding proof of skill and nerve in Icewing Caverns, southwest of Dun Baldar.",sp=0},{t="The Icewing Caverns",b="A Stormpike banner waits deep in the icy tunnels of Icewing Caverns. Frost harpies nest in the frozen recesses and attack unwary trespassers. Bringing back the banner intact shows a recruit can cross dangerous ground, face the predators, and keep discipline under pressure.",sp=0},{t="The Stormpike Insignia",b="Returning from the caverns with the standard earns a soldier the Stormpike initiate’s insignia and a place in the expeditionary force. Haggerdin promises that the insignia can be improved as a soldier earns greater honor on the battlefield, with honors such as the Eye of Command as a distant aim.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is an Alliance officer in the Alterac Mountains who oversees Stormpike Guard recruitment and field recognition. He tests prospective fighters and rewards their service with military insignias.",al={"lieutenant haggerdin","haggerdin","who gives proving grounds"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Icewing Caverns?",a="Icewing Caverns lie southwest of Dun Baldar, the Alliance stronghold in Alterac Valley. Their winding tunnels run beneath the ice and stone.",al={"icewing caverns location","where is icewing caverns","banner location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats dwell inside the Icewing Caverns?",a="Ferocious ice harpies live in Icewing Caverns. Haggerdin warns that they ambush trespassers and tear out their throats.",al={"harpies","what is in icewing caverns","icewing harpies"},it="danger"},{q="Why does the Stormpike Guard require this test?",a="The Stormpike Guard fights a brutal war against the Frostwolf orcs. Haggerdin tests recruits before they join the main lines, so every soldier bearing the banner can fight in harsh conditions.",al={"why proving grounds","why do the banner trial","stormpike initiation"},it="motive"},{q="What is the reward for completing the proving ground?",a="A recruit who returns with the standard earns a Stormpike initiate’s insignia. Haggerdin can improve it as the soldier gains honor in Alterac Valley.",al={"stormpike insignia","eye of command","proving grounds reward"},gp=true},{q="Who are the Frostwolves mentioned by Haggerdin?",a="The Frostwolf Clan is an orcish clan that has lived in Alterac Valley since its exile decades ago. The Stormpike Guard sees them as hostile savages who stand in the way of Alliance interests and excavation in the valley.",al={"frostwolf savages","who are the frostwolves","frostwolf clan"},it="threat"},{q="What is the purpose of the Stormpike Banner in the caverns?",a="Planted deep inside the dangerous Icewing Caverns, the Stormpike Banner serves as a trial marker for recruits seeking to enlist in the expeditionary force. To claim it, you must brave the vicious harpies that infest the caves, demonstrating the courage, resourcefulness, and grit required of a true Stormpike soldier before ever setting foot on the open battlefield.",al={"what is stormpike banner","why banner in icewing caverns","stormpike banner purpose"},it="item",add="b9e84d22"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Stormpike expedition is the Alliance’s main military effort in Alterac. It joins dwarven archaeological ambitions with the defense of Alliance territory against the Horde.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you enter a guard led mostly by Ironforge dwarves seeking ancestral relics and titan mysteries. The trial can be your first step into one of your race’s proudest military units."},kw={"dun baldar","haggerdin","harpies","icewing caverns","insignia","proving grounds","stormpike","stormpike banner"},rel={"npc:lieutenant-haggerdin","zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Lieutenant Haggerdin",faction="Alliance",id=7162,ri={"Stormpike Banner"}},src={"Proving Grounds (Alterac Valley) (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:7321"] = {t="quest",n="Soothing Turtle Bisque",z="hillsbrad",s="In Tarren Mill, Christoph Jeffcoat is trying to prove the Forsaken can cook with care. He needs snapjaw meat from Hillsbrad's waterways and the shores of Lordamere Lake for his turtle bisque.",h="In Tarren Mill, Christoph Jeffcoat is trying to prove the Forsaken can cook with care.",sec={{t="Forsaken Gastronomy",b="Many believe the Forsaken have left the comforts of life behind, including fine cooking. Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill rejects that belief. He boasts that his rich turtle bisque could tempt souls back from beyond the grave. Through careful cooking, he means to show that undead hands can still make a warming dish in a land marked by plague and war.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Snapjaws",b="Jeffcoat once gathered ingredients himself from Hillsbrad's waterways and Lordamere Lake's eastern shores in neighboring Alterac. Duties in Tarren Mill and nearby Alliance forces keep him from hunting. He depends on passing Horde cooks to hunt snapjaws, bring back their meat, and keep the recipe alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does a Forsaken cook care about making hot bisque?",a="The Forsaken do not need food as living mortals do, but Christoph Jeffcoat takes pride in his craft. He wants to show that the undead can cook with skill, and jokes that his broth could bring the dead back to life.",al={"undead cooking","why make bisque","undead eat food"},it="motive"},{q="Where can turtle meat be found for this recipe?",a="Snapjaw meat comes from the aggressive turtles along Hillsbrad Foothills' rivers, in Alterac, and on the shores of Lordamere Lake.",al={"where are turtles","turtle locations","snapjaw locations"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't Christoph Jeffcoat gather his own ingredients?",a="Jeffcoat says his duties in Tarren Mill keep him occupied. Nearby Alliance forces also make his own hunting trips more dangerous.",al={"why doesn't christoph go","jeffcoat stuck in town"},it="why_me"},{q="Is cooking knowledge required to take this quest?",a="Yes. Christoph Jeffcoat shares his recipe only with cooks, and no advanced skill is needed to begin.",al={"do i need cooking","cooking profession requirement"},gp=true},{q="What is Tarren Mill's importance to the Horde in Hillsbrad?",a="Tarren Mill is the Horde's main stronghold in Hillsbrad Foothills. Once a human village, it is now a fortified base for the Forsaken and their allies, facing frequent clashes with Southshore and the Alliance nearby.",al={"what is tarren mill","tarren mill lore"},it="place"},{q="Is turtle bisque unique to the Horde?",a="Alliance cooks can learn a turtle bisque recipe from human chefs in Southshore, who also use local turtles. Christoph Jeffcoat's personal request and outlook belong to the Horde.",al={"alliance version","can alliance get turtle bisque"}},{q="What is the Turtle Meat for?",a="Christoph Jeffcoat needs the turtle meat to brew his signature soothing turtle bisque. While the undead may not feel the cold or hunger like the living, Jeffcoat takes immense pride in his culinary craft. He claims his secret recipe is so good that people would return from the dead just to savor a hot bowl.",al={"turtle meat use","why turtle meat","what is turtle meat used for"},it="item",add="7509a6d7"},{q="What are the snapjaws you hunt for this bisque?",a="Snapjaws are vicious, hard-shelled freshwater turtles native to the waterways of Lordaeron, particularly plentiful along the shores of Lake Lordamere and the local riverbanks. While feral and dangerous to unwary travelers, their tough flesh provides the vital, rich meat Christoph requires for his bisque.",al={"snapjaws hillsbrad","lake lordamere snapjaws","who do i hunt"},it="target",add="5469f6c5"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can learn to make Soothing Turtle Bisque from the snapjaws of Lordamere Lake and Hillsbrad's rivers.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Christoph Jeffcoat's passion for cooking, which death has not dulled.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help Tarren Mill by keeping its provisions and morale strong, alongside defending its borders."},kw={"christoph jeffcoat","cooking","hillsbrad foothills","lordamere lake","snapjaw","soothing turtle bisque","tarren mill","turtle meat"},rel={"npc:christoph-jeffcoat","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","topic:horde","topic:alliance","quest:555"},m={start="Christoph Jeffcoat",level="31",faction="Horde",id=7321,ri={"Turtle Meat"}},src={"Soothing Turtle Bisque (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8249"] = {t="quest",n="Junkboxes Needed",z="hillsbrad",s="Fahrad keeps Ravenholdt supplied with locked boxes for rogue training. His demand never ends, and he trades specialized throwing knives to anyone who brings authentic heavy junkboxes.",h="Fahrad keeps Ravenholdt supplied with locked boxes for rogue training.",sec={{t="Sharpening Ravenholdt's Talons",b="Ravenholdt Manor is a hidden redoubt in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills. Training never ceases there. Master thief Fahrad oversees the guild's operatives and prizes practical skill at picking locks. Zan supplies practice contraptions for new recruits, but Fahrad finds them too crude for experienced thieves who must open stubborn mechanisms in the field.",sp=0},{t="A Curiously Open Arrangement",b="Fahrad contracts for heavy junkboxes stolen from dangerous targets across Azeroth, and he accepts deliveries in batches. Only skilled thieves can lift the boxes from their marks in the wild, but anyone may bring them to the manor. Even boxes picked clean of major valuables earn Fahrad's favor and a supply of the manor's finely balanced throwing knives, so long as a token coin remains inside to motivate the initiates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Fahrad want these junkboxes?",a="Ravenholdt's apprentice rogues need realistic mechanisms for lockpicking practice. Zan, the manor's resident craftsman, makes practice chests that Fahrad considers too elementary for anyone past the beginner stage, so he requires real lockboxes taken from dangerous marks.",al={"why junkboxes","junkboxes purpose","why fahrad wants boxes"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The exchange takes place at Ravenholdt Manor, a secret refuge for the thieves' guild concealed in the mountains north of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"junkboxes needed location","where is fahrad","ravenholdt location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can only rogues turn in this quest?",a="Anyone who can bring heavy junkboxes to the manor may deliver them. Skilled thieves originally steal the boxes from their marks through pickpocketing.",al={"is this rogue only","can anyone do junkboxes needed","other classes junkboxes"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="Why must there still be coins left inside the boxes?",a="Fahrad requires a few coins to remain in each chest, giving rogues in training a practical incentive for their lockpicking efforts.",al={"why leave coins in box","do boxes need loot","empty junkboxes"},it="purpose"},{q="What does Ravenholdt offer in exchange?",a="Contributors earn guild standing and finely crafted throwing knives from Fahrad, who sardonicly wishes they will find a place in someone's heart.",al={"junkboxes needed reward","what does fahrad give","ravenholdt throwing knives"},it="for_you"},{q="Who is Zan that Fahrad complains about?",a="Zan supplies Ravenholdt with locks and practice mechanisms. Fahrad finds Zan's crude work fit only for the rawest beginners, not serious operatives.",al={"who is zan","zan ravenholdt","zan locks"},it="people"},{q="Why does Ravenholdt need an outside rogue to gather junkboxes?",a="Ravenholdt's current trainees are still cutting their teeth and simply lack the skill to obtain intricate locks on their own. The practice mechanisms crafted by their in-house tinker, Zan, are far too crude for advanced training. Fahrad relies on accomplished operatives like you to venture into perilous territory and filch genuine, high-security lockboxes that pose a real challenge.",al={"why ask me for junkboxes","why winstone wolfe needs me","why doesn't ravenholdt get their own junkboxes"},it="why_me",add="45d1fe22"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can source these heavy chests by pickpocketing seasoned adversaries. Ravenholdt gives that illicit skill a place to serve.",["faction:Alliance"]="Ravenholdt lies in contested Lordaeron territory and operates independently. As an Alliance wanderer, you can bring it contracts without regard for faction lines.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde operative, you can brave the trek into the Hillsbrad mountains. Ravenholdt is indifferent to faction loyalties and prizes useful illicit goods above all else."},kw={"heavy junkbox","hillsbrad","junkboxes","lockpicking","pickpocket","ravenholdt","fahrad","zan"},rel={"topic:ravenholdt","zone:hillsbrad"},m={start="Fahrad",["end"]="Fahrad",id=8249},src={"Junkboxes Needed"}}
E["quest:98071"] = {t="quest",n="Brewer's Trade",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad, a case of Fallrook Varietal is bound for Dun Garok. The brew-kin there miss the Fallrook family's vineyards, and a sack of Homebrew Hops comes back in trade.",h="In Hillsbrad, a case of Fallrook Varietal is bound for Dun Garok.",sec={{t="A Taste of the Past",b="The Fallrook cellars still hold cases of wine, though most of its best bottled years are long gone. The Dun Garok brew-kin miss the family's vineyards too, and a trade has been arranged with them.",sp=0},{t="The Exchange at Dun Garok",b="You carry the case southeast to Dun Garok, where the brew-kin gather beside the fireplace at the base of their fort. In return, you bring back a sack of their Homebrew Hops.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is being traded in this exchange?",a="A case of Fallrook Varietal wine from the cellars goes to the Dun Garok brew-kin in return for a sack of their Homebrew Hops.",al={"what am i delivering","brewer's trade items","fallrook wine"}},{q="Where in Dun Garok does the wine need to go?",a="You leave the wine with the brew-kin beside the fireplace where they gather, at the base of their fort.",al={"where is the fireplace","dun garok delivery location","where to leave wine"}},{q="Where is Dun Garok located?",a="Dun Garok lies in the southeast of Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"dun garok location","where is dun garok"}},{q="Who were the Fallrooks?",a="The Fallrooks were a family whose vineyards are missed. Most of their best bottled years have long since been drunk, though cases of their wine remain in the cellars.",al={"fallrook family","fallrook vineyards"}}},kw={"brew-kin","dun garok","fallrook","fallrook varietal","hillsbrad","homebrew hops","hops","wine"},rel={"subzone:dun-garok","zone:hillsbrad"},m={id=98071},src={"In-game quest text: Brewer's Trade"},fv=true}
E["subzone:azurelode-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Azurelode Mine",z="hillsbrad",s="In southwestern Hillsbrad, Azurelode Mine sends iron to the Alliance war effort. Southshore's militia guards the human laborers who work its tunnels.",h="In southwestern Hillsbrad, Azurelode Mine sends iron to the Alliance war effort.",sec={{t="Veins of the Foothills",b="Southwest of the open farmland and just west of Southshore, Azurelode Mine cuts into the ridges along the coast. Human miners work deep underground under Foreman Bonds's watch, drawing iron for arms and armor. That iron helps Alliance defenders hold the region against the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="A Vital Military Target",b="Southshore's garrisons and town militia rely on Azurelode Mine for most of their raw iron. Tarren Mill targets the mine's workers and guards, seeking to break the supply lines that sustain Hillsbrad's human strongholds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Azurelode Mine?",a="The Alliance controls Azurelode Mine, where human miners affiliated with Southshore and the Hillsbrad township work under Foreman Bonds.",al={"who runs azurelode","azurelode mine faction","who owns azurelode"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the mine important to the Horde?",a="Azurelode Mine supplies iron to Southshore's armories and the local Alliance militia. Tarren Mill's leaders target the miners and overseers to cripple human weapon production in the Foothills.",al={"why attack azurelode","battle of hillsbrad mine","horde interest in mine"},it="purpose"},{q="Was Azurelode Mine always part of Hillsbrad?",a="The accounts of this era do not say who held these hills before Hillsbrad. Today, miners from the Hillsbrad Fields work the mine under Foreman Bonds.",al={"greymane wall history","was azurelode gilneas","gilneas mine"},it="origin"},{q="What metals are mined here?",a="Azurelode Mine primarily produces iron ore for nearby human armories.",al={"what ore in azurelode","azurelode resources"},it="item"},{q="What is Azurelode Mine?",a="Azurelode Mine is an active iron-mining operation carved into the hills of southwestern Hillsbrad Foothills, situated south of the Hillsbrad Fields and west of Southshore. It serves as a vital strategic asset for the local human population, supplying vital iron to Alliance armories across the region to fuel their ongoing struggle against hostile forces.",al={"azurelode mine","what is azurelode","azurelode mine info"},it="place",add="9018e270"},{q="What happened at Azurelode Mine?",a="Azurelode Mine has long been worked by miners from the Hillsbrad Fields under Foreman Bonds, supplying iron to the Alliance's armories. Today, it remains fully garrisoned and operational under Alliance control, though it faces escalating pressure as the Forsaken contest Hillsbrad.",al={"azurelode history","history of azurelode mine","azurelode past"},it="history",add="549159c0"},{q="Who lives in or runs Azurelode Mine?",a="The mine is operated by human laborers from the nearby Hillsbrad Fields, directed by Foreman Bonds. Due to the constant danger posed by the Horde and local wildlife, Hillsbrad sentries and armed guards are stationed throughout the tunnels and exterior to defend the miners while they dig.",al={"who runs azurelode mine","azurelode overseer","who works in azurelode"},it="residents",add="b1a6dc2c"},{q="Is Azurelode Mine dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the standard hazards of subterranean excavation, Azurelode Mine is a military target caught in the broader Battle for Hillsbrad. The site is heavily fortified with vigilant human sentries, and Horde operatives frequently probe its tunnels seeking to disrupt ore production, assassinate Foreman Bonds, and slaughter the workforce.",al={"is azurelode dangerous","azurelode threats","danger at azurelode mine"},it="danger",add="7c8c1de2"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The tunnels and ridges around Azurelode hold rich iron deposits, though Alliance miners guard the mine's interior fiercely.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking Azurelode Mine cuts off Southshore's fresh iron supply and supports the Forsaken offensive in the Foothills."},kw={"azurelode mine","foreman bonds","hillsbrad foothills","hillsbrad miners","iron mine","southshore"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","quest:527","subzone:southshore","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance"},src={"Azurelode Mine"}}
E["subzone:chillwind-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Chillwind Point",z="hillsbrad",s="Cold drafts sweep through Chillwind Point, a rocky rise above the mountain pass. The ancient troll ruin sits where Hillsbrad Foothills, the Alterac Mountains, and the Western Plaguelands meet, and Bath'rah the Windwatcher lives among its stones.",h="Cold drafts sweep through Chillwind Point, a rocky rise above the mountain pass.",sec={{t="A Bitter Crossroads",b="Chillwind Point overlooks the ravine from Hillsbrad's edge. The pass leads into the Western Plaguelands, while the Alterac Mountains rise nearby. Long before Lordaeron claimed these routes, ancient trolls built stone structures on the heights. Their weather-beaten remains still face the elements. Cold winds now blow south through the ravine, carrying the chill of the fallen north into the foothills below.",sp=0},{t="The Windwatcher",b="Bath'rah the Windwatcher lives among the old stones at Chillwind Point. The jungle troll hermit communes with the violent gales that course through the gap. Despite the bleak exposure and the nearby Scourge-ravaged lands, his camp is not entirely deserted. Travelers and shamans heading north often seek him out to learn the secrets of the mountain currents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Chillwind Point?",a="Chillwind Point is an ancient troll ruin on a high rise overlooking the pass between Hillsbrad, Alterac, and the Western Plaguelands. Its name comes from the biting drafts that whistle through the nearby gorge.",al={"chillwind point overview","where is chillwind point","what is this place"},it="place"},{q="Is Chillwind Point the same as Chillwind Camp?",a="No. Chillwind Camp is the fortified Alliance and Argent Dawn outpost just north across the border, inside the Western Plaguelands. Chillwind Point is the ruined troll rise to the south.",al={"chillwind point vs camp","chillwind camp difference","is this chillwind camp"}},{q="Who lives at Chillwind Point?",a="Bath'rah the Windwatcher lives alone among the ruins. The friendly jungle troll studies the winds and aids elemental seekers and shamans who brave the pass.",al={"who is here","who is the troll","bathrah"},it="residents"},{q="Why is it so cold here?",a="A narrow mountain ravine beside Chillwind Point funnels freezing drafts from the high northern regions and the blighted Western Plaguelands down into the lower foothills.",al={"why is it chilly","chill winds","freezing wind"},it="name"},{q="What happened to Chillwind Point in the past?",a="This elevated pass once formed part of the prosperous human kingdom of Lordaeron. Long before Lordaeron's fall, however, trolls established the ancient stone structure that still crowns the hill. Today, it stands as an abandoned relic caught between the troubled lands of Alterac and the blight creeping down from the north.",al={"chillwind point history","past of chillwind point","what happened at chillwind point"},it="history",add="8e613e22"},{q="Why is Chillwind Point in ruins?",a="The stone edifice atop the rise is an ancient troll ruin that fell into decay long before the recent wars. With the collapse of Lordaeron and the devastation wrought across the surrounding mountains, no civilized power maintains the pass, leaving only weathered stonework open to the bitter elements.",al={"why is chillwind point ruined","chillwind point ruins","why is chillwind point abandoned"},it="ruin",add="14e6a6f5"},{q="Is Chillwind Point dangerous?",a="The hill itself is relatively calm, home only to the solitary hermit Bath'rah the Windwatcher. However, danger looms directly nearby: the pass funnels bitter drafts down from the plagued horrors of the Western Plaguelands just to the north, and the surrounding wilderness is rife with mountain predators and bandits.",al={"is chillwind point safe","chillwind point danger","threats chillwind point"},it="danger",add="b1aade3c"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can study the pass's wild, funneling gusts with the hermit Bath'rah the Windwatcher, who draws practitioners seeking elemental focus.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you find these ancient ruins just south of the border post at Chillwind Camp, where the contested foothills give way to the Plaguelands."},kw={"alterac","bath'rah","chillwind","chillwind point","hillsbrad","plaguelands","troll ruins","windwatcher"},rel={"npc:bath-rah-the-windwatcher","subzone:chillwind-camp","zone:westernplaguelands","zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","quest:1791","topic:troll","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Chillwind Point"}}
E["subzone:corrahn-s-dagger"] = {t="subzone",n="Corrahn's Dagger",z="hillsbrad",s="Syndicate cutthroats hold Corrahn's Dagger, the second ridge among northern Hillsbrad's four rocky fingers. They use its high ground as a hideout.",h="Syndicate cutthroats hold Corrahn's Dagger, the second ridge among northern Hillsbrad's four rocky fingers.",sec={{t="A Northern Strongpoint",b="Corrahn's Dagger rises in northern Hillsbrad Foothills as the second of four rocky ridges called the fingers of Hillsbrad. Syndicate cutthroats overrun the ridge and use its height to watch the valley below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Corrahn's Dagger?",a="Rogue humans of the Syndicate hold Corrahn's Dagger and use its heights as a hideout.",al={"who is at corrahn's dagger","corrahns dagger faction","who lives here"},it="in_charge"},{q="What are the fingers of Hillsbrad?",a="The fingers of Hillsbrad are four prominent ridges that project south from the northern mountain range into Hillsbrad valley. Corrahn's Dagger is the second ridge.",al={"four fingers hillsbrad","four ridges hillsbrad","hillsbrad fingers"}},{q="What is Corrahn's Dagger?",a="Corrahn's Dagger is the second of the four prominent mountain ridges known as the fingers of Hillsbrad, rising along the northern edge of the foothills. Rogue humans of the Syndicate hold the high ground as a hideout overlooking the valley below.",al={"what is corrahns dagger","corrahns dagger lore","corrahn dagger hill"},it="place",add="2610a3ae"},{q="Is Corrahn's Dagger dangerous?",a="Yes. The ridge is held by Syndicate cutthroats who use the heights as a hideout, and they attack travelers of both the Alliance and the Horde who wander too close.",al={"is corrahns dagger safe","danger corrahns dagger","corrahns dagger enemies"},it="danger",add="dcd9fc97"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf crossing the northern foothills, expect bandits rather than allies at this Syndicate hideout.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken working in Hillsbrad, you face hostility from the Syndicate cutthroats on the ridge."},kw={"corrahn","corrahn's dagger","dagger","four fingers","hillsbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:forsaken","topic:syndicate"},src={"Corrahn's Dagger"}}
E["subzone:darrow-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Darrow Hill",z="hillsbrad",s="In northern Hillsbrad, Darrow Hill's rugged grassland rises beneath the Headland. Mountain lions and stags roam its open slopes, while feral yetis lurk in the Foothill Caverns. Alterac Granite draws travelers into this dangerous frontier.",h="In northern Hillsbrad, Darrow Hill's rugged grassland rises beneath the Headland.",sec={{t="A Treacherous Frontier",b="Darrow Hill stretches below the Headland, joining southern Hillsbrad's rolling pasture to Alterac's jagged, colder heights. Mountain lions and stags move through tall grasses on its rocky slopes, and towering yetis emerge from the Foothill Caverns. The cavern walls hold deposits of dense Alterac Granite, drawing quarry workers, miners, and adventurers into danger. Regional claims remain contentious, and travelers of either faction can be caught unaware on the trails.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Darrow Hill located?",a="Darrow Hill lies in northern Hillsbrad Foothills, directly south of the rocky bluffs called the Headland and east of the main mountain road into Alterac.",al={"darrow hill location","where is darrow hill","darrow hill map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures threaten travelers around Darrow Hill?",a="Stags and mountain lions prowl the open slopes, while savage yetis roam around and inside the Foothill Caverns.",al={"darrow hill mobs","what lives on darrow hill","monsters darrow hill"},it="threat"},{q="What can be found inside the Foothill Caverns?",a="Feral yetis infest the Foothill Caverns, whose rocky walls hold veins of Alterac Granite prized by those who seek it.",al={"foothill caverns","darrow hill cave","what is in the cave"},it="place"},{q="Why is this area considered so dangerous for travelers?",a="Fierce wildlife and yeti dens threaten travelers, and the open ground lies directly beside contested roadways. Alliance and Horde wanderers frequently ambush one another there.",al={"why is darrow hill dangerous","darrow hill pvp","danger at darrow hill"},it="danger"},{q="What is Darrow Hill?",a="Darrow Hill is an elevated, rugged expanse nestled in the northern reaches of the Hillsbrad Foothills, resting directly beneath the towering heights of the Headland. Its open slopes are home to roaming wildlife, while the nearby Foothill Caverns cut into the stone, harboring subterranean dangers beneath the tranquil surface.",al={"what is darrow hill","darrow hill hillsbrad","darrow hill info"},it="place",add="35480940"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Darrow Hill's cave networks, especially the Foothill Caverns, hold rich veins of Alterac Granite and regional minerals. You must contend with the yetis nesting nearby.",["class:Hunter"]="You can hunt mountain lions and stags across the hills as they move between the Alterac tree line and the lower grasslands."},kw={"alterac granite","darrow hill","foothill caverns","headland","hillsbrad foothills","yetis"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Darrow Hill"}}
E["subzone:dun-garok"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Garok",z="hillsbrad",s="Dun Garok guards the southeastern heights of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Captain Ironhill commands its dwarven garrison, which defends Alliance interests and nearby operations such as the Azurelode Mine. To the Forsaken of Tarren Mill, the stronghold is a military threat on their border.",h="Dun Garok guards the southeastern heights of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Foothills",b="Dun Garok holds the crags in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills. Captain Ironhill commands the Ironforge mountaineers and riflemen who defend the outpost. They guard human settlements in Hillsbrad and protect Alliance operations at the Azurelode Mine. Stone walls and deep entrenchments help the garrison hold against nearby threats.",sp=0},{t="Target of Tarren Mill",b="Dun Garok lies close to Tarren Mill, and the Forsaken see it as an intrusion on their southern border. Sylvanas Windrunner's forces resent the armed dwarven troops near their stronghold. They plot to enter the fortress, break its defenses, and kill Captain Ironhill's garrison to secure Forsaken control of Hillsbrad.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Dun Garok?",a="Dun Garok guards the southeastern mountains of the Hillsbrad Foothills as a fortified dwarven outpost. Its Ironforge troops defend Alliance holdings in the region.",al={"dun garok location","what is this dwarven keep","hillsbrad dwarf fort"},it="place"},{q="Who commands Dun Garok?",a="Captain Ironhill commands Dun Garok's mountaineers and riflemen. They defend Hillsbrad and the nearby Azurelode Mine.",al={"dun garok leader","who leads dun garok","captain ironhill"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to destroy Dun Garok?",a="The Forsaken see Dun Garok, near Tarren Mill on their southern border, as a security threat. They send agents to destroy the garrison.",al={"why horde attack dun garok","forsaken dun garok","tarren mill dun garok conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Dun Garok's strategic value to the Alliance?",a="Dun Garok helps the Alliance defend Hillsbrad and protect the nearby Azurelode Mine from hostile seizure.",al={"why is dun garok important","alliance purpose dun garok"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened at Dun Garok?",a="Dun Garok was built as a dwarven stronghold nestled in the southeastern hills to defend nearby human settlements and the Azurelode Mine. Ever since the Forsaken established their dominion in Lordaeron, they have viewed the dwarven fortress as a severe military threat, regularly sending soldiers and mercenaries to harass and attempt to purge its defenders.",al={"dun garok history","what happened here","dun garok lore"},it="history",add="b8973178"},{q="Is Dun Garok dangerous?",a="Yes. The stronghold is heavily fortified and garrisoned by disciplined dwarven soldiers under Captain Ironhill. For members of the Horde and the Forsaken, entering Dun Garok invites immediate hostility from elite riflemen and mountain guards who defend their ramparts with stubborn tenacity.",al={"is dun garok safe","dun garok danger","threats in dun garok"},it="danger",add="d2b489e2"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can look to Dun Garok, where Captain Ironhill and his mountaineers defend their human allies and mark Ironforge's reach into Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a well-defended dwarven enclave that threatens Forsaken security around Tarren Mill. Its garrison is a priority target."},kw={"azurelode mine","dun garok","dwarf","hillsbrad","ironforge","ironhill","keep","mountaineer"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:azurelode-mine","topic:dwarf","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Dun Garok"}}
E["subzone:durnholde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Durnholde Keep",z="hillsbrad",s="Outlaws hold Durnholde Keep, a shattered fortress east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once the Alliance headquarters for the southern orc internment camps, it is now a Syndicate refuge.",h="Outlaws hold Durnholde Keep, a shattered fortress east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Crucible of Captivity",b="After the Second War, the Alliance made Durnholde Keep its headquarters for the southern internment camps. Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore commanded the fortress and its arena, where orcs fought for sport and profit. Blackmoore raised the orphaned infant Go'el as a slave, named him Thrall, and trained him to fight. With Taretha Foxton's aid, Thrall escaped captivity and later united the scattered orc clans beneath the new Horde. He returned to Durnholde, besieged the keep, slew Blackmoore, and called on the earth spirits to shatter its walls.",sp=0},{t="In the Clutches of the Syndicate",b="Durnholde Keep has lain in ruins since its collapse before the Third War. After Lordaeron fell, the Syndicate took refuge among its broken ramparts. These bandits are dispossessed Alterac nobles and cutthroats. From the ruined bailey and towers, they prey on travelers across the Hillsbrad Foothills, using the old fortress as a fortified outpost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Durnholde Keep in ruins?",a="Thrall returned to Durnholde with the liberated Horde to face his former master, Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore. After slaying Blackmoore, he called on the earth spirits to demolish the fortress so it could never again cage his people.",al={"who destroyed durnholde","what happened to durnholde keep","why is durnholde destroyed"},it="ruin"},{q="Who currently occupies Durnholde Keep?",a="The Syndicate holds Durnholde Keep. Its exiled Alterac nobles have become outlaws, using the crumbling ramparts as a refuge for banditry and attacks across Hillsbrad.",al={"who lives in durnholde","durnholde mobs","syndicate at durnholde"},it="residents"},{q="What was Thrall's connection to this place?",a="Aedelas Blackmoore found the orphaned orc as a child and raised him as a slave at Durnholde. Thrall learned tactics and was forced to fight as a gladiator before escaping with help from Taretha Foxton.",al={"did thrall live here","thrall durnholde history","was thrall a prisoner here"},it="people"},{q="What purpose did the keep serve during the Second War?",a="Durnholde was an Alliance stronghold. After the Second War, it became the command center for the internment camps holding the defeated orcs, under Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore.",al={"durnholde second war","what was durnholde used for"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Durnholde Keep?",a="Durnholde Keep is a shattered fortress situated east of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once a bustling military stronghold featuring barracks, an arena, and a mage tower, it served as the administrative command center for the Alliance's orc internment camps following the Second War. Today, it stands as a sprawling ruin, occupied by outlaws and scavengers.",al={"what is durnholde","durnholde keep overview","where is durnholde"},it="place",add="1d89eea7"},{q="What happened at Durnholde Keep?",a="After the Second War, Durnholde became the command center of the orc internment camps and grew infamous under Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore, who raised the captive orc Thrall here as a gladiator. After escaping, Thrall returned at the head of a reformed Horde to liberate his people. He defeated Blackmoore in combat and invoked the earth spirits to shatter the fortress to the ground.",al={"history of durnholde","durnholde lore","siege of durnholde"},it="history",add="d850e42f"},{q="Is Durnholde Keep dangerous?",a="Yes. The crumbled walls and surrounding grounds are heavily infested with operatives of the Syndicate, an aggressive criminal organization composed of former Alterac nobility and brigands. They guard the wreckage fiercely and attack any travelers or adventurers who wander too close to their encampments.",al={"is durnholde dangerous","threats in durnholde keep","what dangers are at durnholde"},it="danger",add="e6548fd4"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs, Durnholde's ruined stones mark where Warchief Thrall cast off his chains, ending decades of orcish captivity and kindling the Horde's rebirth.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Durnholde's shattered ramparts once guarded Lordaeron and upheld its justice. Now Syndicate outlaws and cutthroats make their lair there."},kw={"blackmoore","durnholde keep","hillsbrad","internment","syndicate","taretha foxton","tarren mill","thrall"},rel={"npc:thrall","zone:hillsbrad","topic:syndicate","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:second-war","topic:horde"},src={"Durnholde Keep"}}
E["subzone:eastern-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastern Strand",z="hillsbrad",s="Daggerspine naga hold the Eastern Strand along Hillsbrad's southeastern coast. The beaches and shallows reach toward the Arathi Highlands border.",h="Daggerspine naga hold the Eastern Strand along Hillsbrad's southeastern coast.",sec={{t="A Hostile Shoreline",b="The Daggerspine naga hold the Eastern Strand on Hillsbrad's southeastern edge. Across the bay lies the Western Strand. Southshore and Tarren Mill clash over the region's human farms, while the naga dominate these sandy flats and tidelines. They come from the Great Sea, crossing the sandbars and settling among rocky outcrops. From there, they watch the mainland.",sp=0},{t="Daggerspine Territory",b="Daggerspine warriors and spellcasters prowl the beaches and nearby waters southeast of Southshore, making the coast dangerous for travelers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Eastern Strand located?",a="The Eastern Strand runs along Hillsbrad Foothills' southeastern coast, toward the Arathi Highlands border.",al={"eastern strand location","where is eastern strand","eastern strand map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit the Eastern Strand?",a="Daggerspine naga overrun the Eastern Strand's beach and nearby waters, including foot soldiers, raiders, and spellcasters along the tideline.",al={"eastern strand mobs","who lives on eastern strand","eastern strand enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the naga gathering on this beach?",a="Daggerspine naga occupy the Eastern Strand's beaches and waters. Their purpose beyond holding this coastal territory is unrecorded in the Classic account.",al={"why are naga in hillsbrad","daggerspine attack plans","what are the naga doing here"},it="purpose"},{q="How does the Eastern Strand differ from the Western Strand?",a="Both strands border Hillsbrad's southern coast. The Western Strand lies southwest toward Silverpine, where Torn Fin murlocs dwell. The Eastern Strand lies southeast toward Arathi, held by Daggerspine naga.",al={"western strand vs eastern strand","two beaches in hillsbrad"}},{q="What is the Eastern Strand?",a="The Eastern Strand is the windswept southeastern coastline of Hillsbrad Foothills, facing the cold waters of the Great Sea. While it mirrors the Western Strand across the region's coast, this beach is distinguished by a heavy infestation of Daggerspine naga who prowl the shallows and gather along the surf.",al={"what is eastern strand","eastern strand lore","tell me about eastern strand"},it="place",add="1e981837"},{q="Is the Eastern Strand dangerous?",a="The shoreline is hazardous for travelers. Aggressive Daggerspine naga, including warriors and spellcasters, prowl the beaches and water and attack outsiders who approach their territory.",al={"eastern strand danger","is eastern strand safe","how dangerous is eastern strand"},it="danger",add="05c2d3e2"},{q="Why is it called the Eastern Strand?",a="It is named simply for its geography. 'Strand' is an old term for a shore or beach, and this stretch forms the eastern half of the coast bordering Hillsbrad Foothills, sitting in natural contrast to the Western Strand situated past Southshore.",al={"why called eastern strand","eastern strand name origin","where does eastern strand get its name"},it="name",add="a940bc43"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Daggerspine naga on the Eastern Strand threaten Southshore's sea defenses and nearby patrols from the flank.",["faction:Horde"]="An organized naga advance inland from the coast could disrupt Horde movements and supply lines across lower Hillsbrad."},kw={"beach","coast","daggerspine","eastern strand","hillsbrad foothills","naga"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:naga"},src={"Eastern Strand"}}
E["subzone:growless-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Growless Cave",z="hillsbrad",s="In frigid Growless Cave, mountain yetis roam the cavern in the Alterac Mountains. The cave also holds the Flame of Uzel, a ceremonial pyre tied to Helcular's dark necromancy.",h="In frigid Growless Cave, mountain yetis roam the cavern in the Alterac Mountains.",sec={{t="A Den of Beasts and Dark Magic",b="Territorial mountain yetis roam Growless Cave in the crags above Alterac's foothills. Travelers on the treacherous slopes avoid its entrance, especially when Skhowl, a notorious yeti, prowls outside. The cave holds more than danger from the beasts. Within it stands the Flame of Uzel, an arcane brazier left by the human mage Helcular. Before his death, Helcular meant to use the pyre in a dark ritual to become a lich. Its foul warmth once drew Frostmaw, a massive predator, from the frozen wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live in Growless Cave?",a="Wild mountain yetis native to Alterac live in Growless Cave. Skhowl, a dangerous and rare yeti, sometimes wanders just outside its entrance.",al={"who lives here","growless cave mobs","what is inside growless cave"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Flame of Uzel?",a="The Flame of Uzel is a ceremonial pyre established by Helcular, a former Dalaran mage turned necromancer. He made it for a forbidden ritual meant to transform him into an undying lich.",al={"flame of uzel","pyre in growless cave","helcular flame"}},{q="Who is Frostmaw?",a="Frostmaw is a massive, exceptionally fierce yeti roaming the Alterac peaks. Burning fresh meat on the Flame of Uzel once lured the ravenous beast to the cavern.",al={"frostmaw yeti","frostmaw"}},{q="Why would travelers venture here?",a="Adventurers brave the cave to hunt dangerous yetis for their pelts or to pursue the lingering necromantic artifacts tied to Helcular's legacy in Alterac.",al={"why go to growless cave","growless cave quests"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Growless Cave?",a="Growless Cave is a cavern hollowed into the frigid slopes of the Alterac Mountains. Far from civilized settlements, it serves primarily as a den for savage mountain yetis, shielded from the brutal highland winds.",al={"what is growless cave","growless cave info","about growless cave"},it="place",add="ae5edb73"},{q="What happened at Growless Cave?",a="In the past, the ambitious human mage Helcular chose this remote den to establish the Flame of Uzel. He intended this dark ceremonial pyre to serve as an instrument in his necromantic rituals to ascend into lichdom.",al={"growless cave history","what happened here","helcular growless cave"},it="history",add="719f5ae4"},{q="Is Growless Cave dangerous?",a="Yes. The cave is crawling with ferocious mountain yetis that aggressively defend their lair. On occasion, the wandering beast Skhowl prowls just outside its threshold, and the formidable yeti Frostmaw has been known to frequent the cavern.",al={"how dangerous is growless cave","growless cave danger","is growless cave safe"},it="danger",add="1fe34e74"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken aiding Helcular's vengeance, the cave holds grim significance. His dark rites and relics remain scattered across fallen Alterac.",["class:Mage"]="The Flame of Uzel's remnants warn mages of the peril of turning Kirin Tor wizardry toward necromancy."},kw={"alterac","flame of uzel","frostmaw","growless cave","helcular","skhowl","yeti"},rel={"zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Growless Cave"}}
E["subzone:hillsbrad-fields"] = {t="subzone",n="Hillsbrad Fields",z="hillsbrad",s="In Hillsbrad Fields, farmers and militia face constant attacks from nearby Tarren Mill. The settlement in western Hillsbrad Foothills is one of the few human communities in former Lordaeron to resist the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",h="In Hillsbrad Fields, farmers and militia face constant attacks from nearby Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Defiant Bastion of Lordaeron",b="Hillsbrad Fields stretch from Darrow Hill to the Azurelode Mine, where orchards, pumpkin patches, and pastures supply Southshore and the surviving Alliance resistance. The people endured while much of Lordaeron fell to undeath, keeping the royal tabard and heraldry of their fallen kingdom. Magistrate Burnside and the Council of Hillsbrad lead the township as an independent civic body under constant siege. Verringtan, the local blacksmith, and his apprentices arm the people, so farmers and laborers can defend their land.",sp=0},{t="Front Line of the Undead Advance",b="High Executor Darthalia and the Forsaken forces at Tarren Mill target Hillsbrad's fertile fields. The Undercity sees the thriving human settlement as a threat on its southern flank and directs constant raids against its crops, livestock, councilors, and farmers. Hillsbrad's defenders have formed a hardened militia in response. Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz organize ambushes and fight the undead to protect their homes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there still living humans farming here?",a="Hillsbrad and neighbouring Southshore are among the few settlements in Lordaeron to avoid complete destruction by the Scourge during the Third War. Their people stayed to rebuild and maintain their homeland, while others fled south or joined the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"why are humans in hillsbrad","who lives in hillsbrad fields","are the farmers alive"},it="people"},{q="Who rules over the town and fields?",a="Magistrate Burnside governs the town and fields with Clerk Horrace Whitesteed and the Council of Hillsbrad from the town hall. Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz manage nearby estates, and Verringtan equips the town watch.",al={"who leads hillsbrad","hillsbrad leadership","magistrate of hillsbrad"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking the farms?",a="High Executor Darthalia at Tarren Mill sees Hillsbrad as a dangerous Alliance foothold on the Forsaken border. Undercity orders direct soldiers to break human supply lines by destroying food stores, slaughtering livestock, and killing town leaders to clear the way for Forsaken dominance in the foothills.",al={"why forsaken attack hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad reason","tarren mill attacks"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Hillsbrad during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer ordered an assault on Hillsbrad to break human morale as the Horde built up its forces in the Southshore region. Hillsbrad was destroyed, but the Alliance drove out the orcs and the town was rebuilt.",al={"hillsbrad second war","orcs destroyed hillsbrad","history of hillsbrad fields"},it="history"},{q="What is Hillsbrad Fields?",a="Hillsbrad Fields is the fertile agricultural heartland surrounding the township of Hillsbrad in the western foothills. Its sprawling orchards, pumpkin patches, and pastures provide food not only for the local populace, but for the nearby port of Southshore and Alliance outposts across the region. Unlike much of northern Lordaeron, its farmlands survived the Scourge largely intact, remaining one of the few places where living human farmers still cultivate crops under the banner of the fallen kingdom.",al={"what is hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad fields overview","about hillsbrad fields"},it="place",add="253bd91d"},{q="Is Hillsbrad Fields dangerous?",a="Extremely so, depending on who you are. The fields are currently a primary battleground in the war between the living humans of Hillsbrad and the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill. The farmers, peasants, and town guards are heavily armed, organized, and vigilant against undead incursions, staging vicious ambushes against trespassers. For Forsaken champions sent by High Executor Darthalia, clearing these fortified farmsteads is a bloody and hotly contested campaign.",al={"is hillsbrad fields safe","hillsbrad fields danger","how dangerous is hillsbrad fields"},it="danger",add="c30a4664"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Hillsbrad Fields supply food and stand as a symbol of Lordaeron's enduring spirit. Protect them from the Forsaken's attacks.",["faction:Horde"]="High Executor Darthalia calls for Hillsbrad's farms and militia to be dismantled, securing the southern frontier for the Forsaken."},kw={"battle of hillsbrad","darthalia","farmer getz","farmer ray","hillsbrad","hillsbrad fields","magistrate burnside","southshore","tarren mill","verringtan"},rel={"quest:527","quest:567","zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:azurelode-mine","npc:high-executor-darthalia","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Hillsbrad Fields"}}
E["subzone:lordamere-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Lordamere Lake",z="hillsbrad",s="Lordamere Lake lies between Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains, its waters now shadowed by the undead. Once the northern heart of human life, its cold waters and islands are haunted by Scourge necromancers and feral murlocs.",h="Lordamere Lake lies between Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains, its waters now...",sec={{t="Heart of the Fallen Kingdoms",b="Lordamere Lake once joined the centers of human power in the north. The Capital City of Lordaeron guarded its northern shores, Dalaran rose near the southern reach, and Alterac lined the eastern edge beneath its mountains. Merchant vessels and fishing boats crossed the broad lake without fear. After the devastation of the Third War, the lake became a natural barrier between the Forsaken-held lands of Tirisfal and Silverpine and the treacherous heights of Alterac.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Expanse",b="Dark waters make travel across Lordamere Lake perilous. Fenris Isle lies at its center, where the Scourge necromancer Thule Ravenclaw and his Rot Hide gnolls hold out against the Forsaken. Farther east, aggressive Vile Fin murlocs overrun the Dawning Isles. From the ruins around Dalaran to the shoreline of the Undercity, the lake is now a drowned frontier contested by remnant monsters and the armies of the dead.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What kingdoms historically bordered Lordamere Lake?",a="During the height of the Alliance of Lordaeron, the Kingdom of Lordaeron bordered the lake to the north and west, Dalaran to the south, and Alterac along its eastern mountain bluffs.",al={"who lived on lordamere lake","lordamere lake history","kingdoms around lordamere"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Fenris Isle in the middle of the lake?",a="Rot Hide gnolls hold Fenris Isle under the command of the Scourge necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, and the Forsaken assault them relentlessly.",al={"who is on fenris isle","fenris island lordamere","fenris isle ruler"},sp=1,it="residents",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="What are the Dawning Isles?",a="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of small islands in the eastern part of Lordamere Lake, east of Fenris Isle. Hostile Vile Fin murlocs have overrun and claimed them.",al={"dawning isles location","islands in lordamere lake","dawning isles monsters"},it="place"},{q="How did the lake get its name?",a="The lake's name echoes that of the surrounding kingdom of Lordaeron, whose Capital City stands nearby. The records say little more about how it was named.",al={"lordamere name origin","why is it called lordamere"},it="name"},{q="What is Lordamere Lake?",a="Lordamere Lake is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the Eastern Kingdoms, rivaled only by Darrowmere Lake to the east. Spanning the borders between Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains, its waters historically connected the great human realms of Lordaeron, Dalaran, and Alterac. Today, it serves as a natural dividing line between Forsaken territory and the contested mountain highlands.",al={"what is lordamere lake","about lordamere lake","lordamere lake overview"},it="place",add="dc0bda98"},{q="Is Lordamere Lake dangerous?",a="Yes, its waters and shores harbor severe dangers. The Vile Fin murlocs have infested the Dawning Isles on the lake's eastern waters, attacking anyone who draws near. Farther out, Fenris Isle has fallen to the Scourge and dark magics, making travel across the water perilous for unwary travelers venturing between Silverpine and the Alterac foothills.",al={"is lordamere lake safe","dangers in lordamere lake","threats lordamere lake"},it="danger",add="a5470736"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Lordamere Lake is both a defensive moat protecting Tirisfal and a frontline where Scourge remnants on Fenris Isle must be purged.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see in Lordamere's quiet, foggy waters a reminder of the northern human kingdoms' ruined glory. They once traded freely across its shores."},kw={"alterac mountains","dawning isles","fenris isle","lake lordamere","lordamere lake","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:dawning-isles","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal","zone:alterac","subzone:dalaran","topic:lordaeron","quest:446"},src={"Lordamere Lake"}}
E["subzone:nethander-stead"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethander Stead",z="hillsbrad",s="Nethander Stead lies abandoned along the road east of Southshore, overrun by Mudsnout gnolls. Once a human farm, its fields now hold giant white Mudsnout Blossoms that draw Forsaken alchemists.",h="Nethander Stead lies abandoned along the road east of Southshore, overrun by Mudsnout gnolls.",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="At Nethander Stead, ruined fences and outbuildings stand within sight of Southshore's eastern borders. The farm once formed part of Hillsbrad's working fields, but it was abandoned as security weakened and wild packs moved in. Now the Mudsnout gnolls make their only home in the foothills here. They drive off travelers who come too close to their territory.",sp=0},{t="The Mudsnout Blossoms",b="Giant, pale mushrooms called Mudsnout Blossoms cover the farm's untended plots. The fungi carry potent natural toxins, drawing the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill. Its apothecaries seek samples from the gnolls' ground to distill caustic mixtures, sending covert Horde parties into Alliance territory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Nethander Stead?",a="Nethander Stead is an abandoned human farm along the road just east of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Mudsnout gnolls have overrun it.",al={"what is this farm","nethander stead info","where is nethander stead"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Nethander Stead right now?",a="The Mudsnout gnolls occupy the farmstead, the only place in the Hillsbrad Foothills where this pack makes camp.",al={"who lives here","who is at nethander stead","what mobs are here"},it="residents"},{q="What are the giant white mushrooms growing in the fields?",a="The giant white mushrooms are Mudsnout Blossoms, which grow in the farm's unworked soil. Their toxic properties make them valuable to Forsaken alchemists studying poisons.",al={"white mushrooms","mudsnout mushrooms","mudsnout blossoms"},it="item"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this ruined farm?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks Mudsnout Blossoms from the farm's fields. Their potent juices are an essential ingredient in the Elixir of Agony.",al={"why go here horde","forsaken interest","horde quest nethander"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to Nethander Stead?",a="Once a peaceful human farmstead supporting Hillsbrad and Southshore, Nethander Stead fell to ruin when the Mudsnout gnolls moved in. The original human farmers were displaced or slain, leaving the fields neglected and overgrown with strange fungi while the gnolls claimed the homestead as their own.",al={"nethander stead history","what happened at nethander stead","why is nethander stead abandoned"},it="history",add="a070b78c"},{q="Why is Nethander Stead abandoned?",a="The farm was overrun by the Mudsnout gnoll tribe. Unable to hold their land against the aggressive scavengers, the peasant caretakers were driven out or slaughtered, leaving the barns and homes to decay under gnoll occupation.",al={"why is nethander stead ruined","why did farmers leave nethander stead","who ruined nethander stead"},it="ruin",add="786285bb"},{q="Is Nethander Stead dangerous?",a="Yes. It is occupied by the Mudsnout gnolls, who fiercely defend their territory from outsiders. Anyone wandering off the road east of Southshore into these overgrown fields risks being swarmed by savage gnolls.",al={"is nethander stead safe","nethander stead danger","threats at nethander stead"},it="danger",add="b89e0e83"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the gnolls entrenched just down the eastern road show how fragile Southshore's perimeter remains.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, reaching this farmstead near Southshore means gathering Mudsnout Blossoms for the Royal Apothecary Society's lethal research."},kw={"blossoms","gnolls","hillsbrad","mudsnout","mushrooms","nethander","southshore","stead"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","quest:509","topic:gnoll"},src={"Nethander Stead"}}
E["subzone:purgation-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Purgation Isle",z="hillsbrad",s="Purgation Isle is a spiraling, rocky island lying off the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Crowned with a cemetery and a ruined scout tower, the desolate rock is cursed and swarming with the restless, condemned spirits of fallen humans and dwarves.",h="Purgation Isle is a spiraling, rocky island lying off the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Haunted Sanctuary",b="Rising abruptly from the sea south of Hillsbrad, Purgation Isle is a grim sight marked by winding paths that lead past tombstones to an abandoned watchtower. No living nation claims it today. Instead, the isle is plagued by condemned souls—former paladins, priests, mages, and judges who wander among the graves, unable to find peace in death.",sp=0},{t="Dark Associations",b="The lingering souls trapped upon the island have made it a site of sinister interest. Dark spellcasters, such as the ogre necromancer Kormok, are said to have delighted in drawing upon the island's anguished dead, summoning forth its spirits to do their bidding.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Purgation Isle located?",a="Purgation Isle is an isolated island off the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills, sitting out in the bay south of the mainland.",al={"purgation isle location","where is purgation isle","how to find purgation isle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What haunts the island?",a="The island is overrun by powerful condemned spirits, including cursed paladins, justiciars, clerics, acolytes, and writhing mages of human and dwarven descent.",al={"who is on purgation isle","mobs on purgation isle","purgation isle ghosts"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Kormok and why does he care about this island?",a="Kormok is a notorious ogre necromancer who mastered summoning forth the condemned spirits of Purgation Isle to perform his bidding using specialized dark artifacts.",al={"kormok connection","brazier of invocation ghosts"},it="threat"},{q="What is Purgation Isle?",a="Rising from the waters south of Hillsbrad Foothills, Purgation Isle is a spiraling, ominous crag crowned by an overgrown cemetery and the shattered remnants of an old scout tower. It has long fallen into ruin and desolation, cut off from the mainland and avoided by living sailors.",al={"what is purgation isle","purgation isle","tell me about purgation isle"},it="place",add="17b72096"},{q="Is Purgation Isle dangerous?",a="It is exceedingly dangerous. The island swarms with the restless, tormented specters of condemned paladins, clerics, mages, and judges who violently lash out at any living soul who steps ashore. Even darker forces seek to exploit them; the ogre necromancer Kormok is infamous for binding these tortured spirits to his dark will.",al={"how dangerous is purgation isle","is purgation isle safe","dangers of purgation isle"},it="danger",add="6d7a3de4"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The tragic sight of cursed paladins and justiciars wandering Purgation Isle serves as a somber reminder of what happens when holy defenders fall to dark curses and are denied eternal rest.",["race:Dwarf"]="Among the cursed specters haunting the cemetery are dwarven spirits, binding your kin to this lonely, windswept rock far from the mountains of Khaz Modan."},kw={"arados the damned","hillsbrad","judge thelgram","kormok","purgation isle","spirits"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","topic:dwarf"},src={"Purgation Isle"}}
E["subzone:ravenholdt-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Ravenholdt Manor",z="hillsbrad",s="Ravenholdt Manor watches over Hillsbrad from high in the mountains. Lord Jorach Ravenholdt leads its guild of thieves and assassins, where practitioners of stealth hone their craft beyond the authorities’ reach.",h="Ravenholdt Manor watches over Hillsbrad from high in the mountains.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary in the Shadows",b="Northwest of Durnholde Keep, a narrow pass and winding cave lead to Ravenholdt Manor. The estate stands isolated on the borderlands of the Alterac Mountains, and belongs to Lord Jorach Ravenholdt. He keeps a disciplined enclave of rogues, assassins, and intelligence operatives. A tranquil garden and outdoor training arena give them space to practice lockpicking, poison-crafting, and close-quarters combat under martial experts like Master Kang. Those with a talent for skullduggery are welcome, but watchful sentries greet clumsy outsiders and unwanted visitors with cold suspicion.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Feud in the Foothills",b="Before the First War, the land around Ravenholdt Manor belonged to the kingdom of Alterac, a past recalled by the manor’s weathered orange roof tiles. After Alterac fell, its displaced nobles in the Syndicate sought control of the region, bringing them into conflict with Ravenholdt. Jorach’s followers fight across Hillsbrad and Alterac to preserve their sovereign haven.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Travel to the plateau northwest of Durnholde Keep in Hillsbrad Foothills. Near the northern mountains, an obscure dirt path climbs through a hidden cave and emerges on the manor’s grounds.",al={"where is ravenholdt manor","how to get to ravenholdt","ravenholdt path"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who owns Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt owns the estate and leads the brotherhood of thieves and assassins known as Ravenholdt. Rogues throughout Azeroth hold him in deep respect.",al={"who leads ravenholdt","lord ravenholdt","manor owner"},it="residents"},{q="Why does Ravenholdt hate the Syndicate?",a="Both factions trace their roots to the shattered lands of Alterac. The Syndicate’s displaced nobles turn to banditry and lawlessness, while Ravenholdt works with strict discipline to thwart their ambitions.",al={"ravenholdt vs syndicate","syndicate feud","why fight syndicate"},it="conflict"},{q="Can anyone visit the manor?",a="Travelers can walk onto the grounds, where guards and assassins speak openly with hostility to outsiders. Rogues and trusted operatives receive a warm welcome and extensive training; others are warned to leave.",al={"non-rogue in ravenholdt","are outsiders allowed in ravenholdt"}},{q="What is Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Ravenholdt Manor is the secluded mountain headquarters of the Ravenholdt guild, an enigmatic league of thieves and assassins. Tucked away high in the hills above Hillsbrad and the Alterac border, the estate serves as a sanctuary and training ground where rogues hone their arts, craft subtle poisons, and coordinate covert operations far from the prying eyes of the Alliance and Horde.",al={"what is this place","ravenholdt manor lore","what is ravenholdt"},it="place",add="1390ac44"},{q="What is the history of Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Before the First War, this land was part of the ancient human kingdom of Alterac, reflected in the manor's traditional orange-tiled roof. Today the manor is the seat of Lord Jorach Ravenholdt, and it has stood as a bastion against the lawless Syndicate, quietly housing clandestine figures dedicated to the subtle arts.",al={"ravenholdt history","manor history","who built ravenholdt manor"},it="history",add="bf7fa55a"},{q="Is Ravenholdt Manor dangerous?",a="It depends entirely on who you are. The estate is fortified with watchful sentries, seasoned lookouts, and lethal assassins lurking in the shadows. While practitioners of stealth and shadowcraft are tolerated or welcomed to seek instruction, uninvited intruders or careless wanderers who meddle where they do not belong will find the shadows turning deadly very quickly.",al={"is ravenholdt safe","will ravenholdt attack me","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="258c293d"},{q="Why is it called Ravenholdt Manor?",a="The estate derives its name directly from its master and ancestral noble family, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt. The manor serves as the personal estate and sovereign seat of Lord Ravenholdt, lending both his noble moniker and crest to the brotherhood of rogues operating within its walls.",al={"ravenholdt manor name","why ravenholdt","where does the name ravenholdt come from"},it="name",add="0f3cae48"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can find rigorous trials, specialized training, and a deep network of underground contacts at Ravenholdt Manor, the foremost sanctuary for your profession.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can travel through the mountain pass to seek the rare schematic for the Gnomish Cloaking Device among the manor’s supplies."},kw={"alterac","assassin","hillsbrad","jorach ravenholdt","manor","ravenholdt","rogue guild","syndicate","thief"},rel={"npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt","topic:ravenholdt","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:alterac-kingdom","quest:2300"},src={"Ravenholdt Manor"}}
E["subzone:slaughter-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Slaughter Hollow",z="hillsbrad",s="In the snowy heights of the Alterac Mountains, Crushridge ogres hold Slaughter Hollow as a secluded camp. Travelers rarely come here except to hunt ogres or cross the frozen passes.",h="In the snowy heights of the Alterac Mountains, Crushridge ogres hold Slaughter Hollow as a secluded camp.",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres",b="Slaughter Hollow shelters the Crushridge ogres high in the peaks between Hillsbrad and Alterac. Makeshift fires, scattered bones, and crude shelters mark the mound. Other ogre dens in the highlands often see fights over territory or stolen supplies, but Slaughter Hollow stays quiet and beyond the reach of major military campaigns.",sp=0},{t="Captives and Travelers",b="Crushridge ogres sometimes keep prisoners taken along the mountain trails in their secluded mound. Travelers speak of Rizz Loosebolt, an unlucky gnome locked in a crude cage and trying to bargain with anyone who passes. Captives seldom fare well against the clan's appetite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Slaughter Hollow?",a="Crushridge ogres keep an encampment in Slaughter Hollow, high in the Alterac Mountains. Crude shelters and fires mark their mound.",al={"slaughter hollow lore","what is this place","slaughter hollow hillsbrad"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in Slaughter Hollow?",a="Crushridge ogres live in Slaughter Hollow. The clan also holds the nearby ruins of Alterac City and outposts in the surrounding lands.",al={"who is here","slaughter hollow mobs","who controls slaughter hollow"},it="residents"},{q="Are there any quests here?",a="No formal assignments send travelers directly to Slaughter Hollow. The den lies out of the way, among the mountain paths.",al={"slaughter hollow quests","any quests in slaughter hollow","why come here"},gp=true},{q="Who was the gnome caged here?",a="Rizz Loosebolt, a gnome, is held in a cage inside Slaughter Hollow and offers wares to anyone who finds him.",al={"rizz loosebolt","gnome in cage","slaughter hollow vendor"}},{q="Is Slaughter Hollow dangerous?",a="Yes, Slaughter Hollow is exceptionally hazardous. Deep in the snowy passes of the Alterac Mountains, this hollow serves as an ogre mound crawling with hostile Crushridge ogres. Wandering into their camp without preparation will quickly draw the wrath of multiple hulking brutes.",al={"is slaughter hollow safe","slaughter hollow danger","how dangerous is slaughter hollow"},it="danger",add="446b3423"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Rizz Loosebolt's capture by the Crushridge is a warning to tinkerers and scouts who cross the Alterac passes unprepared."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","hillsbrad","ogre mound","rizz loosebolt","slaughter hollow"},rel={"zone:alterac","zone:hillsbrad","topic:gnome","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Slaughter Hollow"}}
E["subzone:southpoint-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Southpoint Tower",z="hillsbrad",s="Forsaken scouts watch Alliance movements from Southpoint Tower, near Hillsbrad's western edge. The ruined Lordaeron post overlooks the road into Silverpine Forest.",h="Forsaken scouts watch Alliance movements from Southpoint Tower, near Hillsbrad's western edge.",sec={{t="A Ruined Sentinel",b="Southpoint Tower overlooks the highway between Silverpine Forest and Hillsbrad Foothills. The Kingdom of Lordaeron built it to guard traffic between the eastern farmlands and the western woods. After the Third War and the Scourge's destruction of the kingdom, the stonework fell into ruin. Now the tower stands roofless and crumbling, a remnant of human rule in fractured lands.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Hills",b="Forsaken agents watch Alliance patrols from the ruined tower. Deathstalker Lesh is among those stationed there, keeping an eye on nearby human settlements in Hillsbrad Fields and travelers on the main road. The vantage remains valuable despite the collapsed walls. So close to hostile territory, this lonely post often becomes a flashpoint for skirmishes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Southpoint Tower located?",a="Southpoint Tower stands at the western edge of Hillsbrad Foothills, just south of the road into Silverpine Forest and west of Hillsbrad Fields.",al={"southpoint tower location","where is southpoint tower","find southpoint tower"},gp=true},{q="Who controls Southpoint Tower right now?",a="The Forsaken control Southpoint Tower. Deathstalker Lesh watches the road and nearby Alliance forces from within its ruined walls.",al={"who is at southpoint tower","who owns southpoint tower","southpoint tower faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the tower in ruins?",a="The Scourge ravaged the region during Lordaeron's fall, battering and forcing the abandonment of the tower. No one has repaired it, and only broken stone walls remain.",al={"why is southpoint tower broken","who destroyed southpoint tower"},it="ruin"},{q="Why do Alliance players attack this outpost?",a="Alliance travelers attack because a Forsaken scout watches human territory from the isolated post near the border. Its position makes it a tempting target for those traveling between Southshore and the western roads.",al={"why kill deathstalker lesh","alliance attacking southpoint tower"},gp=true},{q="What is Southpoint Tower?",a="Southpoint Tower is a crumbling human watchtower situated along the western edge of the Hillsbrad Foothills, overlooking the road leading into Silverpine Forest. Once a standing fortification for human defenders, it now lies largely broken and exposed, serving as a tactical forward surveillance post.",al={"what is southpoint tower","southpoint tower purpose","about southpoint tower"},it="place",add="dd4aae73"},{q="Who lives in or runs Southpoint Tower?",a="The tower is not a permanent settlement, but it currently hosts Deathstalker Lesh, an operative of the Forsaken. Hidden among the shattered stonework, she uses the elevation to spy on Alliance movements between Southshore and the western borders.",al={"who is at southpoint tower","southpoint tower residents","who lives at southpoint tower"},it="residents",add="f07dd792"},{q="Is Southpoint Tower dangerous?",a="It can be treacherous depending on your allegiance. Deathstalker Lesh will readily strike down Alliance travelers venturing along the road to Silverpine, while Alliance scouts and adventurers frequently target her isolated post to disrupt Forsaken intelligence.",al={"is southpoint tower dangerous","how dangerous is southpoint tower","southpoint tower threats"},it="danger",add="0d7406b8"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can use this perch near the Silverpine border to watch human troop movements out of Hillsbrad.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout, you can target the ruined tower, where an enemy spy watches the road to Silverpine and the human settlements of Hillsbrad."},kw={"deathstalker lesh","hillsbrad fields","hillsbrad foothills","scout tower","silverpine forest","southpoint tower"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-lesh","zone:hillsbrad","zone:silverpine","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","topic:forsaken","subzone:southshore"},src={"Southpoint Tower"}}
E["subzone:southshore"] = {t="subzone",n="Southshore",z="hillsbrad",s="Southshore is a coastal human port in the Hillsbrad Foothills and one of the Alliance's few surviving strongholds in fallen Lordaeron. Once a sleepy fishing village, it now stands as an embattled bastion facing constant hostility from the Forsaken garrison at Tarren Mill, rogue Syndicate bandits, and shoreline monsters.",h="Southshore is a coastal human port in the Hillsbrad Foothills and one of the Alliance's few surviving...",sec={{t="A Beacon in Lordaeron",b="Southshore first rose to prominence during the First War when refugee boats carrying survivors from the fallen kingdom of Stormwind landed upon its beaches. Though contested and overrun during the Second War, it was rebuilt and later endured the horrors of the Third War. Today, while the rest of Lordaeron lies in ruins or under the rule of the Forsaken, Southshore remains fiercely loyal to the Grand Alliance. It offers shelter to displaced human survivors, veteran paladins of the Silver Hand, and scholars of the Kirin Tor.",sp=0},{t="Besieged on All Fronts",b="Despite its scenic docks, where the ship between Menethil Harbor and Auberdine calls, and its famous turtle bisque, life in Southshore is perilous. Led by Magistrate Henry Maleb and Marshal Redpath, the town struggles against relentless pressure. To the north, the Forsaken of Tarren Mill wage a bitter border conflict for dominance over Hillsbrad. Inland, the aristocratic outlaws of the Syndicate raid supply lines and assassinate local leaders, while ogres, murlocs, and naga constantly harass the town's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Southshore still aligned with the Alliance when Lordaeron fell?",a="Southshore was spared total destruction during the Scourge's invasion. Its surviving human populace reaffirmed their historic oaths to the Grand Alliance, receiving military and logistical backing from Stormwind to maintain a foothold in the north.",al={"why is southshore alliance","who controls southshore","southshore alliance lordaeron"},it="side"},{q="Why is there such intense fighting between Southshore and Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is held by the Forsaken, while Southshore is the primary Alliance bastion in the region. Both factions claim rightful dominion over the Hillsbrad Foothills, resulting in near-constant border skirmishes, raids, and sabotage.",al={"southshore tarren mill war","why do southshore and tarren mill fight","hillsbrad conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Who leads the town of Southshore?",a="Civil governance is handled by Magistrate Henry Maleb, who took over after the previous magistrate was assassinated by the Syndicate. Military defense and town security are directed by Marshal Redpath.",al={"southshore leader","who runs southshore","magistrate maleb"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats does Southshore face other than the Forsaken?",a="Beyond the Forsaken, Southshore must fend off coastal murlocs and naga, Crushridge ogres descending from the Alterac Mountains, and the criminal Syndicate based out of Durnholde Keep.",al={"southshore enemies","threats to southshore"},it="threat"},{q="What is Southshore?",a="Southshore is a bustling port town on the southern coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. It serves as one of the last remaining bastions of human civilization and Alliance authority in Lordaeron following the Scourge's destruction of Capital City. Despite being surrounded by hostile factions, it maintains a functioning harbor, civic leadership, and a steadfast garrison.",al={"what is southshore","southshore town","about southshore"},it="place",add="f6e4321c"},{q="What happened at Southshore historically?",a="Originally a simple fishing village, Southshore welcomed the refugees who fled Stormwind after the First War. In the Second War, it became a strategic seaport coveted for offshore oil, falling to the Horde before being retaken and rebuilt after the war.",al={"southshore history","southshore lore","history of southshore"},it="history",add="b35b5b82"},{q="Is Southshore dangerous?",a="For the Alliance, Southshore offers a well-guarded sanctuary, but the surrounding countryside is fraught with danger. Skirmishes with the Forsaken from Tarren Mill frequently spill across the foothills, while coastal murlocs and naga threaten the harbor. Additionally, Syndicate rogues, Crushridge ogres, and lingering undead lurk just outside the town's perimeter.",al={"how dangerous is southshore","is southshore safe","threats in southshore"},it="danger",add="856a6b32"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Southshore serves as your primary haven, quest hub, and military redoubt in northern Lordaeron, offering essential support against both the Forsaken and the Syndicate.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde—especially the Forsaken at nearby Tarren Mill—Southshore represents an obstinate Alliance enclave trespassing on land reclaimed by the dead."},kw={"hillsbrad","jessen","lordaeron","maleb","redpath","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:tarren-mill","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","npc:chef-jessen","quest:555","subzone:durnholde-keep","topic:syndicate","topic:forsaken"},src={"Southshore"}}
E["subzone:southshore-town-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Southshore Town Hall",z="hillsbrad",s="At Southshore Town Hall, Magistrate Henry Maleb directs the town’s affairs and defenses. It remains one of Lordaeron’s last centers of civil authority, while the Alliance struggles to hold ground in the plagued north.",h="At Southshore Town Hall, Magistrate Henry Maleb directs the town’s affairs and defenses.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Civil Rule",b="Southshore Town Hall keeps human rule alive amid Lordaeron’s ruin. Magistrate Henry Maleb governs from his office, working with officials such as Kundric Zanden to secure supplies and preserve order. Undead press from nearby lands, Syndicate rogues threaten the region, and Hillsbrad’s border sees fierce skirmishes. From the hall, town leaders direct Southshore’s survival against these threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who leads the town from the Southshore Town Hall?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb leads Southshore’s civil government from the town hall, directing the settlement’s administration and defense.",al={"who is in charge here","southshore mayor","who runs southshore"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the strategic importance of Southshore Town Hall?",a="Southshore Town Hall is one of the last seats of Lordaeron’s civil leadership in the north. Alliance members look to it for direction, bounties, and coordination against the Forsaken and Syndicate bandits.",al={"why does the town hall matter","southshore importance"},it="purpose"},{q="Who else works inside the town hall?",a="Kundric Zanden and other civil servants work alongside Magistrate Henry Maleb inside the town hall, helping manage local affairs and town operations.",al={"who is inside southshore town hall","kundric zanden","town hall npcs"},it="residents"},{q="How does the town hall maintain ties with the wider Alliance?",a="Southshore was part of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, and its leaders now rely heavily on the Alliance for reinforcements and supplies. That support helps defend the isolated coastal town against nearby hostile forces.",al={"is southshore alliance","ties to stormwind"},it="ties"},{q="What is Southshore Town Hall?",a="This sturdy stone building stands as the administrative heart of Southshore and a vital center of governance for the surviving remnants of Lordaeron. Within its walls, local civic leaders coordinate the settlement's defense, maintain civil order, and manage the daily needs of a refuge surrounded by hostile forces.",al={"southshore town hall","what is southshore town hall","what building is this southshore"},it="place",add="ccaa2d22"},{q="What happened at Southshore Town Hall?",a="Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge during the Third War, Southshore became one of the last major refuges for the kingdom's survivors. The town hall was established as the primary seat of civic authority, where Magistrate Henry Maleb and his councilors took up the monumental task of preserving lawful human society along the southern coast.",al={"history of southshore town hall","what happened here town hall"},it="history",add="eda35516"},{q="Is Southshore Town Hall dangerous?",a="For champions of the Alliance, the town hall is a safe and fortified haven guarded by vigilant town guards. For members of the Horde, however, entering the building is perilous; the town officials and nearby sentries will immediately attack any intruders who breach the town's perimeter.",al={"is southshore town hall safe","is it dangerous in southshore town hall"},it="danger",add="49b6de22"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion arriving in the north, you can look to Southshore Town Hall for regional authority and help against nearby threats.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you see Southshore Town Hall as a reminder of Lordaeron’s lost glory, where a working magistrate still upholds the banners of a shattered kingdom."},kw={"henry maleb","hillsbrad","kundric zanden","lordaeron","magistrate","southshore","town hall"},rel={"subzone:southshore","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","zone:hillsbrad","topic:lordaeron","topic:forsaken","topic:third-war","subzone:fenris-isle"},src={"Southshore Town Hall"}}
E["subzone:strahnbrad"] = {t="subzone",n="Strahnbrad",z="hillsbrad",s="Strahnbrad is a ruined human settlement nestled in the northeastern heights of the Alterac Mountains, near the border of the Western Plaguelands. Once famous as the site of Prince Arthas Menethil's early defense against Blackrock orc raiders, the town has since fallen into decay and serves as a fortified stronghold for the criminal Syndicate.",h="Strahnbrad is a ruined human settlement nestled in the northeastern heights of the Alterac Mountains, near...",sec={{t="A Town of Tragedy",b="Originally a holding of the Kingdom of Alterac before being absorbed into Lordaeron following the Second War, Strahnbrad's misfortune began on the eve of the Third War. Blackrock clan orcs raided the settlement to take human sacrifices for the Burning Legion, leading Prince Arthas Menethil and the Knights of the Silver Hand to ride to its defense. Though Arthas drove the raiders away and slew their slave master, the town was heavily bloodied. When Lordaeron crumbled beneath the Scourge shortly thereafter, Strahnbrad was abandoned to the elements.",sp=0},{t="The Syndicate's Grip",b="Today, Strahnbrad has become a crucial operations hub for the Syndicate, the organization of displaced Alteraci nobility and outlaws plotting to reclaim their fallen realm. Patrolled by human rogues and brigands, its abandoned town hall and blacksmith now serve as hideouts and staging grounds. The Syndicate uses the ruined town to house supplies and captive labor, including unfortunate prisoners like the orc Gol'dir, whom Horde scouts from Tarren Mill actively seek to liberate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Strahnbrad significant in history?",a="Strahnbrad was the site of the opening clash of the Third War for Prince Arthas Menethil. Sent by Uther the Lightbringer to protect the settlement from rampaging Blackrock orcs, Arthas made his first celebrated stand here, rescuing townsfolk and cutting down the orc raiders.",al={"why does strahnbrad matter","arthas strahnbrad","strahnbrad history"},it="history"},{q="Who controls Strahnbrad now?",a="The Syndicate holds Strahnbrad. These human brigands, loyal to the fallen noble bloodlines of Alterac, have fortified the ruined town hall and blacksmith to use as a primary staging ground for their ambitions in the mountains.",al={"who owns strahnbrad","strahnbrad mobs","who lives in strahnbrad"},it="residents"},{q="Which kingdom did Strahnbrad belong to originally?",a="Strahnbrad was originally part of the Kingdom of Alterac before the First War. After Alterac betrayed the Alliance during the Second War, the town was integrated under the domain of the Kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"is strahnbrad alterac or lordaeron","strahnbrad kingdom"},it="history"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this town?",a="The Syndicate captured an orc named Gol'dir and forced him into brutal slave labor within Strahnbrad's ruins. Horde operatives from Tarren Mill, directed by Krusk, send adventurers here to breach the Syndicate's defenses and break Gol'dir out.",al={"horde quests in strahnbrad","krusk strahnbrad","gol'dir strahnbrad"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Strahnbrad?",a="Strahnbrad is a ruined settlement nestled in the northeastern foothills of the Alterac Mountains, near the pass into the Western Plaguelands. Originally a human town that passed from the Kingdom of Alterac to Lordaeron, it now stands derelict, its streets deserted of innocent life and occupied by dangerous outlaws.",al={"what is this place","strahnbrad overview","tell me about strahnbrad"},it="place",add="8ef7b8bc"},{q="Why is Strahnbrad ruined and abandoned?",a="Strahnbrad suffered brutal devastation just prior to the Third War when renegade Blackrock orcs raided the settlement to capture sacrifices for the Burning Legion. Though Prince Arthas Menethil arrived to drive the raiders off, many townsfolk perished. Following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge, the surviving populace scattered or died, leaving the abandoned structures to be seized by bandits.",al={"why is strahnbrad destroyed","who destroyed strahnbrad","why is strahnbrad a ghost town"},it="ruin",add="e385b772"},{q="Is Strahnbrad dangerous to visit?",a="Yes, Strahnbrad is very dangerous. The abandoned town serves as an active stronghold for the Syndicate, a ruthless criminal network of former Alterac nobility and brigands. They attack trespassers on sight and have even been known to take captives for forced labor, making the area hazardous for any lone traveler passing through the mountains.",al={"is strahnbrad safe","strahnbrad hostile","strahnbrad dangers"},it="danger",add="37fa5a7f"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Walking the cobblestones of Strahnbrad recalls the early, untainted days of Prince Arthas Menethil and Uther the Lightbringer, serving as a bitter reminder of how far Lordaeron's heroes have fallen.",["faction:Horde"]="The Syndicate's enslavement of the orc Gol'dir makes Strahnbrad an urgent target for Horde champions seeking to strike at human brigands and rescue their kin."},kw={"alterac","arthas","blackrock","gol'dir","krusk","lordaeron","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:lordaeron","npc:krusk","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:westernplaguelands"},src={"Strahnbrad"}}
E["subzone:tarren-mill"] = {t="subzone",n="Tarren Mill",z="hillsbrad",s="Tarren Mill holds the Horde's line in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills, beneath the Alterac Mountains. Once a peaceful human farming village, it is now a Forsaken outpost locked in conflict with Southshore to the south.",h="Tarren Mill holds the Horde's line in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills, beneath the Alterac Mountains.",sec={{t="From Grain to Grave",b="Tarren Mill's fields and mill have fallen silent since the Third War. Before then, it was a thriving farming town loyal to Lordaeron. During the Second War, Alliance forces near the town freed captured high elven archers from orc encampments, securing Quel'Thalas's full commitment to the Alliance of Lordaeron. The town's living inhabitants are gone, replaced by the Forsaken. Its buildings are weathered, its fields barren, and its mill quiet. The Forsaken fortify Tarren Mill against mountain beasts, Syndicate outlaws, and Alliance skirmishers.",sp=0},{t="Front Line of Hillsbrad",b="Tarren Mill is the Horde's forward base in Hillsbrad. Southshore, the Alliance port, lies directly across from it, and the road between the towns has become a warzone. From Tarren Mill, Horde travelers push back against the human farmers and soldiers occupying Hillsbrad, coordinate strikes against dwarven excavators at Dun Garok, and secure the dangerous roads that climb into the snowy crags of the Alterac Mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Tarren Mill right now?",a="The Forsaken control Tarren Mill, their main Horde outpost in the Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who owns tarren mill","is tarren mill horde or alliance","tarren mill faction"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are Tarren Mill and Southshore fighting?",a="Tarren Mill marks the Forsaken and Horde's southern reach in Lordaeron, while Southshore is the Alliance's last major stronghold in the region. Their closeness drives a struggle for Hillsbrad's fertile land and strategic roads.",al={"southshore vs tarren mill","why fight southshore","hillsbrad war"},it="conflict"},{q="What was Tarren Mill like before the plague?",a="Before the plague, Tarren Mill was a peaceful human farming and milling settlement in the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Second War, Alliance soldiers freed captive high elven archers near the town, securing Quel'Thalas's military pact with the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"tarren mill history","who lived here before","tarren mill lore"},it="origin"},{q="What threats exist around Tarren Mill besides the Alliance?",a="Beyond Southshore's forces, Tarren Mill faces Syndicate bandits, highland yetis and ogres from the Alterac peaks, and fierce mountain wildlife in the foothills.",al={"tarren mill enemies","local dangers hillsbrad"},it="threat"},{q="What is Tarren Mill?",a="Tarren Mill is a northern outpost and settlement in the Hillsbrad Foothills, situated just below the Alterac Mountains. Once a modest farming community of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, it now serves as the primary Forsaken bastion and Horde stronghold in the region, standing as a direct counterweight to the Alliance at Southshore.",al={"tarren mill overview","what is this town","about tarren mill"},it="place",add="51e1ff94"},{q="What happened at Tarren Mill in the past?",a="During the Second War, Horde forces ambushed Silvermoon elven archers near the town, prompting King Terenas to order Alliance troops here to rescue the captives and solidify the elves' alliance with Lordaeron. After the Third War ravaged the kingdom, its human population was lost, and the Forsaken claimed the weathered settlement as their own staging ground.",al={"tarren mill history","past of tarren mill","second war tarren mill"},it="history",add="7a0e9758"},{q="Why is Tarren Mill in such disrepair?",a="The town suffered through the devastation of the Third War, subsequent Scourge attacks, and the loss of its original human population. The Forsaken who occupy it now view Tarren Mill primarily as a strategic military staging ground rather than a comfortable home, leaving its old buildings, church, and withered orchards in a state of neglected decay.",al={"why is tarren mill ruined","why does tarren mill look broken","tarren mill run down"},it="ruin",add="3dc25634"},{q="Is Tarren Mill dangerous?",a="Tarren Mill is exceptionally dangerous. Situated on the volatile front lines of Hillsbrad, it faces relentless skirmishes and counterattacks from Alliance soldiers and champions from Southshore. Beyond the Alliance, Syndicate outlaws lurk in nearby ruins, mountain yetis stalk the northern slopes, and savage Crushridge ogres constantly threaten the perimeter.",al={"is it safe in tarren mill","tarren mill danger","threat level tarren mill"},it="danger",add="4eb188ad"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Tarren Mill is your only major refuge in the Hillsbrad Foothills, with a bat handler, supplies, and vital military support against Alliance forces from Southshore.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, taking Tarren Mill extends Queen Sylvanas's southern borders and turns a once-proud Lordaeron farming town into a stronghold against the living."},kw={"alterac","forsaken","hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills","lordaeron","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","subzone:southshore","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","subzone:dun-garok"},src={"Tarren Mill"}}
E["zone:hillsbrad"] = {t="zone",n="Hillsbrad Foothills",z="hillsbrad",s="Hillsbrad Foothills remains green while war tears through the last pastoral reaches of Lordaeron. Southshore's humans and the Forsaken at Tarren Mill clash across the fields, making the region a violent crossroads for Alliance and Horde armies.",h="Hillsbrad Foothills remains green while war tears through the last pastoral reaches of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Garden Beside the Ruins",b="Hillsbrad remains green while blight consumes much of northern Lordaeron. Rolling pastures, pine groves, and working farms still recall the kingdom before the Third War. Armed patrols, rogue mercenaries, and scavenger beasts cross its fields and roads. Lordaeron's breadbasket has become one of its most contested borderlands.",sp=0},{t="The War of Southshore and Tarren Mill",b="Southshore stands on the southern coast, held by human refugees and soldiers loyal to the Alliance. North of it, Tarren Mill was once a quiet human farming hamlet, until the Scourge destroyed it and the Forsaken fortified it as their southernmost garrison. The open ground between the settlements has become a relentless killing ground, where Alliance and Horde champions skirmish for control of Hillsbrad.",sp=0},{t="Old Scars and Hidden Threats",b="Hillsbrad's violence reaches back to the Second War, when its coast and hills saw the first massive clashes between the Grand Alliance and the Old Horde. Durnholde Keep later served as the internment camp where Thrall was raised before leading the orcish rebellion. Now the keep lies in ruins, held by the Syndicate, displaced human nobles turned bandits. Coastal murlocs, hostile gnolls, and the shadowed dead on Purgation Isle leave no corner of the hills secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why isn't Hillsbrad blighted like the rest of Lordaeron?",a="The Scourge marched mainly through the central corridors toward the capital and northern kingdoms, leaving Hillsbrad largely beyond the reach of the plague cauldrons that ruined the north. Its soil remains fertile and its vegetation healthy, making it the most pristine remnant of old Lordaeron.",al={"why is hillsbrad green","did hillsbrad get plagued","why no plague in hillsbrad"},it="ruin"},{q="Who controls Hillsbrad right now?",a="Neither faction controls all of Hillsbrad. The Alliance holds Southshore and nearby farms such as the Hillsbrad Fields, while the Forsaken hold Tarren Mill to the north. Dwarven forces occupy Dun Garok in the east, and the criminal Syndicate holds the ruins of Durnholde Keep.",al={"who owns hillsbrad","hillsbrad faction control","is hillsbrad alliance or horde"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Durnholde Keep?",a="Durnholde once served as the headquarters of the Alliance's internment camp system after the Second War. Aedelas Blackmoore governed it and raised Thrall there as a gladiator slave. Thrall escaped, rallied the orcs, and laid waste to the keep; after Lordaeron fell, the Syndicate occupied its ruins.",al={"durnholde lore","what happened at durnholde","who runs durnholde"},it="place",nx={15,16}},{q="Why do the Forsaken and humans fight so fiercely here?",a="Tarren Mill marks the southern frontier of Sylvanas Windrunner's domain, while Southshore is the Alliance's main staging ground and port into Lordaeron. The Forsaken see Southshore as a threat to their southern flank, and the humans see the undead as usurpers who must be driven from their homeland.",al={"why the southshore war","southshore vs tarren mill lore","hillsbrad conflict reason"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Purgation Isle?",a="Purgation Isle is a rugged, isolated island off Hillsbrad's southern coast. Powerful undead ghouls, skeletons, and vengeful spirits infest it, making it a dangerous offshore refuge for dark magic and restless dead.",al={"purgation isle lore","island off southshore","why undead on purgation isle"},it="place"},{q="Who are the bandits occupying the camps and towers?",a="The bandits belong to the Syndicate, an organized network of former nobles and foot soldiers from the fallen human kingdom of Alterac. Cast out after their kingdom's betrayal during the Second War, they now seek to reclaim their lands through blackmail, theft, and slaughter.",al={"hillsbrad bandits","who is the syndicate","syndicate in hillsbrad"},it="threat"},{q="What is Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Hillsbrad Foothills is a rolling, temperate coastal territory along the southern edge of fallen Lordaeron, bounded by Silverpine Forest to the west, the snow-draped Alterac Mountains to the north, and Thoradin's Wall leading into the Arathi Highlands to the east. Unlike the blighted lands to the north, Hillsbrad remains lush and pastoral, with green meadows, productive farms, and seaside cliffs. Beneath this idyllic veneer, it serves as a violent borderland contested between the surviving humans of the Alliance and the encroaching Forsaken.",al={"what is hillsbrad","hillsbrad foothills overview","tell me about hillsbrad"},it="place",add="5a0996a2"},{q="What happened at Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Hillsbrad has long been one of the bloodiest battlegrounds in Lordaeron. During the Second War, it saw the very first clashes between the Alliance and the Old Horde, including fierce skirmishes with forest trolls and coastal raids that left towns like Hillsbrad and Southshore briefly in ruins. Later, orc internment camps were centered here at Durnholde Keep until Thrall's rebellion leveled the fortress. When the Third War broke out, Thrall stole ships from Southshore to reach Kalimdor, and the Scourge later swept the north, eventually prompting the Forsaken to seize Tarren Mill.",al={"hillsbrad history","battle of hillsbrad history","past of hillsbrad"},it="history",add="88d7d468"},{q="Is Hillsbrad Foothills dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. Beyond native predators like mountain lions, snapping turtles, and prowling spiders, Hillsbrad is an active war zone. Southshore's human guards and Tarren Mill's undead Deathstalkers hunt opposing travelers along the roads. In addition, cutthroats of the Syndicate operate out of scattered towers and the ruins of Durnholde, hostile Daggerspine naga and Torn Fin murlocs infest the coast, Mudsnout gnolls roam the woods, and dwarf riflemen occupy Dun Garok in force.",al={"how dangerous is hillsbrad","is hillsbrad safe","dangers of hillsbrad"},it="danger",add="10678baf"},{q="What is Tarren Mill and why is the Horde here?",a="Tarren Mill is a dilapidated settlement in the northern foothills that serves as the Forsaken's southernmost stronghold in Lordaeron. Once a peaceful human farming village, it fell during the Scourge invasion and was later occupied by Sylvanas Windrunner's forces. From here, the Horde projects power southward, harboring Apothecaries working on virulent concoctions and stationing troops to mount repeated assaults against Southshore and the nearby human farmlands.",al={"what is tarren mill","why horde in tarren mill","tarren mill horde base"},it="place",add="dea356d1",nx={11}},{q="Was Tarren Mill a human town before?",a="Yes. Prior to the Third War, Tarren Mill was a thriving town under the Kingdom of Lordaeron. In the Second War, King Terenas sent troops here to liberate captured high elven archers held nearby by the Horde, an act that helped cement Quel'Thalas's alliance with humanity. Even after the kingdom fell, a contingent of humans briefly clung to the town before the Scourge and subsequent Forsaken occupation claimed it.",al={"did humans live in tarren mill","was tarren mill human","tarren mill past"},it="history",add="b39e7470"},{q="Who's in charge in Tarren Mill?",a="High Executor Darthalia commands the Forsaken military garrison at Tarren Mill. She directs the war effort throughout the foothills, ordering surgical strikes against human farmers, the town of Southshore, and rival factions across the region. Alongside her, Royal Apothecary Society researchers like Apothecary Lydon oversee local operations and chemical experiments.",al={"who runs tarren mill","tarren mill leader","tarren mill commander"},it="in_charge",add="c8808bc1"},{q="What is the Battle of Hillsbrad actually about?",a="The ongoing battle is a territorial and existential clash for southern Lordaeron. The humans of Southshore and Hillsbrad Fields fight to defend the last remnants of their uncorrupted homeland and retain a vital coastal foothold. Conversely, the Forsaken seek to expand the borders of their fledgling kingdom outward from the Undercity, systematically destroying human agricultural supply lines and driving out the Alliance so they cannot mount a counter-invasion.",al={"why are they fighting in hillsbrad","battle of hillsbrad purpose","hillsbrad war reason"},it="purpose",add="9809687d"},{q="What is Southshore?",a="Southshore is a bustling Alliance port town positioned along the southern coastline. Originally a humble fishing hamlet, it served as the landing point for refugees from Stormwind during the First War before expanding into a heavily defended military harbor in the Second War. Today, led by Magistrate Henry Maleb and Marshal Redpath, it acts as the primary redoubt for human survivors, sailors, and Alliance adventurers in northern Lordaeron.",al={"what is southshore","southshore overview","alliance southshore"},it="place",add="3a05e673"},{q="Was Durnholde Keep where orcs were kept prisoner?",a="Yes. Following the Alliance's victory in the Second War, Durnholde Keep served as the headquarters for the entire southern internment camp network, commanded by Lieutenant General Aedelas Blackmoore. Captured orcs were imprisoned and pacified here by Alliance guards. Most notably, Blackmoore raised the orphaned infant Thrall within its arena walls, who eventually broke free, mobilized his brethren, and smashed the keep to rubble with the aid of the earth spirits.",al={"was durnholde an internment camp","orcs imprisoned at durnholde","durnholde internment"},it="history",add="54a7e72a"},{q="Who holds Durnholde now?",a="The shattered stone courtyards and burnt-out lodges of Durnholde are now occupied by the Syndicate. These exiled nobles, disgraced retainers, and bandits from the fallen kingdom of Alterac have fortified the ruins, using them as a staging ground to raid supply lines, caravans, and travelers across eastern Hillsbrad.",al={"who is at durnholde keep","durnholde bandits","who controls durnholde"},it="residents",add="ee5f5dea"},{q="What is Dun Garok and why are dwarves here?",a="Dun Garok is a sturdy dwarven fortress tucked into the rocky southeastern bluffs of Hillsbrad, garrisoned by the Stormpike clan and Ironforge Mountaineers under Captain Ironhill. These stalwart troops arrived to reinforce Alliance positions, secure nearby mining resources like the Azurelode Mine, and prevent Forsaken forces from pushing eastward through the mountains toward Thoradin's Wall.",al={"what is dun garok","why are there dwarves in hillsbrad","dun garok dwarves"},it="threat",add="7f2bc51a"},{q="What are these murlocs and naga-looking things on the coast?",a="The shoreline is overrun by the Torn Fin tribe of murlocs and serpent-like naga known as the Daggerspine. The Torn Fin stalk the shallows, attacking fishermen and competing with miners along the coast. Meanwhile, the Daggerspine naga have crept ashore to establish coastal enclaves, viciously striking at anyone traveling near the waves or scavenging the shoreline.",al={"hillsbrad coast murlocs","naga in hillsbrad","hillsbrad coastal monsters"},it="threat",add="b8990472"},{q="How did I end up in Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="Your road here depends on your allegiance. If you march with the Horde, you likely journeyed south from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, following the long winding road east along Lordaeron's southern border until you reached Tarren Mill. If you fight for the Alliance, you traveled far from the dwarven halls of Ironforge, marching north across Loch Modan and the sodden marshes of the Wetlands, traversing the Arathi Highlands, and passing through the ancient breach of Thoradin's Wall to reach the port of Southshore. Alternatively, daring sailors and swimmers sometimes brave the sea passage directly north from Menethil Harbor.",al={"how did i get to hillsbrad","how did i get here","why am i in hillsbrad foothills","how do i reach hillsbrad"},it="arrival",add="235a8e20"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Hillsbrad Foothills?",a="You stand on one of the most volatile front lines in Azeroth. For the Alliance, your duty centers on Southshore and Hillsbrad Fields: defending human farmers from undead aggression, hunting the rogue bandits of the Syndicate, and curbing the savage creatures infesting the shores. For the Horde, High Executor Darthalia and the Royal Apothecary Society at Tarren Mill demand the systematic dismantling of human resistance, harvesting ingredients for a new plague, and pushing back against the Stormpike dwarves and Alliance soldiers. Across the fields between the two towns, survival demands eternal vigilance against enemy champions.",al={"what am i doing here","what should i do in hillsbrad","what is my purpose in hillsbrad","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="f17f6b77"}},ang={["race:Human"]="Southshore is one of your people's last refuges in Lordaeron. These pastures recall the great kingdom lost to betrayal and undeath.",["race:Undead"]="Tarren Mill anchors the southern frontier of the Forsaken realm. Apothecary Lydon works there to develop the New Plague and secure your people's future.",["race:Orc"]="Durnholde Keep's ruined ramparts mark where Warchief Thrall broke his chains and rekindled the spirit of the Horde.",["race:Dwarf"]="The soldiers of Dun Garok show Ironforge's resolve to defend its human allies and contain the undead threat north of the Wetlands.",["class:Rogue"]="Ravenholdt Manor lies hidden in the mountains above the foothills. It is the secret gathering place and training ground of Azeroth's most elite guild of thieves and assassins."},kw={"azurelode","dun garok","durnholde","hillsbrad","hillsbrad fields","purgation isle","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill"},rel={"subzone:southshore","subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:durnholde-keep","subzone:hillsbrad-fields","subzone:dun-garok","subzone:purgation-isle","zone:alterac","zone:arathi"},m={levels="20-30"},src={"Hillsbrad Foothills (Classic)","Hillsbrad Foothills"}}
